window.NovaManualData = {"built":"2026-10-10T12:27:20.744Z","recentDays":7,"suite":null,"apps":[{"id":"agent","name":"Nova Agent","colour":"#FF5FA8","glyph":"✦","where":"On the studio computer, and online for phones","links":[["Open Nova Agent","http://localhost:4545/"]],"repo":"na","shared":"","tagline":"Your planner, your Agent and the studio's hands in Acuity, on the studio computer.","intro":"<p>Talk to it, give it a goal, and it plans your days to the second. It also works Acuity&#39;s admin pages for Novacane Studios.</p>\n<p>Nova Agent is the studio&#39;s one app. Everything that used to be a separate Nova app is a panel of it: <strong>Portal</strong> (the staff app: enquiries, website chats, bookings, alerts, Ask NovaBot, sign-in, your planet and the team; Portal is part of it now), <strong>Calendar</strong>, <strong>Notes</strong>, <strong>Index</strong>, <strong>Observatory</strong>, <strong>Lossless audio</strong> and <strong>Admin</strong>. The panels only ever open inside Nova Agent. Nova Agent has one address in each place, <code>/agent/</code>:</p>\n<ul><li>online, for everyone:</li><li>on the studio PC: <code>http://localhost:4545/agent/</code></li></ul>\n<p><code>/agent/</code> (<code>/agent/calendar</code>, <code>/agent/portal</code>, <code>/agent/notes</code>, <code>/agent/index</code>...) opens Nova Agent with that panel. Nova Bot (the website chat) keeps the main address.</p>\n<p>Agent, Missions, Quests, Calendar and the Visualizer run on the studio PC. The online Nova Agent reaches them over a link the PC opens to Nova Bot (<code>src/relay.ts</code>, a WebSocket with <code>AGENT_NOVA_KEY</code>), for signed-in staff only. When the PC is off, the online page says so and the other panels keep working. On the PC itself, its pages open the online Nova Agent, so there&#39;s one address; set <code>NOVA_LOCAL_UI=1</code> in <code>.env</code> to keep using the pages here (when the internet is down).</p>\n<p>On the studio PC, open <code>http://localhost:4545/agent/</code> and you get one screen that fits without scrolling: <strong>Missions</strong> on the left, <strong>Agent</strong> in the middle, <strong>Nova Quests</strong> (today&#39;s plan) on the right, and the <strong>panels</strong> along the bottom.</p>\n<p>Behind Agent sits a planner: tell it a goal and it becomes a <strong>Mission</strong> of <strong>Nova Quests</strong>, fitted around your sleep, your calendar and your travel, with reminders and check-ins as you go. And behind that sits the job it started with: a careful, self-healing browser helper that does what <a href=\"https://acuityscheduling.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Acuity Scheduling</a>&#39;s API can&#39;t, for <a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-bot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Nova Bot</a>.</p>\n<p>All the pictures here come from a separate sample copy with made-up quests and people.</p>","guide":[{"id":"at-a-glance-0","title":"At a glance","html":"<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Agent</strong></td><td>Claude, with tools for quests, missions, Calendar, Acuity (read-only) and its own status</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Missions and Quests</strong></td><td>Goals broken into quests, planned hour by hour (to the second), re-planned on every change</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Reminders</strong></td><td>Pop-ups, check-ins, a morning plan and evening wrap-up, chimes, system notifications and your phone</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Calendar</strong></td><td>Built in, saving to Nova Agent, so Agent and the calendar always agree</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Panels</strong></td><td>Portal, Calendar, Notes, Index, Observatory and Lossless audio, inside Nova Agent or in their own window</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Online</strong></td><td>The same Portal, Index, Calendar and Notes at Nova Bot&#39;s address (<code>/portal/</code> and so on), for the phones</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Index</strong></td><td>Reads what Nova Agent remembers before it replies, and learns after</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Acuity helper</strong></td><td>Changes session types, prices and paid status for Nova Bot, safely, healing itself when pages change</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Visualizer</strong></td><td>Every step the Acuity helper takes, live</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","text":"Agent Claude, with tools for quests, missions, Calendar, Acuity (read-only) and its own status Missions and Quests Goals broken into quests, planned hour by hour (to the second), re-planned on every change Reminders Pop-ups, check-ins, a morning plan and evening wrap-up, chimes, system notifications and your phone Calendar Built in, saving to Nova Agent, so Agent and the calendar always agree Panels Portal, Calendar, Notes, Index, Observatory and Lossless audio, inside Nova Agent or in their own window Online The same Portal, Index, Calendar and Notes at Nova Bot's address ( /portal/ and so on), for the phones Index Reads what Nova Agent remembers before it replies, and learns after Acuity helper Changes session types, prices and paid status for Nova Bot, safely, healing itself when pages change Visualizer Every step the Acuity helper takes, live"},{"id":"the-panels-1","title":"The panels","html":"<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Panel</th><th>What it is</th><th>On the studio PC</th><th>Online (Nova Bot)</th><th>Code</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Agent</strong></td><td>Talk to Nova Agent; Missions and Quests</td><td><code>/</code></td><td></td><td><code>src/</code>, <code>web/agent/</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Portal</strong></td><td>The staff app: enquiries, website chats, bookings, quests, alerts, Ask NovaBot, push to the phones, and sign-in, your planet, the team and invites</td><td><code>/portal/</code></td><td><code>/portal/</code></td><td><code>web/portal/</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Calendar</strong></td><td>Note cards and day cards; Nova Agent plans into it</td><td><code>/calendar/</code></td><td><code>/calendar/</code></td><td><code>web/calendar/</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Notes</strong></td><td>Notes and documents, Google Docs export</td><td><code>/notes/</code></td><td><code>/notes/</code></td><td><code>web/notes/</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Index</strong></td><td>Everything Nova Agent remembers: browse, edit, approve</td><td><code>/app/memory/</code></td><td><code>/app/memory/</code></td><td><code>web/index/</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Observatory</strong></td><td>Every project on this computer, measured and mapped</td><td><code>/observatory/</code></td><td></td><td><code>web/observatory/</code>, <code>scripts/observatory/</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Lossless audio</strong></td><td>Raw PCM between two devices, anywhere</td><td></td><td>its own address for now</td><td><code>web/lossless/</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>What they share (themes, sounds, the badge, the Manual) is in <code>web/shared/</code>. Each panel&#39;s guide is in <code>docs/apps//</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Signing in on the PC.</strong> Portal uses Nova Bot&#39;s staff API. Sign in on the Portal panel and Nova Agent signs in to Nova Bot as you (an app sign-in; the token stays in <code>data/signin.json</code> and never reaches the browser); after that the panels work with your own permissions, and Nova Agent works for you. Only Nova Agent&#39;s own pages can use it.</p>\n<p><strong>Online.</strong> Nova Bot&#39;s worker copies the panels in at build time (its <code>scripts/sync-apps.mjs</code>, from this repo&#39;s <code>web/</code>) and serves them for phones and anywhere away from the studio PC. Portal&#39;s old address (<code>/app/</code>) opens Portal; its API (<code>/app/api/</code>), Index (<code>/app/memory/</code>) and the push helper that phones which installed Portal still use (<code>/app/sw.js</code>) keep their addresses.</p>","text":"Panel What it is On the studio PC Online (Nova Bot) Code Agent Talk to Nova Agent; Missions and Quests / src/ , web/agent/ Portal The staff app: enquiries, website chats, bookings, quests, alerts, Ask NovaBot, push to the phones, and sign-in, your planet, the team and invites /portal/ /portal/ web/portal/ Calendar Note cards and day cards; Nova Agent plans into it /calendar/ /calendar/ web/calendar/ Notes Notes and documents, Google Docs export /notes/ /notes/ web/notes/ Index Everything Nova Agent remembers: browse, edit, approve /app/memory/ /app/memory/ web/index/ Observatory Every project on this computer, measured and mapped /observatory/ web/observatory/ , scripts/observatory/ Lossless audio Raw PCM between two devices, anywhere its own address for now web/lossless/ What they share (themes, sounds, the badge, the Manual) is in web/shared/ . Each panel's guide is in docs/apps// . Signing in on the PC. Portal uses Nova Bot's staff API. Sign in on the Portal panel and Nova Agent signs in to Nova Bot as you (an app sign-in; the token stays in data/signin.json and never reaches the browser); after that the panels work with your own permissions, and Nova Agent works for you. Only Nova Agent's own pages can use it. Online. Nova Bot's worker copies the panels in at build time (its scripts/sync-apps.mjs , from this repo's web/ ) and serves them for phones and anywhere away from the studio PC. Portal's old address ( /app/ ) opens Portal; its API ( /app/api/ ), Index ( /app/memory/ ) and the push helper that phones which installed Portal still use ( /app/sw.js ) keep their addresses."},{"id":"what-it-does-2","title":"What it does","html":"<h4>Agent, in the middle</h4>\n<p>Agent (<code>src/chat.ts</code>) is Claude with tools. Ask it what to do next (&quot;What should I do now?&quot; gives one clear recommendation), plan a mission, block out an evening (&quot;I&#39;m out tonight from 7 to 11&quot;), push your day back (&quot;I&#39;m running late&quot;), add or change Calendar note cards and day cards (&quot;make 31 October a Halloween day card&quot;), look at the studio&#39;s Acuity bookings, check the Acuity login, research anything on the web (with links to where it came from), look at any public webpage (it opens it in a browser of its own, never the Acuity one, and sees a screenshot and the page&#39;s contents), or ask how Nova Agent is doing. Whatever it changes shows up as a little chip under its reply, and the plan beside it redraws straight away.</p>\n<p>On a wide screen the three columns sit side by side above Nova Agent, all on one screen; on a phone or a very short window they stack (Agent first) and the page scrolls.</p>\n<h4>Missions and Quests</h4>\n<p>Today: the now card, then Ahead, Done, Coming up, Pulses and Needs a slot. Coming up: the next few days at a glance. Missions: each one&#39;s progress ring and its quests.</p>\n<p>Tell Nova Agent any goal, in the studio or anywhere in your life (&quot;release the EP by 1 December&quot;, &quot;I&#39;ve fallen behind on my 52-release challenge and have two months left: I need a content strategy, a release strategy and the quickest way to film and edit it all&quot;) and it becomes a <strong>Mission</strong>. Claude (<code>src/quests/planner.ts</code>) writes:</p>\n<ul><li>a <strong>strategy</strong>, in the sections the goal needs (release, content, production, filming and editing, a typical week, how to catch up), with the maths done;</li><li><strong>tracks</strong> (workstreams such as Music, Content, Release, Gear), each with its own colour and progress bar;</li><li>dated <strong>milestones</strong>, which also appear in Calendar as ◆ cards;</li><li><strong>Quests</strong>, each with a length, a priority, a deadline, what it waits for, where it happens and the travel to get there. Work that repeats per item (every song&#39;s finish → mix → film → edit → post) is described once as a <strong>series</strong> and written out here with exact spacing;</li><li>the <strong>assumptions</strong> it made and the <strong>questions</strong> that would sharpen it. Answer them in the mission&#39;s <strong>Refine</strong> tab (or just tell Agent) and the work that&#39;s left is planned again;</li><li><strong>research</strong>: when current facts would make the plan better (how a platform works now, distributor lead times, prices, opening hours), it searches the web and reads pages while it plans. What it used is listed under &quot;Researched on the web&quot; in the mission&#39;s Plan tab, each with a link, and only pages it really read are kept.</li></ul>\n<p>Tap a mission to open its plan: <strong>Plan</strong> (tracks and strategy), <strong>Roadmap</strong> (milestones by month, tick them off), <strong>Quests</strong> (by week, filtered by track) and <strong>Refine</strong>.</p>\n<p>As you type to Agent, a <strong>cue</strong> above the box shows what the message will become (Nova Mission, Quest, repeating quest, pulse, blocked time, quest update, mission detail, calendar card, studio bookings or a question) and what it picked out (deadline, time, length, how often, how many, platforms).</p>\n<p>Then a planner with no AI in it (<code>src/quests/scheduler.ts</code>) fits every quest into your days:</p>\n<ul><li>around your <strong>rhythm</strong>: get up, a start-up time, wind-down and bedtime, a buffer between quests, a proper break after long ones, a cap on quest hours per day, and <strong>days off</strong> with no quests at all (the ⚙ button; say &quot;I can&#39;t work Sundays&quot; and the planner sets it);</li><li>around Calendar entries and any <strong>blocked time</strong>;</li><li>most urgent first (the least slack between when it may start and its deadline, weighted by priority), never before the quests it depends on, in the part of the day it suits;</li><li>as far ahead as the furthest deadline needs (up to a year), not just the rhythm&#39;s &quot;plan ahead&quot; days;</li><li>with <strong>travel time</strong> in front of anything somewhere else, and a &quot;leave by&quot; reminder;</li><li>flagging anything that can&#39;t make its deadline as <strong>at risk</strong>, and anything that can&#39;t be placed at all under <strong>Needs a slot</strong>, with the reason.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Any length, from a second to forever</strong> (<code>src/quests/lengths.ts</code>):</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Kind</th><th>Example</th><th>How it&#39;s planned</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Seconds</td><td>&quot;Text Dana back&quot;, 30 s</td><td>Placed to the second; quick ones go back to back</td></tr><tr><td>Hours</td><td>&quot;Comp the vocal takes&quot;, 1 h 15 min</td><td>One slot</td></tr><tr><td>Long work</td><td>&quot;Mix the EP&quot;, 8 h</td><td>Split into sessions of up to 3 hours (&quot;part 2 of 3&quot;), in order</td></tr><tr><td>Ongoing</td><td>&quot;Practise scales&quot;, 20 min a day</td><td>A session every day, weekday, week or any interval, until you end it or its deadline passes</td></tr><tr><td>Pulse</td><td>&quot;Drink some water&quot;, every 2 min</td><td>Repeats faster than every 5 minutes run on their own exact timer (down to every second), only while you&#39;re awake, without taking slots in the plan</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong>Pace limits</strong> (in the rhythm) are the safety switch: on, quests start a few minutes from now, on 5-minute marks, with buffers and breaks; off, they can start right now, to the second, back to back.</p>\n<p>It <strong>re-plans on every change</strong>: finish early and the rest moves up, press Not now and it finds a new slot, and a quest left unanswered an hour after its end is moved and you&#39;re told where. Missions can be paused, resumed or removed, and a mission finishes itself when its last quest is done.</p>\n<h4>Reminders, check-ins and chimes</h4>\n<p>Checked every 10 seconds (<code>src/quests/reminders.ts</code>):</p>\n<ul><li>a <strong>reminder</strong> before each quest (or before you need to leave), with Start and In 15 min;</li><li>a <strong>check-in</strong> when it should be finished: Done, +15 min or Move it;</li><li>a <strong>morning plan</strong> and an <strong>evening wrap-up</strong>;</li><li>each <strong>pulse</strong> as one ticking card that counts its beats, instead of a pile of pop-ups.</li></ul>\n<p>Each kind has its own bright <strong>chime</strong>, made live in the browser. Press 🔔 for <strong>system notifications</strong>, which arrive even with Nova Agent in the background and bring it back when clicked. With the rhythm&#39;s phone setting on, they also go to the <strong>your phone</strong>, where Nova Agent, Quest and Mission alerts each have their own label, check-ins stay on screen until they&#39;re answered, and a pulse replaces its last notification.</p>\n<h4>Quests on the phones</h4>\n<p>Nova Agent sends its plan (missions, quests, pulses, and Calendar&#39;s note and day cards) to Nova Bot&#39;s worker whenever it changes, and every minute so &quot;now&quot; keeps moving (<code>src/quests/portalsync.ts</code>). Portal&#39;s Quests and Calendar tabs show it on the staff phones, and taps made there (Done, Start, Not now, Skip, pause a mission) come back with each job check and are carried out within about a second.</p>\n<h4>Calendar, built in</h4>\n<p>Calendar is a panel (<code>web/calendar/</code>) served at <code>/calendar/</code>. Inside Nova Agent it saves to <code>data/calendar.json</code> instead of only the browser, so Agent, the planner and the calendar always see the same note cards and day cards. Every planned quest and blocked time shows up in it as a note card (✦ for a quest, ∞ for a repeat, ⚠ when at risk, ✓ when done), and its theme colours the whole of Nova Agent. The <strong>Calendar</strong> tab fits it to the plan column with no scrolling.</p>\n<h4>The Nova Agent, inside or in a window</h4>\n<p>The ✦ Nova Agent launcher, with the &quot;Open apps&quot; switch. Calendar opened inside Nova Agent from the rail.</p>\n<p>The rail down the left (and the ✦ Nova Agent launcher) holds every Nova app: Portal, Notes, Calendar, Nova Bot, the visualizer, Index, Admin, all links and features, Observatory and the code. One switch decides where they open:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Inside Nova Agent</strong>: the app takes the middle of the screen, with &quot;← Nova Agent&quot;, reload and &quot;↗ open in its own window&quot; above it. Nova Agent serves Calendar, Notes (<code>/notes/</code>), Observatory (<code>/observatory/</code>) and Index (<code>/app/memory/</code>) itself, from the folders next to it, so they open inside in any browser.</li><li><strong>New window</strong>: each app in its own tab or window.</li></ul>\n<p>Admin and the links page always get their own window: they refuse to be shown inside other pages, which keeps their sign-in safe, and Nova Agent says so once.</p>\n<h4>Sound effects</h4>\n<p>Novacane&#39;s soft glass tones, warm under-tones and breaths of air for every tap, tab, switch, open, close, send, done and delete, made live with the Web Audio API (no sound files). Ambient, not beeps: everything swells in, chords bloom together rather than running up like a game, and a tap is a low felt touch. They&#39;re in D lydian, the same key as the ambient music, so the two always sound right together; they&#39;re placed across left and right and washed in a little reverb and echo, and kept quiet: calm, relaxing and lush, never loud or chatty. Every sound swells in slowly, with a warm, soft top end and plenty of space; never more than three notes at once; the small sounds (taps, tabs, menus) keep well apart and the same one doesn&#39;t come straight back.</p>\n<p><strong>Quiet extras</strong>, barely there and with their own switch (Portal → Options → Quiet extras, or on a phone the gear → Quiet extras): a breath of air as you scroll (quieter the slower you go, a few times a second at most), the softest touch per key when typing in a box, tones that rise and fall as you drag a slider, a sound when you pick up and put down something you drag (Calendar&#39;s note cards, with a tiny tick at each step), and an extra-faint shimmer as the mouse arrives on a tile. They&#39;re off to begin with (calm first) and only heard while sound effects are on. Nova Agent chimes when it answers, and a short &quot;hello&quot; (D–A–C♯–F♯) plays when sounds are switched on. The 🔊 switch at the top left turns them off (on a phone: the gear → Sound), and the choice is remembered on that device. It&#39;s the same <code>web/shared/sfx.js</code> in every panel.</p>\n<p><strong>Every panel sounds like itself</strong>, all in the same key: Notes is paper and pencil, Calendar soft clock ticks and chimes, Portal deep and roomy like its planet, Index droplets that echo away, Observatory the wide night sky, Lossless audio a soft electric piano, Visualizer glass glints, Quests a warm kalimba and Missions a low, steady swell. A button that opens a panel sounds like that panel. Different kinds of things have their own sounds (switches, tick boxes, menus, lists, links, tabs…), each button has its own notes, and no sound plays exactly the same way twice running, so they never get too familiar. When sounds come thick and fast they get softer by themselves, and come back after a pause.</p>\n<h4>The panels bar and motion</h4>\n<p>It shows and hides itself (<strong>Auto</strong>, the default): always there on Nova Agent&#39;s home. With a panel open it follows what you do, not timers: on a computer it&#39;s in view while the mouse is near the bottom and steps aside once you work higher up in the panel; on a phone it steps aside when you scroll down a good way on purpose and comes back as soon as you scroll up a little or tap the little handle at the bottom (pages that hardly scroll never hide it).</p>\n<p>Each panel&#39;s icon is from one line-art set, in its own colour (Notes amber, Calendar moon-violet, Index teal…) blended with the theme&#39;s accent, so the icons change with the theme and still keep their own mood. It can also be <strong>Always shown</strong> or <strong>Always hidden</strong>: choose in the Panels window (the PANELS button) or on a phone in the gear (Bar). Remembered on the device (<code>web/agent/assets/bar.js</code> and <code>bar.css</code>).</p>\n<p>Along the bottom on a computer: every panel in its four groups (Apps, Tasks, Tools, Helpers), edge to edge. It&#39;s the same bar whatever is open; with a panel open it only gets smaller. Motion is light (only scale and opacity move): buttons and tiles press in softly, the open panel&#39;s tile breathes, and panels fade in as they open (<code>web/shared/inside.js</code>, and Calendar&#39;s <code>embed.js</code>). It all stops when the device asks for less motion or Portal&#39;s Options → Animations is off.</p>\n<h4>One look, the top bar, and the status line</h4>\n<p><strong>One theme for everything:</strong> in the Panels window (the gear at the top; on a phone the phone&#39;s gear → Theme &amp; look) pick a theme (Novacane, Solar Flare, Pulsar, Aurora, Eclipse, Quasar or Mono) and every app, task, tool and helper wears it, whatever its own theme setting; &quot;Each panel&#39;s own&quot; goes back to each panel&#39;s own. <strong>Colour everything from my planet</strong> tints it all with the colours of your planet in Portal (Nova Bot sends them with who you are). Saved on the device; every open panel follows at once (<code>web/shared/look.js</code>, loaded first in every panel).</p>\n<p><strong>The top bar</strong> (Nova Agent&#39;s header) has the same choice as the panels bar: Auto (with a panel open it slides away while you work and comes back when the mouse goes to the top, or you scroll up on a phone), Always shown, or Always hidden. Typing in any box hides the panels bar until you&#39;re done or the mouse goes to the bottom.</p>\n<p><strong>The status line</strong> runs under the panels bar (inside the bar on a phone), one line tall: the version and build, the latest change in a few still words (for the group or panel you point at, or the one that&#39;s open), when you came on and were last off, what you&#39;ve done lately (tap it for the list) and a 12-hour clock (<code>web/agent/assets/status.js</code>; the words come from <code>web/shared/status-data.js</code>, made by <code>npm run status</code>, which <code>npm run manual</code> runs too).</p>\n<p><strong>The icons</strong> are little glowing scenes of space, each on its own small Novacane nebula (its own colour mixed with the theme&#39;s): the Novacane sigil in an orbiting orb (Agent), a ringed planet and its moon (Portal), the moon over its phases (Calendar), a quill writing a constellation (Notes), a glowing star cluster (Index), a comet streaking to a star flag (Quests), a rocket (Missions), a pulsar (Lossless audio), a spiral galaxy (Visualizer), a domed observatory under the moon (Observatory) and a star atlas (Manual). The panels bar itself is a strip of night sky: nebula light in the theme&#39;s colours, faint stars, the sigil softly in the corner, a glowing edge and shimmering group names; its tiles sit right on the sky (no boxes), with a soft glow behind the one you point at and a line of light under the open one. The same glowing edge and nebula light are on the top bar, the columns, an open panel&#39;s frame, the pop-up windows and the status line, and every button, tab and box (in the panels too) glows the same way when you&#39;re on it (<code>glow.css</code>). On a computer the top bar, the panels bar and the status line are only as wide as what&#39;s in them. <strong>Centred text:</strong> all text in Nova Agent and its panels is centred (Panels window → Centre all text switches it off); what you write in a Notes document, and code, keep their own alignment. It comes and goes with a quick spring, its tiles popping in one after another. The gear (settings) is on computers too: it opens the Panels window.</p>\n<h4>The latest polish</h4>\n<ul><li>The panels bar is smaller, with each group&#39;s name centred between two fine lines of light.</li><li>The status line is plain words with small icons: the version, what&#39;s new (&quot;Calendar: note cards back&quot;), &quot;Here since …&quot;, &quot;Last left …&quot;, what you did last (&quot;Opened Notes · 2 min ago&quot;: tap for the list) and the day and time.</li><li>The two settings buttons look different: sliders at the top for Look &amp; layout (theme, bars, text), and the sun and moon over the horizon on Quests for your daily rhythm.</li><li>Quests fits more on one screen: the next thing is a full card, the rest slim one-line rows (time and title) that open on a tap.</li><li>Scrollbars everywhere are slim, rounded and glowing in the theme&#39;s colours, with soft sounds when you take hold of one, as you drag it (a tone that follows where you are) and let go.</li><li>The sky behind Nova Agent is a deep nebula with a faint band of the galaxy and far galaxies, and it takes on the colour of the app that&#39;s open, slowly.</li><li>The columns&#39; titles are centred, and so is the conversation (every message in the middle).</li></ul>\n<h4>Every window size</h4>\n<p>Nova Agent fits whatever size its window is: computer windows down to 481px tall keep the computer layout, getting tighter as they get shorter (a slimmer header, Agent&#39;s suggestions in one row you swipe, smaller bars); narrower computer windows get slimmer side columns and smaller buttons; tablets and windows between phone and computer size get the bar in one centred row; and phones keep their own layout. In Auto, the mouse anywhere in the lower part of the window (its bottom 14%) brings the panels bar up. Inside Nova Agent, Notes never runs off the screen: its toolbar wraps, and the page starts as tall as the window.</p>\n<h4>Today in music (the front page)</h4>\n<p>Under the welcome, until you start talking to Agent: small cards, a line or two each. The <strong>Top 10 worldwide</strong> (live: the songs most played on Apple Music across 12 countries, via Nova Bot&#39;s /music-world, kept 6 hours), <strong>popular genres</strong>, <strong>budget gear</strong> (what each does, rough price), the <strong>music industry</strong> (IFPI Global Music Report 2026: $31.7bn in 2025, up 6.4%), a musician&#39;s <strong>quote of the day</strong> with their picture (from Wikipedia; &quot;attributed&quot; when its origin isn&#39;t certain) and a <strong>song of the day</strong> (named and described, with a link to its lyrics: lyrics themselves are copyrighted). A tap on a card opens a short list. Data: <code>web/agent/assets/music-data.js</code>.</p>\n<h4>Phones and tablets</h4>\n<p>Nova Agent knows when it&#39;s on a phone or a tablet from the device itself (iPads included), not just the window&#39;s size (<code>look.js</code> puts is-touch / is-phone / is-tablet on every page). There it&#39;s made for fingers and kept light: bigger tap targets, no zoom when you tap into a box, nothing that needs a mouse, no frosted-glass blur or drifting sky. On a tablet showing the computer layout the bars hide and show with your swipes and a handle brings them back. The conversation&#39;s pages turn with a sideways swipe (<code>web/agent/assets/touch.css</code>).</p>\n<h4>Ambient music</h4>\n<p>Quiet, never-ending Novacane ambient music: slow warm pads, a soft bass, star-like bells, now and then a short soft electric-piano phrase, and a faint ocean of air, all made live (no sound files, nothing downloaded) by <code>web/shared/ambient.js</code>. It&#39;s off until you switch it on with the ♫ switch at the top left (on a phone: the gear → Music; in Portal: its music button). There&#39;s one player for the whole app, in Nova Agent&#39;s main page, so it carries on while panels open and close, and every switch shows the same state. On or off is remembered on the device: when it was on, it starts again on your first tap (browsers only allow sound after a tap). The volume is Portal&#39;s Options → Ambient music volume.</p>\n<h4>Index: it remembers</h4>\n<p>Before each reply and each mission plan, Nova Agent asks Index (the suite&#39;s shared memory, on Nova Bot&#39;s worker) for the few facts that matter: the studio&#39;s, and those of the person Nova Agent works for (found by itself: see below). The read is quick (a short timeout and a 30-second cache) and never holds a reply up for long. After each conversation, the exchange is handed back to be learned from, in the background (<code>src/memory.ts</code>). It reads studio and staff memory only, never customers&#39;.</p>\n<p>Index itself opens inside Nova Agent from the rail, through Nova Agent&#39;s own key: you can browse and edit the studio&#39;s and staff memory there, while approvals of customers&#39; facts stay behind a Portal sign-in. Without <code>AGENT_NOVA_KEY</code>, memory is simply switched off.</p>\n<h4>The Acuity helper</h4>\n<p>The job Nova Agent was built for. It drives Acuity&#39;s admin pages in a real Chromium, the way a person would, for the jobs Acuity&#39;s API can&#39;t do.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Jobs from Nova Bot</strong> (<code>src/jobs.ts</code>): it waits on the worker for jobs and picks each one up within about a second. Today that&#39;s <code>change</code> jobs (staff asked in Portal to change a booking&#39;s session type, price or paid status); it does them in Acuity, checks the result and reports back to staff phones. Customer bookings go through Acuity&#39;s own booking page, so the deposit is always paid first; <code>book</code> jobs are still understood here.</li><li><strong>Logs itself in</strong> and saves the session; logs back in when it expires.</li><li><strong>Self-healing element finder</strong> (<code>src/heal/</code>): every task says <em>what</em> it wants (&quot;the Cancel Appointment button&quot;), never <em>how</em> to find it. <code>resolve()</code> tries the selector memory first (instant and free), then asks Claude, checks the answer against the page, and remembers it.</li><li><strong>Appointment actions</strong> (<code>src/acuity/</code>) from the command line: list, search, book, cancel, edit and reschedule.</li><li><strong>Safety first</strong>: a dry-run mode that stops before every final click, a second layer that refuses any change-making request, exact-match rules for cancel and edit, and a read-only healthcheck every morning. See Safety.</li></ul>\n<h4>The visualizer</h4>\n<p>Anatomy, live steps, what the browser sees and the selector memory.  Where the agent last found each element, and how often.</p>\n<p><code>/visualizer</code> shows the Acuity helper at work: its anatomy, every step in plain English, what the browser sees, and its memory. Its buttons only ever run read-only tasks (check the login, the next 7 or last 30 days, a read-only tour, the healthcheck), and <strong>Wipe memory</strong> lets you watch it heal again. These screenshots are of an idle visualizer: at work it shows real Acuity pages and client names, which is why Nova Agent only ever listens on <code>127.0.0.1</code>.</p>\n<h4>An app for your launcher</h4>\n<p>Open <code>http://localhost:4545/agent/</code> (or the online address, on a phone: Share → Add to Home Screen) and press <strong>Install app</strong>: Nova Agent opens in its own window, with shortcuts to Today, a new mission, Calendar and the visualizer. Its service worker shows reminders as system notifications; nothing is cached, because Nova Agent is its own server on the same machine.</p>","text":"Agent, in the middle Agent ( src/chat.ts ) is Claude with tools. Ask it what to do next (\"What should I do now?\" gives one clear recommendation), plan a mission, block out an evening (\"I'm out tonight from 7 to 11\"), push your day back (\"I'm running late\"), add or change Calendar note cards and day cards (\"make 31 October a Halloween day card\"), look at the studio's Acuity bookings, check the Acuity login, research anything on the web (with links to where it came from), look at any public webpage (it opens it in a browser of its own, never the Acuity one, and sees a screenshot and the page's contents), or ask how Nova Agent is doing. Whatever it changes shows up as a little chip under its reply, and the plan beside it redraws straight away. On a wide screen the three columns sit side by side above Nova Agent, all on one screen; on a phone or a very short window they stack (Agent first) and the page scrolls. Missions and Quests Today: the now card, then Ahead, Done, Coming up, Pulses and Needs a slot. Coming up: the next few days at a glance. Missions: each one's progress ring and its quests. Tell Nova Agent any goal, in the studio or anywhere in your life (\"release the EP by 1 December\", \"I've fallen behind on my 52-release challenge and have two months left: I need a content strategy, a release strategy and the quickest way to film and edit it all\") and it becomes a Mission . Claude ( src/quests/planner.ts ) writes: a strategy , in the sections the goal needs (release, content, production, filming and editing, a typical week, how to catch up), with the maths done; tracks (workstreams such as Music, Content, Release, Gear), each with its own colour and progress bar; dated milestones , which also appear in Calendar as ◆ cards; Quests , each with a length, a priority, a deadline, what it waits for, where it happens and the travel to get there. Work that repeats per item (every song's finish → mix → film → edit → post) is described once as a series and written out here with exact spacing; the assumptions it made and the questions that would sharpen it. Answer them in the mission's Refine tab (or just tell Agent) and the work that's left is planned again; research : when current facts would make the plan better (how a platform works now, distributor lead times, prices, opening hours), it searches the web and reads pages while it plans. What it used is listed under \"Researched on the web\" in the mission's Plan tab, each with a link, and only pages it really read are kept. Tap a mission to open its plan: Plan (tracks and strategy), Roadmap (milestones by month, tick them off), Quests (by week, filtered by track) and Refine . As you type to Agent, a cue above the box shows what the message will become (Nova Mission, Quest, repeating quest, pulse, blocked time, quest update, mission detail, calendar card, studio bookings or a question) and what it picked out (deadline, time, length, how often, how many, platforms). Then a planner with no AI in it ( src/quests/scheduler.ts ) fits every quest into your days: around your rhythm : get up, a start-up time, wind-down and bedtime, a buffer between quests, a proper break after long ones, a cap on quest hours per day, and days off with no quests at all (the ⚙ button; say \"I can't work Sundays\" and the planner sets it); around Calendar entries and any blocked time ; most urgent first (the least slack between when it may start and its deadline, weighted by priority), never before the quests it depends on, in the part of the day it suits; as far ahead as the furthest deadline needs (up to a year), not just the rhythm's \"plan ahead\" days; with travel time in front of anything somewhere else, and a \"leave by\" reminder; flagging anything that can't make its deadline as at risk , and anything that can't be placed at all under Needs a slot , with the reason. Any length, from a second to forever ( src/quests/lengths.ts ): Kind Example How it's planned Seconds \"Text Dana back\", 30 s Placed to the second"},{"id":"safety-3","title":"Safety","html":"<ul><li><strong>Dry run</strong> (<code>DRY_RUN=true</code>): book, cancel and edit stop before the final click. As a second layer, the browser refuses any request that could change something in Acuity. Acuity&#39;s cancel is a plain GET, so this also blocks anything carrying Acuity&#39;s <code>__csrf_magic</code> change token.</li><li><strong>The healthcheck</strong> always runs with that second layer on, even when live.</li><li><strong>Cancel and edit</strong> need an exact date and time match (and the client&#39;s name if given). If more than one appointment matches, the agent refuses.</li><li><strong>Agent is read-only in Acuity</strong>: it can look at bookings and check the login, never book, move or cancel.</li><li><strong>The page&#39;s buttons</strong> only work from the page itself (a custom header other websites can&#39;t send), and Nova Agent only listens on this computer.</li><li><strong>Alerts</strong> (login problems, failed healthchecks) go to the console, <code>data/alerts.log</code>, and staff phones through the worker when <code>AGENT_NOVA_KEY</code> is set. Repeats are held back for six hours.</li></ul>","text":"Dry run ( DRY_RUN=true ): book, cancel and edit stop before the final click. As a second layer, the browser refuses any request that could change something in Acuity. Acuity's cancel is a plain GET, so this also blocks anything carrying Acuity's __csrf_magic change token. The healthcheck always runs with that second layer on, even when live. Cancel and edit need an exact date and time match (and the client's name if given). If more than one appointment matches, the agent refuses. Agent is read-only in Acuity : it can look at bookings and check the login, never book, move or cancel. The page's buttons only work from the page itself (a custom header other websites can't send), and Nova Agent only listens on this computer. Alerts (login problems, failed healthchecks) go to the console, data/alerts.log , and staff phones through the worker when AGENT_NOVA_KEY is set. Repeats are held back for six hours."},{"id":"works-with-4","title":"Works with","html":"<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Project</th><th>What it is</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong><a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-agent\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">nova-agent</a></strong></td><td>This repo: the studio&#39;s one app, with every panel</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-bot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">nova-bot</a></td><td>NovaBot on the website, and Nova Agent&#39;s back end online (sign-in, push, bookings, memory, jobs)</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-club\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">nova-club</a></td><td>Members&#39; Android app that shows the studio&#39;s busy times</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","text":"Project What it is nova-agent This repo: the studio's one app, with every panel nova-bot NovaBot on the website, and Nova Agent's back end online (sign-in, push, bookings, memory, jobs) nova-club Members' Android app that shows the studio's busy times"}],"built":[{"id":"how-it-works-0","title":"How it works","html":"<pre><code>flowchart LR\n    You[You, at the studio PC] --&gt; UI[Nova Agent page&lt;br/&gt;Agent · plan · suite]\n    UI --&gt; Chat[Agent&lt;br/&gt;src/chat.ts] --&gt; Claude[Claude]\n    Chat --&gt; Q[(Quests and calendar&lt;br/&gt;data/)]\n    UI --&gt; Q\n    Chat &lt;--&gt;|reads before, learns after| NI[Index&lt;br/&gt;on Nova Bot&#39;s worker]\n    Q --&gt;|plan, reminders| Phone[your phone]\n    S[Staff in Portal] --&gt; NB[Nova Bot Worker]\n    NB --&gt;|queues jobs| J[(agent_jobs)]\n    NA[Acuity helper] --&gt;|&quot;any jobs?&quot; long-poll| J\n    NA --&gt; R[resolve&amp;#40;&amp;#41;] --&gt;|1st| M[(Selector memory)]\n    R --&gt;|if memory fails| Claude\n    NA --&gt; B[Playwright Chromium] --&gt; A[Acuity admin pages]\n    NA --&gt;|result| NB</code></pre>\n<ul><li><strong>No open ports.</strong> Nova Agent only listens on <code>127.0.0.1</code> and only calls out to the worker, so it runs on any always-on computer.</li><li><strong>Limits.</strong> <code>BOOKINGS_PER_VISITOR_PER_DAY</code> (default 2) is sent to the worker each time Nova Agent checks in.</li><li><strong>Notes on Acuity&#39;s real pages</strong> (addresses, buttons, forms, and the safety finding that cancelling is a plain GET) are in docs/acuity-ui-notes.md. Read it before changing cancel, book or edit.</li></ul>","text":"flowchart LR You[You, at the studio PC] --> UI[Nova Agent page<br/>Agent · plan · suite] UI --> Chat[Agent<br/>src/chat.ts] --> Claude[Claude] Chat --> Q[(Quests and calendar<br/>data/)] UI --> Q Chat <-->|reads before, learns after| NI[Index<br/>on Nova Bot's worker] Q -->|plan, reminders| Phone[your phone] S[Staff in Portal] --> NB[Nova Bot Worker] NB -->|queues jobs| J[(agent_jobs)] NA[Acuity helper] -->|\"any jobs?\" long-poll| J NA --> R[resolve&#40;&#41;] -->|1st| M[(Selector memory)] R -->|if memory fails| Claude NA --> B[Playwright Chromium] --> A[Acuity admin pages] NA -->|result| NB No open ports. Nova Agent only listens on 127.0.0.1 and only calls out to the worker, so it runs on any always-on computer. Limits. BOOKINGS_PER_VISITOR_PER_DAY (default 2) is sent to the worker each time Nova Agent checks in. Notes on Acuity's real pages (addresses, buttons, forms, and the safety finding that cancelling is a plain GET) are in docs/acuity-ui-notes.md. Read it before changing cancel, book or edit."},{"id":"run-it-locally-1","title":"Run it locally","html":"<p>You need Node 22 or newer. Acuity is only needed for the Acuity helper, and only with an account you&#39;re allowed to automate.</p>\n<pre><code>git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-agent.git\ncd nova-agent             # (already cloned? git submodule update --init  brings in calendar/)\nnpm install\nnpx playwright install chromium\ncp .env.example .env      # then fill it in\nnpm run visualizer        # http://localhost:4545/agent/\nnpm run login             # for the Acuity helper: log in once in a visible browser window\nnpm start                 # should say &quot;Logged in to Acuity&quot;</code></pre>\n<p>Agent and mission planning need <code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code> in <code>.env</code> (Claude also powers the self-healing element finder). Jobs, phone alerts, the phones&#39; Quests sync and Index memory need <code>AGENT_NOVA_KEY</code>; without it they&#39;re simply off. To bring the calendar up to date with its own repo: <code>git submodule update --remote calendar</code>.</p>\n<p>Observatory, Notes and Index open inside Nova Agent when their repos sit next to this one (<code>../no</code>, <code>../nn</code>, <code>../ni</code>).</p>\n<p><code>DRY_RUN=true</code> is the default in <code>.env.example</code>, so book, cancel and edit stop before the final click until you decide otherwise.</p>\n<h4>A second copy with sample data</h4>\n<p><code>NOVA_DATA_DIR</code> points Nova Agent at another data folder, so a preview or a screenshots copy never touches the real quests, calendar or Acuity session:</p>\n<pre><code>NOVA_DATA_DIR=/tmp/nova-sample AGENT_NOVA_KEY= DRY_RUN=true VISUALIZER_PORT=4547 npm run visualizer</code></pre>\n<p>With <code>AGENT_NOVA_KEY</code> empty it won&#39;t collect jobs, read memory or send phone alerts.</p>\n<h4>Commands</h4>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>npm run visualizer</code></td><td>Nova Agent itself: Agent and plan at http://localhost:4545, reminders, the phones&#39; Quests sync, the daily healthcheck and job collection (<code>npm run service</code> is the same)</td></tr><tr><td><code>npm start</code></td><td>Checks the Acuity login; logs in automatically if the session expired</td></tr><tr><td><code>npm run login</code></td><td>Opens a visible browser so you can log in to Acuity by hand</td></tr><tr><td><code>npm run list</code></td><td>Appointments for the next 7 days</td></tr><tr><td><code>npm run list -- 2026-09-01 2026-09-30</code></td><td>Appointments between two dates</td></tr><tr><td><code>npm run search -- name=Kai</code></td><td>Search; also <code>type=</code>, <code>email=</code>, <code>phone=</code>, <code>from=</code>, <code>to=</code> (default: today to 60 days ahead)</td></tr><tr><td><code>npm run book -- &quot;type=...&quot; date=... time=... first=... last=... email=...</code></td><td>Book (stops before the final click if <code>DRY_RUN=true</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>npm run cancel -- date=... time=... &quot;name=...&quot; [notify=no]</code></td><td>Cancel (same safety)</td></tr><tr><td><code>npm run edit -- date=... time=... &quot;name=...&quot; [phone= email= first= last= type= notes= newdate= newtime=]</code></td><td>Edit and/or reschedule (same safety)</td></tr><tr><td><code>npm run healthcheck</code></td><td>Read-only check that every Acuity page and button can still be found</td></tr><tr><td><code>npm run typecheck</code></td><td>Checks the code for type errors</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h4>Running it all the time</h4>\n<p><code>deploy/agent-nova.service</code> is a systemd <strong>user</strong> service that runs Nova Agent (the page, reminders, the daily healthcheck and job collection), starts when you log in, and restarts if it crashes. Edit its <code>WorkingDirectory</code> to where you cloned the repo, then:</p>\n<pre><code>cp deploy/agent-nova.service ~/.config/systemd/user/\nsystemctl --user daemon-reload\nsystemctl --user enable --now agent-nova\njournalctl --user -u agent-nova -f      # its log\nsystemctl --user restart agent-nova     # after changing .env or code\nloginctl enable-linger $USER            # keep it running when logged out</code></pre>\n<p>On a server with no screen, <code>npm run login</code> won&#39;t work; with <code>ACUITY_EMAIL</code> and <code>ACUITY_PASSWORD</code> set, the agent logs itself in instead. View it through an SSH tunnel: <code>ssh -L 4545:localhost:4545 your-server</code>.</p>","text":"You need Node 22 or newer. Acuity is only needed for the Acuity helper, and only with an account you're allowed to automate. git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-agent.git cd nova-agent # (already cloned? git submodule update --init brings in calendar/) npm install npx playwright install chromium cp .env.example .env # then fill it in npm run visualizer # http://localhost:4545/agent/ npm run login # for the Acuity helper: log in once in a visible browser window npm start # should say \"Logged in to Acuity\" Agent and mission planning need ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in .env (Claude also powers the self-healing element finder). Jobs, phone alerts, the phones' Quests sync and Index memory need AGENT_NOVA_KEY ; without it they're simply off. To bring the calendar up to date with its own repo: git submodule update --remote calendar . Observatory, Notes and Index open inside Nova Agent when their repos sit next to this one ( ../no , ../nn , ../ni ). DRY_RUN=true is the default in .env.example , so book, cancel and edit stop before the final click until you decide otherwise. A second copy with sample data NOVA_DATA_DIR points Nova Agent at another data folder, so a preview or a screenshots copy never touches the real quests, calendar or Acuity session: NOVA_DATA_DIR=/tmp/nova-sample AGENT_NOVA_KEY= DRY_RUN=true VISUALIZER_PORT=4547 npm run visualizer With AGENT_NOVA_KEY empty it won't collect jobs, read memory or send phone alerts. Commands Command What it does npm run visualizer Nova Agent itself: Agent and plan at http://localhost:4545, reminders, the phones' Quests sync, the daily healthcheck and job collection ( npm run service is the same) npm start Checks the Acuity login; logs in automatically if the session expired npm run login Opens a visible browser so you can log in to Acuity by hand npm run list Appointments for the next 7 days npm run list -- 2026-09-01 2026-09-30 Appointments between two dates npm run search -- name=Kai Search; also type= , email= , phone= , from= , to= (default: today to 60 days ahead) npm run book -- \"type=...\" date=... time=... first=... last=... email=... Book (stops before the final click if DRY_RUN=true ) npm run cancel -- date=... time=... \"name=...\" [notify=no] Cancel (same safety) npm run edit -- date=... time=... \"name=...\" [phone= email= first= last= type= notes= newdate= newtime=] Edit and/or reschedule (same safety) npm run healthcheck Read-only check that every Acuity page and button can still be found npm run typecheck Checks the code for type errors Running it all the time deploy/agent-nova.service is a systemd user service that runs Nova Agent (the page, reminders, the daily healthcheck and job collection), starts when you log in, and restarts if it crashes. Edit its WorkingDirectory to where you cloned the repo, then: cp deploy/agent-nova.service ~/.config/systemd/user/ systemctl --user daemon-reload systemctl --user enable --now agent-nova journalctl --user -u agent-nova -f # its log systemctl --user restart agent-nova # after changing .env or code loginctl enable-linger $USER # keep it running when logged out On a server with no screen, npm run login won't work; with ACUITY_EMAIL and ACUITY_PASSWORD set, the agent logs itself in instead. View it through an SSH tunnel: ssh -L 4545:localhost:4545 your-server ."},{"id":"configuration-2","title":"Configuration","html":"<p>All settings come from <code>.env</code> (copy <code>.env.example</code>); variables already set in the shell win. Names only here; never commit <code>.env</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Default</th><th>What it&#39;s for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code></td><td>–</td><td>Agent, mission planning and the AI element finder</td></tr><tr><td><code>NOVA_MODEL</code></td><td><code>claude-opus-5-5</code></td><td>The Claude model name</td></tr><tr><td><code>NOVA_WORKER_URL</code></td><td>Novacane&#39;s worker</td><td>Nova Bot&#39;s worker: jobs, alerts, the phones&#39; Quests sync and Index</td></tr><tr><td><code>AGENT_NOVA_KEY</code></td><td>–</td><td>Must match the worker&#39;s <code>AGENT_NOVA_KEY</code> secret; blank = no jobs, phone alerts, Quests sync or memory</td></tr><tr><td><code>NOVA_STAFF_ID</code></td><td><em>(found by itself)</em></td><td>Only to force who Nova Agent works for. Without it, Nova Agent picks the studio&#39;s first Portal admin, and anyone can switch it to themselves with <strong>Connect as me</strong> on the Nova Agent badge (kept in <code>data/staff.json</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>NOVA_DATA_DIR</code></td><td><code>data/</code></td><td>Where everything is kept; point a second copy somewhere else</td></tr><tr><td><code>ACUITY_EMAIL</code>, <code>ACUITY_PASSWORD</code></td><td>–</td><td>Automatic re-login</td></tr><tr><td><code>ACUITY_ADMIN_URL</code></td><td>Acuity&#39;s appointments page</td><td>The page used to check the login</td></tr><tr><td><code>ACUITY_TIMEZONE</code></td><td><code>Europe/London</code></td><td>The business&#39;s timezone; &quot;today&quot; is worked out in it</td></tr><tr><td><code>JOBS_EVERY_SECONDS</code></td><td><code>10</code></td><td>How long to wait before asking again if the worker answers at once</td></tr><tr><td><code>ACTION_PAUSE_MS</code></td><td><code>150</code></td><td>Longest human-like pause before each click or typed box (0 = flat out)</td></tr><tr><td><code>BOOKINGS_PER_VISITOR_PER_DAY</code></td><td><code>2</code></td><td>A number, or <code>unlimited</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>HEALTHCHECK_CRON</code></td><td><code>0 6 * * *</code></td><td>When the read-only healthcheck runs (UK time)</td></tr><tr><td><code>VISUALIZER_PORT</code></td><td><code>4545</code></td><td>Nova Agent&#39;s page</td></tr><tr><td><code>HEADLESS</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Show the browser or not</td></tr><tr><td><code>DRY_RUN</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Stop before every final click (the status pill says <strong>Rehearsal</strong>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>NOTIFY_CLIENTS</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Tick Acuity&#39;s &quot;Send email to client&quot; when cancelling</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Your rhythm (wake, sleep, buffers, breaks, the daily cap, reminders, check-ins, briefings, phone alerts and pace limits) is set on the page with ⚙, or by asking Agent.</p>\n<p>Everything Nova Agent writes at run time goes in <code>data/</code> (or <code>NOVA_DATA_DIR</code>), which git ignores: quests and missions (<code>quests.json</code>), the calendar (<code>calendar.json</code>), the saved Acuity session (<code>session.json</code>, which works like a password), the selector memory, the healthcheck result, screenshots, daily logs (<code>logs/.jsonl</code>, which include client names) and <code>alerts.log</code>.</p>","text":"All settings come from .env (copy .env.example ); variables already set in the shell win. Names only here; never commit .env . Name Default What it's for ANTHROPIC_API_KEY – Agent, mission planning and the AI element finder NOVA_MODEL claude-opus-5-5 The Claude model name NOVA_WORKER_URL Novacane's worker Nova Bot's worker: jobs, alerts, the phones' Quests sync and Index AGENT_NOVA_KEY – Must match the worker's AGENT_NOVA_KEY secret; blank = no jobs, phone alerts, Quests sync or memory NOVA_STAFF_ID (found by itself) Only to force who Nova Agent works for. Without it, Nova Agent picks the studio's first Portal admin, and anyone can switch it to themselves with Connect as me on the Nova Agent badge (kept in data/staff.json ) NOVA_DATA_DIR data/ Where everything is kept; point a second copy somewhere else ACUITY_EMAIL , ACUITY_PASSWORD – Automatic re-login ACUITY_ADMIN_URL Acuity's appointments page The page used to check the login ACUITY_TIMEZONE Europe/London The business's timezone; \"today\" is worked out in it JOBS_EVERY_SECONDS 10 How long to wait before asking again if the worker answers at once ACTION_PAUSE_MS 150 Longest human-like pause before each click or typed box (0 = flat out) BOOKINGS_PER_VISITOR_PER_DAY 2 A number, or unlimited HEALTHCHECK_CRON 0 6 * * * When the read-only healthcheck runs (UK time) VISUALIZER_PORT 4545 Nova Agent's page HEADLESS true Show the browser or not DRY_RUN true Stop before every final click (the status pill says Rehearsal ) NOTIFY_CLIENTS true Tick Acuity's \"Send email to client\" when cancelling Your rhythm (wake, sleep, buffers, breaks, the daily cap, reminders, check-ins, briefings, phone alerts and pace limits) is set on the page with ⚙, or by asking Agent. Everything Nova Agent writes at run time goes in data/ (or NOVA_DATA_DIR ), which git ignores: quests and missions ( quests.json ), the calendar ( calendar.json ), the saved Acuity session ( session.json , which works like a password), the selector memory, the healthcheck result, screenshots, daily logs ( logs/.jsonl , which include client names) and alerts.log ."},{"id":"tests-3","title":"Tests","html":"<p><code>npm test</code> runs the Quest reminders on a simulated clock (Vitest fake timers, a pretend Nova Bot worker and a throwaway data folder: <code>test/harness.ts</code>): a reminder every 30 minutes for 4 hours pings exactly 8 times, a ping the worker turns away is retried, Nova Agent being off across a session gives one late &quot;Missed&quot; ping, no session is moved past without a delivery record, taps from the phones count once, and the BST/GMT clock changes. It also checks that edits save or say why (100 rapid edits included), that saves from Calendar merge with changes made elsewhere, and that a mission re-plan keeps quests changed by hand.</p>\n<p><code>npx tsx test/scheduler.test.ts</code> checks the Quest planner (sleep, deadlines, priorities, dependencies, travel, buffers, breaks, the daily cap, blocked time and at-risk flags), and <code>npx tsx test/planner.test.ts</code> checks mission plans (series written out with exact spacing, quests months ahead, one-day windows not being crowded out, and days off). <code>npm run typecheck</code> checks the types, and <code>npm run healthcheck</code> is a read-only check against the real Acuity pages. The worker side of the job queue is covered by Nova Bot&#39;s tests (<code>test/agent-nova.spec.js</code>).</p>\n<p>To try each Acuity action by hand, make a test booking in Acuity under a made-up name with your own email, then run (with <code>DRY_RUN=true</code> first to rehearse):</p>\n<pre><code>npm run edit -- date=2026-10-31 time=17:00 &quot;name=Dana Hollis&quot; phone=07700900789 &quot;notes=Test note from Nova Agent&quot;\nnpm run edit -- date=2026-10-31 time=17:00 &quot;name=Dana Hollis&quot; newdate=2026-11-04 newtime=14:00\nnpm run book -- &quot;type=Voiceover Recording with Engineer - 1 hour&quot; date=2026-11-05 time=15:00 first=Agent last=Test email=you@example.com\nnpm run cancel -- date=2026-11-05 time=15:00 &quot;name=Agent Test&quot;\nnpm run cancel -- date=2026-11-04 time=14:00 &quot;name=Dana Hollis&quot;</code></pre>\n<p>Each one ends with ✓ or ✗. The visualizer&#39;s <strong>Read-only tour</strong> shows the AI element finder at work: the first run heals each element and saves it, the second comes straight from memory.</p>","text":"npm test runs the Quest reminders on a simulated clock (Vitest fake timers, a pretend Nova Bot worker and a throwaway data folder: test/harness.ts ): a reminder every 30 minutes for 4 hours pings exactly 8 times, a ping the worker turns away is retried, Nova Agent being off across a session gives one late \"Missed\" ping, no session is moved past without a delivery record, taps from the phones count once, and the BST/GMT clock changes. It also checks that edits save or say why (100 rapid edits included), that saves from Calendar merge with changes made elsewhere, and that a mission re-plan keeps quests changed by hand. npx tsx test/scheduler.test.ts checks the Quest planner (sleep, deadlines, priorities, dependencies, travel, buffers, breaks, the daily cap, blocked time and at-risk flags), and npx tsx test/planner.test.ts checks mission plans (series written out with exact spacing, quests months ahead, one-day windows not being crowded out, and days off). npm run typecheck checks the types, and npm run healthcheck is a read-only check against the real Acuity pages. The worker side of the job queue is covered by Nova Bot's tests ( test/agent-nova.spec.js ). To try each Acuity action by hand, make a test booking in Acuity under a made-up name with your own email, then run (with DRY_RUN=true first to rehearse): npm run edit -- date=2026-10-31 time=17:00 \"name=Dana Hollis\" phone=07700900789 \"notes=Test note from Nova Agent\" npm run edit -- date=2026-10-31 time=17:00 \"name=Dana Hollis\" newdate=2026-11-04 newtime=14:00 npm run book -- \"type=Voiceover Recording with Engineer - 1 hour\" date=2026-11-05 time=15:00 first=Agent last=Test email=you@example.com npm run cancel -- date=2026-11-05 time=15:00 \"name=Agent Test\" npm run cancel -- date=2026-11-04 time=14:00 \"name=Dana Hollis\" Each one ends with ✓ or ✗. The visualizer's Read-only tour shows the AI element finder at work: the first run heals each element and saves it, the second comes straight from memory."},{"id":"project-layout-4","title":"Project layout","html":"<pre><code>src/visualizer/server.ts  Nova Agent&#39;s server: the pages, the plan&#39;s API, the suite apps, reminders\nsrc/visualizer/chat.html  the main page: Nova Agent rail, Agent, Today, Missions, Calendar\nsrc/visualizer/page.html  the visualizer\nsrc/visualizer/app/       the installable app: manifest, service worker, icons, sfx.js (sound effects)\nsrc/visualizer/calendar-sync.js  makes Calendar save to Nova Agent\nsrc/chat.ts               Agent: Claude with quest, calendar, Acuity (read-only), web and status tools\nsrc/web.ts                web research and seeing webpages (public pages only, in a browser of its own)\nsrc/memory.ts             Index: what the suite remembers, read before replies, learned after\nsrc/config.ts             every setting, read once from .env\nsrc/quests/store.ts       Missions, Quests, blocked time and your rhythm (quests.json)\nsrc/quests/scheduler.ts   the planner: places every quest at a time, to the second (no AI)\nsrc/quests/lengths.ts     lengths from a second to forever: sessions, repeats, plain words\nsrc/quests/pulses.ts      repeats faster than every 5 minutes, each on its own timer\nsrc/quests/planner.ts     turning a goal into a Mission and its Quests (Claude)\nsrc/quests/plan.ts        re-planning, and mirroring quests into Calendar\nsrc/quests/reminders.ts   reminders, check-ins, the morning plan and evening wrap-up\nsrc/quests/deliveries.ts  every phone ping: sent once, checked, retried, logged (data/nova.db)\nsrc/quests/portalsync.ts     the plan to the phones (Portal), and their taps back\nsrc/quests/actions.ts     everything Agent and the page can do with them\nsrc/calendar/store.ts     Calendar&#39;s data (calendar.json, with a revision per save)\nsrc/calendar/page.ts      saves from the calendar page, merged with changes made elsewhere\nsrc/index.ts              command-line entry point for the Acuity helper\nsrc/browser.ts            Chromium, the saved session and the change-blocking safety layer\nsrc/tasks.ts              the tasks (check login, list, search, book, cancel, edit)\nsrc/jobs.ts               collecting jobs from Nova Bot&#39;s worker and reporting results\nsrc/healthcheck.ts        the daily read-only healthcheck\nsrc/alerts.ts             alerts to the console, alerts.log and staff phones\nsrc/llm.ts                the Claude client (JSON answers, with web research for mission plans)\nsrc/heal/                 resolve() and the selector memory\nsrc/acuity/               Acuity pages: login, list, book, cancel, edit, targets, types\nsrc/trace.ts              every step, for the console, logs and visualizer\ntest/harness.ts           the simulated clock for `npm test`\ntest/*.spec.ts            reminders, deliveries, taps from the phones, clock changes\ntest/scheduler.test.ts    planner checks\ntest/planner.test.ts      mission plans: series written out, quests far ahead\ntest/web.test.ts          research only cites pages it read; public webpages only\nweb/agent/                Nova Agent&#39;s own page (chat.html), the visualizer and the installable app\nweb/portal/               the Portal panel (Portal is part of it; old-app-address/ is what\n                          phones that installed Portal from its old address, /app/ still use)\nweb/calendar/ web/notes/ web/index/ web/observatory/ web/lossless/   the other panels\nweb/shared/               themes, sounds, the badge and the Manual (manual-data.js: npm run manual)\nsrc/signin.ts             signing in to Nova Bot as a person, for Portal on the PC\nscripts/                  the manual builder; scripts/observatory/ scans and captures your projects\ndocs/apps/&lt;panel&gt;/        each panel&#39;s guide and pictures\ndeploy/agent-nova.service systemd user service\ndocs/acuity-ui-notes.md   what Acuity&#39;s real admin pages look like\ndocs/media/               README images</code></pre>","text":"src/visualizer/server.ts Nova Agent's server: the pages, the plan's API, the suite apps, reminders src/visualizer/chat.html the main page: Nova Agent rail, Agent, Today, Missions, Calendar src/visualizer/page.html the visualizer src/visualizer/app/ the installable app: manifest, service worker, icons, sfx.js (sound effects) src/visualizer/calendar-sync.js makes Calendar save to Nova Agent src/chat.ts Agent: Claude with quest, calendar, Acuity (read-only), web and status tools src/web.ts web research and seeing webpages (public pages only, in a browser of its own) src/memory.ts Index: what the suite remembers, read before replies, learned after src/config.ts every setting, read once from .env src/quests/store.ts Missions, Quests, blocked time and your rhythm (quests.json) src/quests/scheduler.ts the planner: places every quest at a time, to the second (no AI) src/quests/lengths.ts lengths from a second to forever: sessions, repeats, plain words src/quests/pulses.ts repeats faster than every 5 minutes, each on its own timer src/quests/planner.ts turning a goal into a Mission and its Quests (Claude) src/quests/plan.ts re-planning, and mirroring quests into Calendar src/quests/reminders.ts reminders, check-ins, the morning plan and evening wrap-up src/quests/deliveries.ts every phone ping: sent once, checked, retried, logged (data/nova.db) src/quests/portalsync.ts the plan to the phones (Portal), and their taps back src/quests/actions.ts everything Agent and the page can do with them src/calendar/store.ts Calendar's data (calendar.json, with a revision per save) src/calendar/page.ts saves from the calendar page, merged with changes made elsewhere src/index.ts command-line entry point for the Acuity helper src/browser.ts Chromium, the saved session and the change-blocking safety layer src/tasks.ts the tasks (check login, list, search, book, cancel, edit) src/jobs.ts collecting jobs from Nova Bot's worker and reporting results src/healthcheck.ts the daily read-only healthcheck src/alerts.ts alerts to the console, alerts.log and staff phones src/llm.ts the Claude client (JSON answers, with web research for mission plans) src/heal/ resolve() and the selector memory src/acuity/ Acuity pages: login, list, book, cancel, edit, targets, types src/trace.ts every step, for the console, logs and visualizer test/harness.ts the simulated clock for `npm test` test/*.spec.ts reminders, deliveries, taps from the phones, clock changes test/scheduler.test.ts planner checks test/planner.test.ts mission plans: series written out, quests far ahead test/web.test.ts research only cites pages it read; public webpages only web/agent/ Nova Agent's own page (chat.html), the visualizer and the installable app web/portal/ the Portal panel (Portal is part of it; old-app-address/ is what phones that installed Portal from its old address, /app/ still use) web/calendar/ web/notes/ web/index/ web/observatory/ web/lossless/ the other panels web/shared/ themes, sounds, the badge and the Manual (manual-data.js: npm run manual) src/signin.ts signing in to Nova Bot as a person, for Portal on the PC scripts/ the manual builder; scripts/observatory/ scans and captures your projects docs/apps/<panel>/ each panel's guide and pictures deploy/agent-nova.service systemd user service docs/acuity-ui-notes.md what Acuity's real admin pages look like docs/media/ README images"}],"news":[],"history":{"total":112,"first":"2026-10-06T15:47:46+01:00","commits":[{"hash":"ae32409","date":"2026-10-10T01:26:38+01:00","subject":"Observatory: more on screen, in Nova Agent's glass; Agent: \"Give me a goal\" sits last, by the box","body":"Observatory: the title, the six numbers and the links share one slim header (the colours and\nthe languages the next line), the search, filters and sort stay at the top as one row, and the\ndecks are tighter with a glowing glass edge, so a full row of decks shows straight away. Short\nwindows drop the summary line and the goal (both in each deck's details); phones get one small\nblock above the projects, with the numbers sliding sideways. Nothing removed.\nAgent's welcome: the suggestions, Today in music, then the hello (\"Give me a goal…\") at the\nbottom, next to where you type."},{"hash":"1cfd0a1","date":"2026-10-10T01:15:46+01:00","subject":"Undo: the Manual keeps \"Nova Agent\" (the rename to \"Agent\" isn't wanted)","body":"This reverts commit 6d0274f."},{"hash":"6d0274f","date":"2026-10-10T01:15:21+01:00","subject":"Manual: the app is \"Agent\" (Nova Agent's own page and the Manual's header keep \"Nova Agent\")","body":"Renamed when the Manual is built, so the READMEs on GitHub keep their words."},{"hash":"ec262d1","date":"2026-10-10T01:11:19+01:00","subject":"Manual: every panel's description is back (not the \"A Nova Agent panel\" note); no badge scraps","body":"The description is the first bold line under the title, skipping the note above it that says\nwhere the panel lives. GitHub badges are left out of the manual's intros."},{"hash":"5de742c","date":"2026-10-09T21:42:53+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent: \"Chat\" is now \"Agent\" everywhere you see it","body":"The section title, the panels bar, the phone menu, the status line, the hints, the\ninstall description, Portal's and Calendar's mentions and the manual. Nova Bot's website\nchats (Portal's Chats tab, Index's customer facts) keep their name. Code names stay."},{"hash":"2644a3e","date":"2026-10-09T17:18:58+01:00","subject":"Chat's content panels: no corner brackets","body":""},{"hash":"bd2a993","date":"2026-10-09T17:14:00+01:00","subject":"Status line: Auto, Always shown or Always hidden, and each part optional; Calendar: fits, spacing, colour, centring (follows Centre all text)","body":""},{"hash":"5c20c51","date":"2026-10-09T17:05:04+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent reopens the app you had open (and where you were in it) after a refresh or next time","body":""},{"hash":"9a359b8","date":"2026-10-09T16:50:53+01:00","subject":"Missions and Quests stay inside their own columns","body":""},{"hash":"d1c9203","date":"2026-10-09T16:49:35+01:00","subject":"Missions: one message, not two, when signed out","body":""},{"hash":"bab699e","date":"2026-10-09T16:48:40+01:00","subject":"Today in music: a card's list opens inside the panel (‹ Back), never floating over anything; Missions says so when empty","body":""},{"hash":"9ac5375","date":"2026-10-09T16:42:55+01:00","subject":"Today in music: exact covers through Nova Bot, live updates (charts every 30 minutes, new picks each day)","body":""},{"hash":"ad65166","date":"2026-10-09T16:39:25+01:00","subject":"Today in music: pictures that match the words (the exact gear photographed, a cover per genre named, a record shop for the industry); no Hey I'm Nova Agent heading","body":""},{"hash":"9215e27","date":"2026-10-09T16:36:41+01:00","subject":"Missions and Quests: a minimum height, and the title and buttons stack when narrow","body":""},{"hash":"d012746","date":"2026-10-09T16:34:10+01:00","subject":"Top 10 card: the #1's cover through Nova Bot, no drawing while it loads","body":""},{"hash":"715c638","date":"2026-10-09T16:33:57+01:00","subject":"Music cards: photos only for gear and the industry, no drawings","body":""},{"hash":"ab6d6b2","date":"2026-10-09T11:48:04+01:00","subject":"Missions and Quests never show over an open app","body":""},{"hash":"d8996fd","date":"2026-10-09T11:45:11+01:00","subject":"Music cards: album-cover-like photos for gear and the industry, and one finish for every picture","body":""},{"hash":"e50667d","date":"2026-10-09T11:43:24+01:00","subject":"Missions and Quests scroll inside once they're full, instead of running off the screen","body":""},{"hash":"1eebefe","date":"2026-10-09T11:40:48+01:00","subject":"Music cards: real photos for gear and the industry, matching the album art","body":""},{"hash":"be20d75","date":"2026-10-09T11:38:54+01:00","subject":"Music cards: drawn pictures for gear (by kind), the industry and the charts, matching the album art; pictures lined up","body":""},{"hash":"aad9afb","date":"2026-10-09T11:37:00+01:00","subject":"One centre line: equal side columns, the brand panel as wide as Chat; its small word is just Novacane","body":""},{"hash":"cef50cd","date":"2026-10-09T11:11:26+01:00","subject":"Front page: the biggest size that fits, searched (text rewraps)","body":""},{"hash":"1dd96ae","date":"2026-10-09T11:09:21+01:00","subject":"Front page: fit again once fonts and pictures are in","body":""},{"hash":"a76ec7f","date":"2026-10-09T11:08:33+01:00","subject":"The front page fills the Chat panel: bigger when there's room, smaller when not","body":""},{"hash":"99fa6d3","date":"2026-10-09T11:04:08+01:00","subject":"The front page and its cards centred top to bottom","body":""},{"hash":"c1be90e","date":"2026-10-09T10:54:31+01:00","subject":"Phones and tablets detected from the device; made for fingers and kept light; swipe to turn the conversation's pages","body":""},{"hash":"137b27e","date":"2026-10-09T10:48:37+01:00","subject":"The chat column's title is Chat","body":""},{"hash":"aecb8e9","date":"2026-10-09T05:03:52+01:00","subject":"The conversation in pages (← → or Space, ‹ ›, or All), and it scrolls again","body":"Fixes: a hidden welcome stopped the conversation scrolling, and a later style kept the welcome\nshowing after the chat began. Each question with its reply is a page; long pages scroll."},{"hash":"a1cd151","date":"2026-10-09T04:44:11+01:00","subject":"Quote of the day: no picture when there's no photo","body":""},{"hash":"0b620e1","date":"2026-10-09T04:43:15+01:00","subject":"Quests' date centred; bigger pictures where there's room","body":""},{"hash":"cc55e78","date":"2026-10-09T04:40:39+01:00","subject":"A theme picked in any app applies everywhere; pictures above their words; centred status line on phones","body":""},{"hash":"97c82d8","date":"2026-10-09T04:37:25+01:00","subject":"Content panels: no star on the top edge","body":""},{"hash":"c35f716","date":"2026-10-09T04:34:12+01:00","subject":"Front page fits without scrolling; richer content panel borders; song of the day as a card","body":"Ideas beyond the first four wait behind More ideas. The welcome is measured and drawn a little\nsmaller when it needs to be (never below 65%; only a very small window can still scroll). The\ncontent panels get a glowing gradient edge, lit corner brackets, a star in the top edge and a\nsoft nebula inside. The song of the day is a card (its art, and a tap shows what it's about and\nthe lyrics link)."},{"hash":"6ac7842","date":"2026-10-09T04:25:34+01:00","subject":"Welcome in content panels; pictures on the music cards; quotes change every 2 to 16 minutes","body":"The welcome's areas are bordered content panels (the hello, the suggestions, Today in music), all\ncentred, with nothing cut short (lines wrap). Pictures: album art for the #1, genres and the song\nof the day (Apple's music search via Nova Bot), photos for gear and musicians (Wikipedia). The\nquote changes by itself at a random 2 to 16 minutes, fading, never the same twice running."},{"hash":"8a73566","date":"2026-10-09T04:13:56+01:00","subject":"Today in music on the front page: Top 10 worldwide, genres, budget gear, the industry's money, a quote and a song of the day","body":""},{"hash":"32e3268","date":"2026-10-09T03:28:20+01:00","subject":"Panels make room for the bars, Missions and Quests size to their contents, centred everywhere, Portal in the middle of the Apps","body":"While the panels bar or the top bar is in view over an open panel, the panel moves out of its way\n(margins, eased) instead of being covered; phones too. Missions and Quests are as tall (and, within\nlimits, as wide) as what's in them, growing to full height then scrolling. The columns' titles stay\ncentred at every size, and rows that fit (suggestions, chips, tabs) sit in the middle. Portal is in\nthe middle of the Apps: Chat, Calendar, Portal, Notes, Index."},{"hash":"9f9f863","date":"2026-10-09T03:23:17+01:00","subject":"A quiet sky: no glow spots or glow under the panels, softer nebula, fainter stars","body":""},{"hash":"b9eb764","date":"2026-10-09T03:19:20+01:00","subject":"Every window size usable; the lower part of the window brings up the bar; Notes stays on screen","body":"Phone layout only below 481px tall (short computer windows keep the computer layout, tighter).\nNarrower computer windows: slimmer columns, a shorter New button, smaller tool buttons. Short\nones: slimmer header, one swipeable row of suggestions, smaller bars. Tablets: the bar in one\ncentred row. The column titles' grid applies on computers only (phones keep their own header).\nThe bottom 14% of the window brings the bar up. Notes inside Nova Agent: its toolbar wraps, the\npage starts as tall as the window, the outline's lines end with an ellipsis."},{"hash":"154133c","date":"2026-10-09T03:08:06+01:00","subject":"Smaller bar, clearer status line, distinct settings icons, compact Quests, glowing scrollbars with sounds, a shifting cosmic sky, centred titles and chat","body":""},{"hash":"1d9cff9","date":"2026-10-09T02:54:25+01:00","subject":"No glass bubbles, one glow everywhere, bars fit their contents, centred text","body":"The panels bar's tiles sit right on the night sky (a glow behind the one you point at, a line of\nlight under the open one, glowing lines between groups). glow.css: the same edge and nebula light\non the header, columns, panel frame, pop-ups and status line, and the same glow on buttons, tabs\nand boxes, in the panels too. On computers the three bars are as wide as their contents. All text\nis centred (a switch in the Panels window turns it off); Notes documents and code keep their own."},{"hash":"a8c65b8","date":"2026-10-09T02:45:30+01:00","subject":"Glowing space-scene icons, a night-sky panels bar, springy show and hide, a still status line","body":"Icons: illustrated scenes on small Novacane nebulae, in each panel's colour mixed with the\ntheme. The bar: nebula light, faint stars, the sigil watermark, a glowing edge, shimmering\ngroup names, glass tiles. Show and hide: a quick spring in, a quick exit, tiles popping in one\nafter another. The status line: no Panels button (the gear opens the Panels window on computers\ntoo) and the news in a few still words."},{"hash":"263cf4f","date":"2026-10-09T02:31:27+01:00","subject":"Cosmic icons, one theme for everything, planet colours, smart top bar, status line","body":"Icons: a cosmic set, each with its own colour (mixed with the theme), sky and shape; Talk to\nNova Agent, Quests and Missions have their own. look.js: one theme for every panel (or each its\nown), and colour everything from your planet. Typing hides the panels bar. The top bar: Auto,\nAlways shown or Always hidden. The status line under the bar: Panels button (the top one is\ngone), version and build, what changed lately for the part of the bar you point at, on and off\ntimes, recent activity and a 12-hour clock. Lossless audio's sounds come along."},{"hash":"d815e8c","date":"2026-10-09T02:04:58+01:00","subject":"Calmer sounds, a bar that follows what you do, themed panel icons","body":"Sounds: quieter, warmer and slower to swell, at most three notes, small sounds kept apart;\nthe quiet extras start off. The bar: on a computer it follows the mouse (near the bottom: in\nview; working higher up: away); on a phone deliberate scrolling (down a good way: away; up a\nlittle or the handle: back), never timers; ignores the page moving by itself and short pages.\nIcons: one line-art set, each panel in its own colour mixed with the theme's accent."},{"hash":"a42ee32","date":"2026-10-09T01:51:32+01:00","subject":"The panels bar shows and hides itself (Auto), or always shown, or always hidden","body":"Auto: there on the home; with a panel open it stays a moment then slides away; back with the\nmouse at the bottom edge, scrolling up, or the phone's handle. The choice is in the Panels\nwindow and the phone's gear, remembered on the device. Only transform and opacity move."},{"hash":"d844c0b","date":"2026-10-09T01:47:50+01:00","subject":"Every panel sounds like itself; never the same twice; music that wanders","body":"Themes: Notes paper and pencil, Calendar ticks and chimes, Portal deep and roomy, Index echoing\ndroplets, Observatory the night sky, Lossless soft electric piano, Visualizer glass glints,\nQuests kalimba, Missions a low swell. Buttons that open a panel sound like it. New kinds:\ntick boxes, menus, lists, links. Each play picks another note and voicing with tiny pitch\ndifferences; rapid sounds soften themselves. Fixes a fade-in clash that could silence a sound.\nMusic: chords wander (recent ones less likely), moods change every few minutes, piano phrases\nare made up fresh. Lossless audio now has the shared sounds too."},{"hash":"c228593","date":"2026-10-09T01:24:38+01:00","subject":"Calmer, lusher sounds, and quiet extras with their own switch","body":"Every sound is quieter with a warm top end and more space. New, barely-there extras:\nscrolling, typing, sliders, dragging (Calendar's note cards: pick up, each step, put down)\nand hovering, each kept to its own pace. Their own switch in Portal's Options and the\nphone's gear; only heard while sound effects are on."},{"hash":"8ff866a","date":"2026-10-09T01:18:58+01:00","subject":"One panels bar everywhere (no Panels box), softer ambient sounds, light motion","body":"The panels strip loses its Panels box and keeps the same groups and tiles whatever is open;\nwith a panel open it only gets smaller. Sounds swell in and chords bloom together instead of\nrunning up; taps are a low felt touch. Buttons and tiles press in softly, the open panel's\ntile breathes, panels fade in (scale and opacity only; off for reduced motion or calm)."},{"hash":"48b4b4c","date":"2026-10-09T00:58:39+01:00","subject":"Lush Novacane sounds, and quiet ambient music across all of Nova Agent","body":"Sound effects: glass bells, warm under-tones and breaths of air, in the music's key, with\nstereo, reverb and echo; a hello chime when sounds are switched on. Every old sound kept.\nAmbient music moves to shared/ and becomes one player for the whole app (header switch,\nphone gear → Music, Portal's button), remembered on the device, with a soft electric-piano\nphrase now and then."},{"hash":"e777051","date":"2026-10-08T23:36:18+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'shared-notes' into grouped-bar","body":""},{"hash":"4458493","date":"2026-10-08T23:36:18+01:00","subject":"Panels in four groups everywhere, and the Novacane sigil as Nova Agent's icon","body":"Apps (Chat, Portal, Calendar, Notes, Index) · Tasks (Quests, Missions) ·\nTools (Lossless, Visualizer) · Helpers (Observatory, Manual), all in view at\nonce on phones (labelled bar) and computers (strip and launcher). Quests,\nMissions and the Manual open in place. The app icon, tab icon and header\nmark are the Novacane sigil."},{"hash":"8f8db84","date":"2026-10-08T23:34:26+01:00","subject":"Notes: Shared and Local notes","body":"Shared notes are the team's: kept by Nova Bot (/notes-api/), seen and edited by\neveryone signed in with Portal on every device, synced every 15 s and on focus,\nreadable offline with changes queued until the connection is back. Local notes\nstay on this device, as before. One tap by \"Saved\" moves a note between the two\n(with Undo); All · Shared · Local above the list, a badge on each note. Two\npeople changing a shared note at once keeps both (\"… (conflicted copy)\").\nOn the studio PC, Nova Agent passes /notes-api/ on with its sign-in.\nEvery existing Notes feature stays."},{"hash":"29e6d5e","date":"2026-10-08T17:45:50+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'main' into calendar-pro","body":""},{"hash":"27a756e","date":"2026-10-08T17:45:50+01:00","subject":"WIP calendar-pro","body":""},{"hash":"a70307d","date":"2026-10-08T17:44:17+01:00","subject":"Admin lives in Portal: no Admin button in Nova Agent","body":"Portal gets an Admin section for admins (Studio pages, Crew, Google, Links),\nshown inside Portal. Nova Agent's bar and launcher lose Admin and All links;\ninviting from the crew page is hidden."},{"hash":"eec91d2","date":"2026-10-08T17:32:09+01:00","subject":"Phones: every place on the bar at once (two rows), no sideways scrolling","body":"The bar is a grid: half the places per row upright (12 → two rows of 6),\none row on its side; each column fits its longest word. The edge fades and\nscroll-into-view are gone. Toasts sit above the taller bar."},{"hash":"f4a2edc","date":"2026-10-08T17:18:51+01:00","subject":"Phones: one bar along the bottom, always there, every place on it","body":"- Nova Agent's bar stays on every panel (the panel sits between the header\n  and the bar), and shows every place directly: Chat, Portal, Calendar,\n  Notes, Quests, Missions, Index, Observatory, Lossless, Admin, Visualizer,\n  Manual. Swipe it for the rest; its edges fade where it goes on, and the\n  open one scrolls into view. No More button.\n- The same header on every panel; settings (reload the panel, rhythm, new\n  mission, sound, all links, refresh) behind a gear in it.\n- The last three panels stay loaded, so going back to one is instant and\n  it's where you left it; a panel fades in when ready (no white flash).\n- Inside Nova Agent on a phone or small tablet, Portal's and Index's\n  sections are a row under their header, never a second bar at the bottom."},{"hash":"04715a2","date":"2026-10-08T17:00:55+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'mobile-panels' into mobile-shell","body":""},{"hash":"e884855","date":"2026-10-08T17:00:33+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent on phones: a bar along the bottom, one screen at a time, sized to what's visible","body":"- A bar along the bottom (Chat · Portal · Calendar · Notes · More); More is a\n  sheet with everything else (Quests, Missions, Index, Observatory, Lossless,\n  Admin, Visualizer, links, Manual, rhythm, sound, install).\n- The home shows one thing at a time (Chat, Quests or Missions) instead of\n  one long scroll; suggestions are a row you swipe; the message box sits at\n  the bottom; the floating Manual button moves into More.\n- Sized to the visible screen (visual viewport), so the keyboard never hides\n  the message box; safe areas for the notch and home bar; slimmer on its side.\n- A panel opens full screen and the bar steps aside (Portal has its own tabs);\n  its name switches panels (More), and the phone's back button closes it.\n  Switching panels no longer piles up back steps.\n- The status says its word (Live, Rehearsal, PC off, Signed out) in colour.\n- Lighter: no frosted glass, drifting c"},{"hash":"932c20c","date":"2026-10-08T16:59:59+01:00","subject":"Panels on phones: fit, lighter, less scrolling","body":"- Notes: one top bar (notes list, the note's name, Google Docs) and the menus;\n  the toolbar is one row you swipe, with the everyday tools (the rest stay in\n  the menus); 16px fields; no glass blur, grain or drifting background.\n- Observatory: a slim title, the numbers as a compact strip, each project as\n  one short row with a small drawn cover (no full-size screenshots on phones);\n  category chips in one row; no star map, no moving sky, no blur.\n- Calendar and Index: no glass blur or endless decorative motion on phones.\n- Lossless audio: snug margins, big buttons, 16px fields.\n- Visualizer: no error when the studio PC is off; fits a phone."},{"hash":"3fbe6c1","date":"2026-10-08T15:30:34+01:00","subject":"Portal on phones: a Today screen, five tabs, full-screen inside Nova Agent, lighter","body":"- Inside Nova Agent on a phone, an open panel gets the whole screen (Nova\n  Agent's header, the panels strip and the floating Manual step aside; the\n  slim bar keeps ← Nova Agent, and the panel's name switches panels), with\n  room for the notch and the home bar.\n- Portal opens on Today: new enquiries, today's chats and bookings, alerts\n  and quests at a glance (each tile opens its section), then the newest\n  enquiries.\n- Phones: five tabs (Today, Enquiries, Chats, Calendar, More); Quests,\n  Alerts, NovaBot and You are under More with their counts. Enquiries fold\n  to one line until tapped; compact alerts and chats; small headings on one\n  line; a smaller planet on You; inputs at 16px (no zoom on typing).\n- Lighter: no frosted glass or moving titles on phones; the ambient music\n  engine loads after the first screen; the Manual (and its 287 KB of\n  content) loads only outside frames, and p"},{"hash":"ed420d6","date":"2026-10-08T13:33:52+01:00","subject":"Portal is the one sign-in","body":"Signed out, the planet opens Portal's sign-in (in Nova Agent's viewer): no\nsign-in form of its own, and no Sign in with Google anywhere. Google is a\nconnection, not a way in: Portal's You page shows it (connected as whom), with\nSet up / Connect Google for admins (Admin → Google). Notes asks\n/auth/google-status for the studio's Google key."},{"hash":"3f9e2df","date":"2026-10-08T13:28:18+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'google' into relay","body":""},{"hash":"d529416","date":"2026-10-08T13:27:09+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent online reaches the studio PC; one address","body":"- src/relay.ts: the PC dials out to Nova Bot (/nova-agent/link, a WebSocket\n  with AGENT_NOVA_KEY) and answers signed-in staff members' requests for\n  Nova Agent's own addresses (chat, Missions, Quests, Calendar's data, files\n  it wrote, the Visualizer's feeds for admins), streamed both ways. Relayed\n  requests never count as from this computer's own page. Reconnects by itself.\n- Online, chat.html says calmly when the PC is off (chat paused, a note on\n  Missions and Quests, the pill says PC off) and comes back by itself.\n- Calendar online uses Nova Agent's calendar; what a browser had before is\n  kept aside once (nova-calendar/before-nova-agent).\n- The PC's own pages open Nova Agent online, so /agent/ online is the one\n  address; NOVA_LOCAL_UI=1 keeps them here (for when the internet is down)."},{"hash":"4fabb4b","date":"2026-10-08T13:26:32+01:00","subject":"Sign in with Google, on the planet and in Portal; Notes uses the studio's Google","body":"- The planet's sign-in card and Portal's sign-in card get a Sign in with\n  Google button once an admin has set Google up (Admin → Google). Google's\n  page opens in a small window (full screen in the installed phone app) and\n  every panel follows when it's done.\n- On the studio PC, Nova Agent starts it (/auth/google): it makes up a\n  verifier, Nova Bot sends back a one-time code to /auth/google/done, and\n  Nova Agent swaps the two for its own sign-in (src/signin.ts).\n- Notes' Save to Google Docs uses the studio's Google key, with nothing to\n  set up; without it, a button opens Admin → Google."},{"hash":"21e7798","date":"2026-10-08T13:15:28+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'main' into relay","body":""},{"hash":"a996289","date":"2026-10-08T13:15:28+01:00","subject":"WIP: Nova Agent's online link (from the earlier attempt)","body":""},{"hash":"3f6f340","date":"2026-10-08T12:00:57+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent: no shortcuts that leave it","body":"The Nova Bot website and Code (GitHub) tiles are gone: /agent/ is the only\naddress, and everything in it stays inside it."},{"hash":"f796db5","date":"2026-10-08T11:47:15+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent lives at /agent/, on the PC and online","body":"/ goes on to /agent/, and /agent/<panel> opens Nova Agent with that panel.\nPanels opened on their own, notifications and the app's shortcuts open\n/agent/?open=<panel>. The installed app starts at /agent/."},{"hash":"00484d5","date":"2026-10-08T11:38:21+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent is the one app: panels open only inside it","body":"- A panel opened on its own (/portal/, /calendar/, /notes/, /app/memory/,\n  /observatory/, /lossless/, /visualizer, /admin...) opens Nova Agent with\n  that panel instead: /?open=<its address>, keeping its query and #hash.\n  The server tells by Sec-Fetch-Dest; inside.js (and Calendar's embed.js)\n  catch browsers that don't say.\n- Nova Agent reads ?open= and opens the panel; a tapped notification opens\n  its panel too (nova-open from the service worker).\n- No more \"Inside / Window\" switch or open-in-a-window button. Visualizer\n  and Admin are panels; Admin is passed on to Nova Bot with this computer's\n  sign-in (Portal first when signed out).\n- One installable app: /sw.js handles phone notifications for the whole\n  app (Portal subscribes through it, keeping an old /app/ or /portal/\n  address if the phone has one, so nothing arrives twice); the old service\n  workers open taps in Nova Agent."},{"hash":"3b87ce8","date":"2026-10-08T02:16:18+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'portal-merge' into sign-in","body":""},{"hash":"0f31499","date":"2026-10-08T02:16:18+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'live-fixes' into sign-in","body":""},{"hash":"d926227","date":"2026-10-08T02:16:18+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'panels-fit' into sign-in","body":""},{"hash":"37073d2","date":"2026-10-08T02:15:25+01:00","subject":"One Portal: one staff app at /portal/","body":"Portal is gone as a separate panel. Portal is the one staff app: one header,\none tab bar with Portal's work tabs (Enquiries, Chats, Calendar, Quests,\nAlerts, NovaBot) plus You (your planet and profile; admins reach the crew\nand the admin pages from there). Portal's sign-in, setup and invite cards\nreplace Portal's old sign-in screen.\n- web/portal's scripts and styles move into web/portal (app.js, app.css,\n  ambient.js, options.js, suite.js). portal.js runs the page (who's signed\n  in, the address, the You tab) and starts the work tabs (window.NovaHub);\n  the tabs hand sign-outs back (window.PortalPage). Tabs follow the\n  address: /portal/?view=enquiries|chats|calendar|quests|alerts|bot|me|crew,\n  #nova opens Alerts, no ?view opens the starting tab from Options (which\n  can now be You). Tells the badge when sign-in changes (NovaPortal.changed).\n- portal.css is scoped to Portal's own parts (.pv) with p"},{"hash":"8ac9531","date":"2026-10-08T02:04:26+01:00","subject":"Lossless audio and Observatory as panels everywhere; docs at the real addresses","body":"- Lossless audio is served by Nova Agent at /lossless/ and opens inside it like\n  the other panels. Signalling and the relay setup come from Nova Bot (which now\n  serves it online too), so the other device can be anywhere; invite links point\n  at the online address. /lossless/ice lets Nova Agent's own page ask.\n- Observatory online asks for a Portal sign-in before showing the projects\n  (Nova Bot keeps them for signed-in staff).\n- Calendar's and Notes' guides link to their addresses on Nova Bot, not the old\n  standalone sites."},{"hash":"53332dc","date":"2026-10-08T02:04:14+01:00","subject":"Panels fit inside Nova Agent's viewer","body":"- While a panel is open, the panels strip shrinks to one row of small\n  switchers (services and admin as icons) and the viewer bar slims down:\n  the panel gets about 80px more height (431 → 511 at 1280×720). Only in\n  the side-by-side layout; stacked on a phone it's unchanged.\n- /shared/inside.js marks <html class=\"embed\"> when a panel is shown in a\n  frame (as Calendar's own embed.js already did), for frame-only fixes.\n- Notes in a frame: a slimmer two-row header (no kicker, smaller mark,\n  icon-only Import/Export/Google Docs below 1500px so the menus aren't\n  cut off), a tighter toolbar, and no word count in short frames. The\n  writing area goes from 215px to 377px tall at 1280×720.\n- Observatory in a frame: a smaller title block. Its stat numbers size to\n  their card (container units), so \"142,408\" no longer breaks in two.\n- Index in a frame: a slimmer tab bar."},{"hash":"a57ed30","date":"2026-10-08T01:58:47+01:00","subject":"Sign in and out from the planet at the top","body":"- The planet shows someone only when they're really signed in on this\n  computer: /auth/me answers 401 without a sign-in, instead of who Nova\n  Agent works for. So the planet and the panels never disagree (before,\n  Portal showed you signed in while Portal asked you to sign in).\n- Signed out, the badge's card has the sign-in form right there; signed in,\n  it has Your profile, Your Index and Sign out. Profile and Index open in\n  Nova Agent's viewer.\n- Signing in or out on any page tells the others (BroadcastChannel); open\n  panels start again so they follow. Portal can call NovaPortal.changed().\n- Nova Bot out of reach: still signed in, shown from the saved sign-in.\n- The old \"Connect as me\" (/auth/link) is gone; Portal's connect was\n  removed from Nova Bot already."},{"hash":"326ecf9","date":"2026-10-08T01:33:59+01:00","subject":"Portal and Index: Portal is the one sign-in","body":"The shared-password box is gone from Portal's and Index's sign-in screens:\nsigned out, there's one button, to Portal, which brings you back to\n/app/ or /app/memory/ (not the old /studio/ and /index/). The guides\nand the Manual say the same."},{"hash":"9e079ef","date":"2026-10-08T00:47:29+01:00","subject":"Notes and Calendar show the current version after an update","body":"Their offline helpers answered from the cache first and refreshed in the\nbackground, so after every change you saw the previous version once (old\nnames, old behaviour). Online they now fetch fresh first and use the cache\nonly when offline. Inside Nova Agent, where nothing needs to work offline,\ntheir helper clears what it kept, unregisters and reloads the page."},{"hash":"100fb09","date":"2026-10-08T00:43:48+01:00","subject":"Plain names: everything is Nova Agent, and its panels are Portal, Portal, Calendar…","body":"Undoes the made-up names. \"Studio\" is Portal again and \"Crew\" is Portal again\n(only where the earlier rename had changed them; real uses of the words are\nkept). Every panel and feature drops \"Nova\": Portal, Portal, Calendar, Notes,\nIndex, Observatory, Missions, Quests and the Manual. \"Nova\" stays for Nova\nAgent itself, Nova Bot and Nova Club.\nThe original addresses are back: Portal at /app/, Portal at /portal/ and\nIndex at /app/memory/ (the panels live in web/portal, web/portal, web/index).\nNova Agent's own icons move to /agent/ to make room. /studio/, /crew/ and\n/index/ redirect, for anything that picked them up yesterday."},{"hash":"0544d88","date":"2026-10-07T23:39:33+01:00","subject":"The Nova Manual is built from Nova Agent's own docs and history","body":"scripts/build-manual.mjs (npm run manual) reads Nova Agent's README and each\npanel's docs/apps/<panel>/README.md, with each panel's git history,\nincluding its history from before it joined Nova Agent (the subtree\nmerge's second parent). It writes one manual, web/shared/manual-data.js;\nthe copy-sharing script is gone. Nova Bot's chapter still comes from its\nown repo next door."},{"hash":"008c7bb","date":"2026-10-07T23:38:25+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent talks to Nova Bot at /nova-agent/*; hubsync is studiosync","body":"Pushes, alerts, jobs, the plan for Studio and \"who am I\" go to Nova Bot's\n/nova-agent/* routes (Nova Bot still answers the old /portal/* too). Deploy\nNova Bot first, then restart Nova Agent. Studio's guide and pictures (from\nNova Bot's README) are in docs/apps/studio."},{"hash":"4b86f1f","date":"2026-10-07T23:33:47+01:00","subject":"Portal is Studio, Nova Portal is Crew, and the suite is Nova Agent","body":"- Renamed everywhere in Nova Agent: the code, its page, the panels, the\n  docs and the chat's instructions. On phones, notifications and the\n  installed app say Nova Agent.\n- Nova Agent's launcher lists its panels (Chat, Studio, Crew, Calendar,\n  Notes, Index, Observatory, Lossless audio), which all open inside it from\n  this computer, and Services and admin (Nova Bot, the Visualizer, Admin,\n  All links, the code).\n- On the studio PC, Studio's sign-in is your own account (the shared studio\n  password field is hidden there).\nChecked in a browser on a test copy: every panel opens inside Nova Agent,\nand signed out, Studio and Crew show their sign-in."},{"hash":"4e9cec4","date":"2026-10-07T23:30:56+01:00","subject":"Studio and Crew work inside Nova Agent on the studio PC","body":"Signing in on the Crew panel signs Nova Agent in to Nova Bot as that person\n(an app token, src/signin.ts). The token stays in data/signin.json (0600)\nand never reaches the browser; Studio's and Crew's requests to Nova Bot's\nstaff API (/app/api, /auth, /staff) are passed on with it, so each person\ngets exactly their own permissions, Index approvals included. Nova Agent\nalso works for whoever signs in. Nova Bot ending the session signs out here.\nOnly Nova Agent's own pages can use it: the request must be for localhost\n(not a look-alike address) and changes must come from Nova Agent's origin.\nThe shared studio password stays a phone thing; on the PC it says to sign\nin on the Crew panel. Studio doesn't sign the PC up for phone pushes."},{"hash":"d3b02ec","date":"2026-10-07T23:29:25+01:00","subject":"One copy of what the panels share; Studio at /studio/, Crew at /crew/, Index at /index/","body":"- web/shared: the themes, sounds, the Portal badge and the Nova Manual,\n  once, instead of a copy in every app (4-5 copies each before). Nova\n  Agent serves it at /shared/ and no longer fetches the themes from Nova\n  Bot.\n- Studio (was Portal) lives at /studio/, Crew (was Nova Portal) at\n  /crew/ and Index (was at /app/memory/) at /index/; every link between\n  them follows. /app/memory/ redirects. The worker API paths (/app/api,\n  /auth, /staff) are unchanged.\n- Calendar's and Notes' offline helpers no longer list the shared files."},{"hash":"fef653e","date":"2026-10-07T23:27:20+01:00","subject":"Panels laid out: Studio (was Portal), Crew (was Nova Portal), Index…","body":"- web/studio: Portal's staff app, now Nova Agent's Studio panel\n- web/crew: Nova Portal's app (sign-in, me, crew, invites), now the Crew\n  panel, with the planet avatar generator beside it\n- web/index, web/calendar, web/notes, web/observatory: the panels\n- Each app's README and pictures move to docs/apps/<panel>\n- The manual and badge scripts move to scripts/, and the Observatory's\n  scanning tools to scripts/observatory (npm run observatory:scan,\n  :capture, :build), writing into web/observatory as before\n- Calendar's and Notes' own deploy configs (their separate workers.dev\n  sites) are dropped: they're panels now\nPaths inside the panels are fixed up next."},{"hash":"fa02889","date":"2026-10-07T23:25:37+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent's page and every panel are served from web/ in this repo","body":"web/agent holds Nova Agent's own page (chat.html, the visualizer, the\ncalendar sync script and the installable app's files). Calendar, Notes,\nIndex, Observatory and the Portal's badge and manual are served from\nweb/<panel> instead of the folders next to Nova Agent."},{"hash":"b5ca368","date":"2026-10-07T22:07:28+01:00","subject":"Nova Missions: a re-plan keeps quests changed by hand (P0-2)","body":"refineMission() deleted every open quest of the mission and made new ones\nfrom Claude's new plan, so anything changed by hand (a pinned time, notes,\na new length) was lost the next time the mission was re-planned.\nQuests now record when they were last changed by hand (`edited`, set by\nupdateQuest: the chat, the page and Nova Calendar). A re-plan keeps those\nas they are and tells Claude to plan around them; the rest are replaced\nas before."},{"hash":"69fec30","date":"2026-10-07T22:06:23+01:00","subject":"Nova Calendar: the revision a page loaded is known even before any save","body":"Just after Nova Agent starts, nothing has been saved yet, so the revision\nthe page loaded wasn't in the in-memory history: its first save was taken\nas coming from an unknown copy (nothing deleted, and the page reloaded).\nThe file's current revision now counts as known.\nChecked in a browser against a test copy: saving from the page needs no\nreload; with Nova Agent stopped, a change is kept, a banner says it isn't\nsaved yet, and it lands by itself once Nova Agent is back."},{"hash":"00f59de","date":"2026-10-07T22:04:16+01:00","subject":"Nova Calendar: a save from the page never wipes out other changes (P0-2)","body":"The calendar page sent the whole calendar on every save and it was written\nstraight over calendar.json, so:\n- a tab left open wiped out what the chat (or another tab) changed since;\n- moving or renaming a quest's card snapped back at the next re-plan;\n- a save while Nova Agent was restarting was dropped (.catch(() => {})),\n  and the next page load replaced it with the server's copy;\n- a damaged calendar.json was read as empty and saved over.\nNow:\n- calendar.json has a revision (`rev`) that goes up with every save, and\n  the last 50 are kept in memory. The page says which revision it loaded\n  (X-Nova-Rev); its changes since then are merged with changes made\n  elsewhere (a card changed in both places: the later change wins; a\n  delete never beats an edit). If that revision isn't known any more, the\n  page's additions and edits are kept, nothing is deleted, and it says so.\n- A quest card mo"},{"hash":"c7d962d","date":"2026-10-07T22:01:19+01:00","subject":"Nova Quests: an edit saves, or says why it didn't (P0-2)","body":"Edits could be lost without a word:\n- cleanQuest() quietly dropped what it couldn't read: a deadline or pinned\n  time written \"2026-10-08 17:00\" or with a zone (\"…Z\") became \"none\",\n  a long title was cut short, an unknown priority became \"normal\", and the\n  chat still said \"Updated\".\n- A damaged quests.json was read as empty, so the next save wiped it.\n- The Nova Agent page swallowed a failed request (Nova Agent restarting).\nNow:\n- updateQuest() checks each change first: unknown fields, unreadable times\n  and values that don't fit are refused with the reason. Common ways of\n  writing a time are understood; times with a zone become UK time.\n- It reads the quest back from the file and refuses to report success if\n  anything didn't stick.\n- A repeat given a new interval counts its next session from the last one\n  at the new spacing, instead of keeping the old next time.\n- quests.json keeps"},{"hash":"ce8db19","date":"2026-10-07T21:47:44+01:00","subject":"Nova Quests across the clock changes (BST/GMT)","body":"Tests for a 30-minute repeat across 25 Oct 2026 (02:00 BST -> 01:00 GMT)\nand 28 Mar 2027 (01:00 GMT -> 02:00 BST), on the simulated clock.\n- Spring: the hour that never happens (01:00, 01:30) comes as one\n  \"Missed\" ping, and the 02:00 session still pings on time: a slot already\n  under way when a repeat moves on is now kept (pinned where it falls)\n  instead of skipped, and a \"Missed\" ping only covers slots that have no\n  ping of their own.\n- Autumn: each wall-clock session pings once, in order. Times are UK wall\n  clock, so the repeated hour (01:00-02:00 GMT) has no pings of its own:\n  a 90-minute real gap once a year. Moving the planner to UTC instants\n  would close it; left for later."},{"hash":"bcceb72","date":"2026-10-07T21:44:47+01:00","subject":"Portal taps count once, for the session they were tapped on","body":"A \"Session done\" tap could be handed to Nova Agent twice (two loops collect\ntaps from the worker, which reads then clears them). The second copy then\ncounted against the session the first had just lined up, skipping it with\nno ping, and near the deadline it ended the whole repeat.\n- Taps can carry a tap id (seen once, remembered in data/nova.db) and the\n  session they were tapped on; a \"done\" for a session that's already moved\n  on changes nothing. Taps without them still work as before.\n- Quest and mission ids: exact match first; a shortened id only finds one\n  if no other id starts the same way, and an empty id finds nothing."},{"hash":"18e45cb","date":"2026-10-07T21:43:50+01:00","subject":"Nova Quests: a repeat never moves past a session whose ping didn't arrive (P0-1)","body":"Repeating reminders could be used up without a ping ever reaching a phone:\nthe push was fire-and-forget (`.catch(() => {})`, status and `phones`\nignored), and replan() moved a repeat past any session that had ended,\nincluding ones that passed while Nova Agent was off or the worker was down.\n- deliveries.ts: every phone ping is kept in data/nova.db (node:sqlite),\n  keyed quest id + session start + kind so it is sent once, and goes\n  scheduled -> sent -> delivered (the worker says phones > 0), or retrying\n  with backoff, or expired once it's past its ttl (said on the page, never\n  silent). Every attempt is logged with its status and error.\n- replan() moves a repeat on only once its session is delivered, given up\n  on visibly, or marked done (acknowledged). A session that went by with no\n  ping at all gets one late \"Missed\" ping; slots jumped over are covered by\n  that same ping, so every s"},{"hash":"3b9eb24","date":"2026-10-07T21:37:36+01:00","subject":"Nova Quests: a simulated-clock test harness, with Vitest","body":"test/harness.ts runs Nova Quests on fake timers (Date, setTimeout and\nsetInterval move together), against a pretend Nova Bot worker that records\nevery /portal/notify, with a fresh data folder per test. `npm test` runs it.\nRegression tests for what works today: a reminder every 30 minutes for 4\nhours pings exactly 8 times, re-planning doesn't ping a session twice, and\npulses beat on their own timer, each replacing the last on the phone."},{"hash":"856c991","date":"2026-10-07T16:29:56+01:00","subject":"Nova Missions plan with web research; Nova Agent sees webpages; the Nova Manual","body":"Missions are full plans now: a written strategy, tracks, dated\nmilestones, series written out per item, assumptions and questions,\nand a Refine tab that re-plans what's left. The page fits one screen.\nWhile it plans, Claude can search the web and read pages (web_search\nand web_fetch); the findings it used are kept on the mission with\ntheir links, and only pages it really read count (checkedFindings).\nIn the chat it can research too, and page_look opens any public page\nin a browser of its own (never the Acuity session) and sees a\nscreenshot and the page's contents. Local and private addresses are\nrefused, for the page and everything it loads (src/web.ts).\nThe Nova Manual (from Nova Portal) is on the chat page and the\nvisualizer, served at /portal/manual.js like the badge."},{"hash":"d630135","date":"2026-10-07T02:01:11+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent finds who it works for by itself","body":"No NOVA_STAFF_ID needed: it uses the studio's first Nova Portal admin, or\nwhoever pressed Connect as me on its badge (data/staff.json). Nova Index\nmemory and the badge both ask src/staff.ts, so they always agree."},{"hash":"ce81fc7","date":"2026-10-07T01:50:10+01:00","subject":"The Nova Portal badge: who Nova Agent works for, on its page and every app it serves","body":""},{"hash":"bfdea8f","date":"2026-10-07T01:10:29+01:00","subject":"NOVA_DATA_DIR: run a second Nova Agent on separate data","body":"A preview or a screenshots copy with sample data can now point at its own\nfolder, so it never touches the real quests, calendar or session."},{"hash":"4a3c64b","date":"2026-10-07T00:23:52+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent reads and feeds Nova Index, and opens it inside","body":"- Before each reply and mission plan, the studio's and this staff member's\n  memory (NOVA_STAFF_ID) is read in; each conversation is handed back to learn\n  from, in the background\n- Nova Index opens inside Nova Agent (served from ns/ni, its data through\n  Nova Agent's own key: studio and staff memory; approvals stay in Portal)\n- The chat knows the suite remembers, and says so"},{"hash":"bda17d5","date":"2026-10-06T23:17:26+01:00","subject":"Nova Notes opens inside Nova Agent in any browser; calendar fits its window","body":"- Nova Agent serves Nova Notes at /notes/ (like Nova Observatory), so the\n  viewer shows it in privacy-minded browsers that block apps inside other\n  apps from saving; its 'own window' button still opens the web app\n- Calendar bump: it fits the Calendar tab and the viewer with no scrolling"},{"hash":"e3d0f39","date":"2026-10-06T23:10:52+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent: open apps inside or in a window, fits on one screen, sound effects","body":"- The Nova suite's apps open inside Nova Agent (a viewer beside the rail) or\n  in their own window, switched in the rail or launcher; apps that refuse to\n  be shown inside others (Portal, admin, GitHub) get a window with a note\n- Today's small tabs (Ahead, Done, Coming up, Pulses, Needs a slot), a\n  one-click new-mission form, a compact welcome and rail: no scrolling at\n  1280 x 720\n- Sound effects on every action (switch in the header), a chime for answers;\n  the visualizer has them too"},{"hash":"e84a156","date":"2026-10-06T22:57:15+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent: the chat in the middle, the Nova suite beside it, Observatory always on","body":"- Wide screens: the Nova suite rail on the left, the chat dead centre, the\n  plan on the right (equal sides); the conversation and prompt sit centred in\n  the chat column; mid widths keep an icon rail; phones are unchanged\n- Nova Observatory is served at /observatory/, so its links always work"},{"hash":"a964c51","date":"2026-10-06T22:49:13+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent: centred, with the Nova suite one tap away; quests and missions stand out","body":"- The header centres Nova Agent, with the live status on the left and a Nova\n  suite launcher on the right (Portal, Notes, Calendar, NovaBot, visualizer,\n  admin, all links and features, Observatory, code)\n- The chat panel keeps each part on its own row, so the message box never\n  covers the messages when the Now strip is hidden\n- Quest cards say Nova Quest (and their mission), missions wear a gold badge,\n  with entrance, shine, a sweeping light on the current quest, and an animated\n  progress ring; repeats no longer show both 'until' and 'due'"},{"hash":"901e044","date":"2026-10-06T21:32:31+01:00","subject":"Links button, Nova Calendar cards in Portal, calendar bump","body":""},{"hash":"51ec32c","date":"2026-10-06T21:11:21+01:00","subject":"Send the Nova Quest plan to Portal, and carry out taps made there","body":"Nova Agent sends its missions, quests and pulses to Nova Bot's worker whenever\nthey change (and every minute); Done, Start, Not now, Skip, Stop, Pause and\nResume tapped in Portal come back with each job check."},{"hash":"f604315","date":"2026-10-06T20:59:26+01:00","subject":"Pulses: repeats faster than every 5 minutes, down to every second","body":"They run on their own exact timers while you're awake, take no slots in the\nplan, ping the page as one ticking card and replace each other on the phone.\nThe chat no longer refuses or bargains over how often things repeat."},{"hash":"9933848","date":"2026-10-06T20:52:09+01:00","subject":"Add a pace limits safety switch to the quest planner","body":"On (the default): quests start a few minutes ahead, on 5-minute marks, with\nbuffers and breaks. Off: right away, to the second, back to back. In the\nrhythm settings and the chat's rhythm_set."},{"hash":"102d942","date":"2026-10-06T20:44:39+01:00","subject":"Quests of any length, Portal alerts, and an installable app","body":"Quests run from a second to forever: placed to the second, long work split into\nsessions, and ongoing quests that repeat daily, weekly or at any interval until\nended or their deadline. Quest, mission and agent alerts go to Portal with\ntheir own labels and buzz; the page pings per kind. Nova Agent is now an\ninstallable app with launcher shortcuts."},{"hash":"8b54800","date":"2026-10-06T19:28:40+01:00","subject":"Add Nova Missions and Nova Quests: goal planning, an hour-by-hour planner, reminders and check-ins","body":"A Mission is a goal that Claude breaks into Quests; a deterministic planner fits\nthem around sleep, calendar entries, blocked time and travel, most urgent first,\nand re-plans on every change. The page gains Today, Missions and Calendar views,\npop-up reminders with a chime, and rhythm settings; the chat gains quest tools."},{"hash":"acad275","date":"2026-10-06T18:31:53+01:00","subject":"Talk to Nova Agent, with Nova Calendar built in","body":"A chat page in the Nova suite style (the new home page; the visualizer\nmoves to /visualizer) where Claude answers as Nova Agent with tools for\nNova Calendar note cards and day cards, read-only Acuity bookings, the\nlogin check and status. Nova Calendar comes in as a git submodule at\ncalendar/, served at /calendar/ and saving to data/calendar.json, so the\nchat and the calendar always agree."},{"hash":"bb02db0","date":"2026-10-06T15:47:46+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent: self-healing browser helper for Acuity's admin pages","body":""}],"work":[{"state":"changed","file":"package.json"},{"state":"changed","file":"scripts/build-manual.mjs"},{"state":"changed","file":"scripts/build-status.mjs"},{"state":"changed","file":"scripts/observatory/capture.mjs"},{"state":"changed","file":"scripts/observatory/projects.config.example.json"},{"state":"changed","file":"src/chat.ts"},{"state":"changed","file":"src/jobs.ts"},{"state":"changed","file":"src/quests/actions.ts"},{"state":"changed","file":"src/quests/deliveries.ts"},{"state":"changed","file":"src/quests/hubsync.ts -> src/quests/portalsync.ts"},{"state":"changed","file":"src/quests/reminders.ts"},{"state":"changed","file":"src/relay.ts"},{"state":"changed","file":"src/signin.ts"},{"state":"changed","file":"src/visualizer/server.ts"},{"state":"changed","file":"test/taps.spec.ts"},{"state":"changed","file":"web/agent/assets/novabot-icon.svg"},{"state":"changed","file":"web/agent/assets/sw.js"},{"state":"changed","file":"web/agent/chat.html"}],"workCount":18,"workStat":"18 files changed, 45 insertions(+), 37 deletions(-)"}},{"id":"portal","name":"Portal","colour":"#9DB4FF","glyph":"◉","where":"A Nova Agent panel; online on the staff phones","links":[["Open Portal","http://localhost:4545/portal/"],["Online","https://novacane-worker.novacane-studio.workers.dev/portal/"]],"repo":"na","shared":"","tagline":"The studio's staff app, one sign-in for the whole of Nova Agent, and a planet for everyone.","intro":"<blockquote><strong>A Nova Agent panel.</strong> Its code is in <code>web/portal/</code> in Nova Agent&#39;s repo, and it opens inside Nova Agent at <code>/portal/</code>. Online, Nova Bot serves it at the same address, and it installs on a phone.</blockquote>\n<p><strong>The studio&#39;s staff app, one sign-in for the whole of Nova Agent, and a planet for everyone.</strong> A panel of <a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-agent\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Nova Agent</a>, for Novacane Studios.</p>\n<p>Portal is where the staff work: enquiries, website chats, bookings, quests, alerts, Ask NovaBot and push notifications to the staff phones. It&#39;s also where you sign in (once, for Portal, Index and the admin pages), and where every member of the team has a profile with a unique planet, drawn from their id.</p>\n<p>Portal&#39;s old address, <code>/app/</code>, opens Portal (with the same tab: <code>/app/?view=alerts</code> is <code>/portal/?view=alerts</code>). Phones that added Portal to the Home Screen keep working and keep getting notifications; adding Portal to the Home Screen gives the new icon.</p>","guide":[{"id":"the-tabs-0","title":"The tabs","html":"<p>Along the bottom on a phone, down the side on a desktop:</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Tab</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Enquiries · Chats · Calendar · Quests · Alerts · NovaBot</strong></td><td>The work tabs. See the work tabs.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>You</strong></td><td>Your planet (it&#39;s the tab&#39;s icon), your profile, your Index, and for admins the crew and the admin pages.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>The address follows the tab, so a reload or a link lands in the same place: <code>/portal/?view=enquiries</code> (or <code>chats</code>, <code>calendar</code>, <code>quests</code>, <code>alerts</code>, <code>bot</code>), <code>/portal/?view=me</code>, <code>/portal/?view=crew</code>, <code>/portal/?id=</code>. With no <code>?view=</code>, Portal opens on the starting tab from Options; a Nova Agent notification (<code>#nova</code>) opens Alerts.</p>\n<p>Sign in with Portal.  Enquiries: email, call, send a booking link, read the chat, mark done.  The smart calendar: the week at a glance, and days that glow as they fill.    A day: how full it is, a clash, a tight changeover, and free slots.  Quests from Nova Agent: what&#39;s on now and today&#39;s plan.  Missions: progress, deadlines and anything at risk.    Alerts: every booking is checked with Acuity itself.  The Nova Agent sheet: every app, one tap away.  🔒 All links, each checked as you open it.    What&#39;s changed and everything the suite can do.  Options: theme, text, motion, sound and the starting tab.  Ask NovaBot in staff mode: a booking link, deposit first.</p>\n<p>Tap a free slot, and NovaBot · bookings opens with the request already written.</p>","text":"Along the bottom on a phone, down the side on a desktop: Tab Enquiries · Chats · Calendar · Quests · Alerts · NovaBot The work tabs. See the work tabs. You Your planet (it's the tab's icon), your profile, your Index, and for admins the crew and the admin pages. The address follows the tab, so a reload or a link lands in the same place: /portal/?view=enquiries (or chats , calendar , quests , alerts , bot ), /portal/?view=me , /portal/?view=crew , /portal/?id= . With no ?view= , Portal opens on the starting tab from Options; a Nova Agent notification ( #nova ) opens Alerts. Sign in with Portal. Enquiries: email, call, send a booking link, read the chat, mark done. The smart calendar: the week at a glance, and days that glow as they fill. A day: how full it is, a clash, a tight changeover, and free slots. Quests from Nova Agent: what's on now and today's plan. Missions: progress, deadlines and anything at risk. Alerts: every booking is checked with Acuity itself. The Nova Agent sheet: every app, one tap away. 🔒 All links, each checked as you open it. What's changed and everything the suite can do. Options: theme, text, motion, sound and the starting tab. Ask NovaBot in staff mode: a booking link, deposit first. Tap a free slot, and NovaBot · bookings opens with the request already written."},{"id":"signing-in-1","title":"Signing in","html":"<ul><li><strong>Sign in once, everywhere:</strong> email and password give you a secure session that Portal, Index and the admin pages all trust. Signing out (from any of them) ends it everywhere at once.</li><li><strong>Setting up:</strong> the very first admin is created with the <code>ADMIN_PASSWORD</code> secret, to prove it&#39;s you. After that, admins <strong>invite</strong> people with a link (valid for 7 days), and each person chooses their own password. Nobody else ever knows it.</li><li><strong>On the studio PC</strong>, signing in here signs Nova Agent in to Nova Bot as you.</li><li><strong>Nova Club and other native apps</strong> can sign in through the same API and get an app token instead of a cookie.</li></ul>","text":"Sign in once, everywhere: email and password give you a secure session that Portal, Index and the admin pages all trust. Signing out (from any of them) ends it everywhere at once. Setting up: the very first admin is created with the ADMIN_PASSWORD secret, to prove it's you. After that, admins invite people with a link (valid for 7 days), and each person chooses their own password. Nobody else ever knows it. On the studio PC , signing in here signs Nova Agent in to Nova Bot as you. Nova Club and other native apps can sign in through the same API and get an app token instead of a cookie."},{"id":"you-and-the-crew-2","title":"You, and the crew","html":"<ul><li><strong>Your profile:</strong> your planet, big and animated, with your name, role and &quot;member since&quot;. You can re-roll your planet (or go back to your original), change your name, open your own Index, and sign out.</li><li><strong>The crew (admins):</strong> everyone as a planet, with their role, status and last sign-in. Invite people, change roles, switch accounts off (which signs them out at once), and send fresh invite links.</li><li><strong>Roles:</strong></li><li class=\"sub\"><strong>Admins</strong> see and manage everything, including customers&#39; facts and approvals in Index.</li><li class=\"sub\"><strong>Staff</strong> see the studio&#39;s memory and their own partition.</li><li><strong>The badge, on every Nova Agent panel:</strong> `` shows your planet, your name and your role in the top bar. Tap it for your planet up close and links to your profile and your Index.</li><li><strong>The Manual, on every panel:</strong> `<code> sits beside the badge. It has a **Guide**, **How it&#39;s built**, the **History** and **What&#39;s new** for every panel, with search. Press **?** on any panel, or add </code>#nova-manual` to the address.</li></ul>","text":"Your profile: your planet, big and animated, with your name, role and \"member since\". You can re-roll your planet (or go back to your original), change your name, open your own Index, and sign out. The crew (admins): everyone as a planet, with their role, status and last sign-in. Invite people, change roles, switch accounts off (which signs them out at once), and send fresh invite links. Roles: Admins see and manage everything, including customers' facts and approvals in Index. Staff see the studio's memory and their own partition. The badge, on every Nova Agent panel: `` shows your planet, your name and your role in the top bar. Tap it for your planet up close and links to your profile and your Index. The Manual, on every panel: ` sits beside the badge. It has a **Guide**, **How it's built**, the **History** and **What's new** for every panel, with search. Press **?** on any panel, or add #nova-manual` to the address."},{"id":"the-work-tabs-3","title":"The work tabs","html":"<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Tab</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Enquiries</strong></td><td>Every enquiry NovaBot took. Email, call, make a booking link with the customer&#39;s details filled in, read the chat it came from, mark it done.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Chats</strong></td><td>What customers asked NovaBot on the website (kept for 90 days).</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Calendar</strong></td><td>Every booking in Acuity&#39;s diary, as a month you can swipe, with Calendar&#39;s cards and planned quests alongside. See the smart calendar.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Quests</strong></td><td>Nova Agent&#39;s plan, synced from the studio computer: the quest on now, repeating pulses, today, Missions with progress rings, and every quest. Taps (Start, Done, +15 min, Not now, Skip, Pause) go straight back to Nova Agent.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Alerts</strong></td><td>Every notification that reached a phone, newest first, with colour-coded labels, exact times, Call/Email buttons and an auto-delete switch.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>NovaBot</strong></td><td>Two chats. <strong>Ask Nova</strong> answers questions about the studio&#39;s bookings, enquiries and alerts (Nova Bot&#39;s <code>src/studio-ask.js</code>). <strong>NovaBot · bookings</strong> is NovaBot with the booking tools, talking to you as staff: get a link for a client, find, move, cancel or change a booking. Every change shows a summary and waits for a yes.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","text":"Tab What it does Enquiries Every enquiry NovaBot took. Email, call, make a booking link with the customer's details filled in, read the chat it came from, mark it done. Chats What customers asked NovaBot on the website (kept for 90 days). Calendar Every booking in Acuity's diary, as a month you can swipe, with Calendar's cards and planned quests alongside. See the smart calendar. Quests Nova Agent's plan, synced from the studio computer: the quest on now, repeating pulses, today, Missions with progress rings, and every quest. Taps (Start, Done, +15 min, Not now, Skip, Pause) go straight back to Nova Agent. Alerts Every notification that reached a phone, newest first, with colour-coded labels, exact times, Call/Email buttons and an auto-delete switch. NovaBot Two chats. Ask Nova answers questions about the studio's bookings, enquiries and alerts (Nova Bot's src/studio-ask.js ). NovaBot · bookings is NovaBot with the booking tools, talking to you as staff: get a link for a client, find, move, cancel or change a booking. Every change shows a summary and waits for a yes."},{"id":"the-smart-calendar-4","title":"The smart calendar","html":"<ul><li><strong>The week at a glance</strong>: sessions, hours booked and how full, session value, the busiest day, the next free hour, and any clashes.</li><li><strong>Glowing days</strong>: each day glows brighter as it fills; a nearly full day says FULL.</li><li><strong>A day in detail</strong>: hours booked, a fill meter, ⚠ clashes, ⏱ tight changeovers (under 15 minutes), and free slots of an hour or more within opening hours.</li><li><strong>One tap from a booking link</strong>: tapping a free slot opens NovaBot · bookings with the request written for you. &quot;✦ Ask Nova&quot; buttons ask about the week or the day.</li></ul>","text":"The week at a glance : sessions, hours booked and how full, session value, the busiest day, the next free hour, and any clashes. Glowing days : each day glows brighter as it fills; a nearly full day says FULL. A day in detail : hours booked, a fill meter, ⚠ clashes, ⏱ tight changeovers (under 15 minutes), and free slots of an hour or more within opening hours. One tap from a booking link : tapping a free slot opens NovaBot · bookings with the request written for you. \"✦ Ask Nova\" buttons ask about the week or the day."},{"id":"features-5","title":"Features","html":"<ul><li><strong>Real-booking checks.</strong> A booking alert asks Acuity about that booking as it comes into view: &quot;✓ Real booking: confirmed in Acuity&quot;, with the deposit paid, or &quot;Cancelled&quot; or &quot;Not found&quot;. Tests are labelled as tests, so nothing fake can pass for a booking.</li><li><strong>Push notifications that work with the app closed</strong> (Nova Bot&#39;s <code>src/push.js</code>, and <code>web/portal/sw.js</code>; phones that installed Portal from <code>/app/</code> keep <code>/app/sw.js</code>). New enquiries, bookings (with every detail from Acuity&#39;s private calendar feed), and alerts from Nova Agent, Quest and Mission. Android gets rich notifications with their own buzz; iPhones get the plain version, so nothing is ever lost.</li><li><strong>Pings.</strong> With Portal open, an alert rings out with a bright ping (a different one for each kind) and drops a banner from the top.</li><li><strong>Staff voice.</strong> Tap the mic and say what to do (&quot;show alerts&quot;, &quot;call Eric&quot;, &quot;new enquiries&quot;, &quot;ask NovaBot what the prices are&quot;); Whisper on Workers AI writes it down. Hands-free mode listens while the app is open for anything that starts with &quot;Nova&quot;.</li><li><strong>Quests from Nova Agent</strong> (<code>src/agent-nova.js</code>): Nova Agent sends its plan here every time it changes, and picks up taps within about a second.</li><li><strong>Ambient music</strong> (<code>web/shared/ambient.js</code>, moved from <code>web/portal/</code>): Novacane&#39;s quiet, never-ending soundtrack made live with the Web Audio API (no audio files), now with a soft electric-piano phrase now and then. Inside Nova Agent, Portal&#39;s music button works the one player in Nova Agent&#39;s main page, so the music carries on across panels.</li><li><strong>Sound effects</strong> (<code>web/shared/sfx.js</code>): Novacane&#39;s glass bells, warm under-tones and soft breaths of air for taps, tabs, switches, sends and deletes, all in the music&#39;s key, and a two-note chime when NovaBot answers.</li><li><strong>Six themes</strong>: Cosmic, Ember, Aurora, Ocean, Gold and Mono, shared with the admin pages.</li><li><strong>Options</strong> (<code>web/portal/options.js</code>): theme, text alignment and size, how times show on alerts, animations, the drifting starfield, sound effects, pings, music volume and the starting tab (any work tab, or You). Saved on the device.</li><li><strong>The suite sheet</strong> (<code>web/portal/suite.js</code>): tap the Portal brand to see every Nova app, 🔒 <strong>All links</strong> (every live and testing address, each checked on the spot), <strong>What&#39;s changed</strong> (every change by day and app: what, why and what&#39;s better), <strong>everything the suite can do</strong>, and the theme picker.</li></ul>\n<p>Switching themes in Options.  Browsing the suite sheet.</p>\n<p>One screen, six themes.</p>\n<p>On a desktop, the tabs become a side rail and lists go two-up.</p>\n<p>Ask Nova (questions about the studio&#39;s own diary)</p>\n<p><strong>Behind the scenes:</strong> Acuity&#39;s API can&#39;t change a booking&#39;s session type, price or paid status, so those changes are queued for <a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-agent\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Nova Agent</a>, the browser helper on the studio computer, which does them in Acuity&#39;s admin pages and reports back (<code>src/agent-nova.js</code>). Every day at 06:00 UK time the Worker checks it can still reach Acuity&#39;s API and alerts staff phones if not (<code>src/health.js</code>).</p>","text":"Real-booking checks. A booking alert asks Acuity about that booking as it comes into view: \"✓ Real booking: confirmed in Acuity\", with the deposit paid, or \"Cancelled\" or \"Not found\". Tests are labelled as tests, so nothing fake can pass for a booking. Push notifications that work with the app closed (Nova Bot's src/push.js , and web/portal/sw.js ; phones that installed Portal from /app/ keep /app/sw.js ). New enquiries, bookings (with every detail from Acuity's private calendar feed), and alerts from Nova Agent, Quest and Mission. Android gets rich notifications with their own buzz; iPhones get the plain version, so nothing is ever lost. Pings. With Portal open, an alert rings out with a bright ping (a different one for each kind) and drops a banner from the top. Staff voice. Tap the mic and say what to do (\"show alerts\", \"call Eric\", \"new enquiries\", \"ask NovaBot what the prices are\"); Whisper on Workers AI writes it down. Hands-free mode listens while the app is open for anything that starts with \"Nova\". Quests from Nova Agent ( src/agent-nova.js ): Nova Agent sends its plan here every time it changes, and picks up taps within about a second. Ambient music ( web/shared/ambient.js , moved from web/portal/ ): Novacane's quiet, never-ending soundtrack made live with the Web Audio API (no audio files), now with a soft electric-piano phrase now and then. Inside Nova Agent, Portal's music button works the one player in Nova Agent's main page, so the music carries on across panels. Sound effects ( web/shared/sfx.js ): Novacane's glass bells, warm under-tones and soft breaths of air for taps, tabs, switches, sends and deletes, all in the music's key, and a two-note chime when NovaBot answers. Six themes : Cosmic, Ember, Aurora, Ocean, Gold and Mono, shared with the admin pages. Options ( web/portal/options.js ): theme, text alignment and size, how times show on alerts, animations, the drifting starfield, sound effects, pings, music volume and the starting tab (any work tab, or You). Saved on the device. The suite sheet ( web/portal/suite.js ): tap the Portal brand to see every Nova app, 🔒 All links (every live and testing address, each checked on the spot), What's changed (every change by day and app: what, why and what's better), everything the suite can do , and the theme picker. Switching themes in Options. Browsing the suite sheet. One screen, six themes. On a desktop, the tabs become a side rail and lists go two-up. Ask Nova (questions about the studio's own diary) Behind the scenes: Acuity's API can't change a booking's session type, price or paid status, so those changes are queued for Nova Agent , the browser helper on the studio computer, which does them in Acuity's admin pages and reports back ( src/agent-nova.js ). Every day at 06:00 UK time the Worker checks it can still reach Acuity's API and alerts staff phones if not ( src/health.js )."},{"id":"the-planets-6","title":"The planets","html":"<p><code>planet/</code> is a pure, deterministic generator: <code>generatePlanet(seed, theme, overrides?)</code> then <code>renderPlanetSVG(planet, { size, animate })</code>. The same seed and theme always give the same planet, so nothing is stored but the seed.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Kinds:</strong> banded gas giants, cratered rocky worlds, ocean worlds with continents, molten worlds with glowing cracks, ice worlds, and ringed giants.</li><li><strong>Details:</strong> each has a palette drawn from the theme&#39;s ramps, an atmosphere glow, clouds or bands, and maybe rings (split properly in front of and behind the planet), up to three moons, an aurora or a storm.</li><li><strong>A real sphere:</strong> surface detail is projected onto it, with limb darkening, a terminator shadow and a specular highlight. Small badges simplify themselves, and the 512px hero animates.</li><li><strong>Speed:</strong> 1,000 planets generate and render in about half a second.</li><li><strong>Themes hold all the art direction:</strong> palettes, surfaces, glow, rings, moons, naming and the starfield. The Nova look lives in <code>planet/themes/nova.js</code>. When the studio&#39;s own lore is ready, it becomes a new theme file, with no change to the generator. A test proves it with a &quot;lore&quot; theme.</li><li><strong>Porting:</strong> <code>planet/README.md</code> documents the exact random number generator and draw order, so a Kotlin port (for Nova Club) draws identical planets.</li></ul>","text":"planet/ is a pure, deterministic generator: generatePlanet(seed, theme, overrides?) then renderPlanetSVG(planet, { size, animate }) . The same seed and theme always give the same planet, so nothing is stored but the seed. Kinds: banded gas giants, cratered rocky worlds, ocean worlds with continents, molten worlds with glowing cracks, ice worlds, and ringed giants. Details: each has a palette drawn from the theme's ramps, an atmosphere glow, clouds or bands, and maybe rings (split properly in front of and behind the planet), up to three moons, an aurora or a storm. A real sphere: surface detail is projected onto it, with limb darkening, a terminator shadow and a specular highlight. Small badges simplify themselves, and the 512px hero animates. Speed: 1,000 planets generate and render in about half a second. Themes hold all the art direction: palettes, surfaces, glow, rings, moons, naming and the starfield. The Nova look lives in planet/themes/nova.js . When the studio's own lore is ready, it becomes a new theme file, with no change to the generator. A test proves it with a \"lore\" theme. Porting: planet/README.md documents the exact random number generator and draw order, so a Kotlin port (for Nova Club) draws identical planets."}],"built":[{"id":"the-api-on-nova-bot-s-worker-0","title":"The API (on Nova Bot's worker)","html":"<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>POST /auth/login</code></td><td><code>{ email, password, client? }</code> → session cookie, or an app token with <code>client: &quot;app&quot;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /auth/logout</code></td><td>ends this session everywhere</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /auth/me</code> · <code>GET /auth/status</code></td><td>who&#39;s signed in · <code>{ setupNeeded, signedIn, staff }</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /auth/setup</code></td><td>the first admin (with the <code>ADMIN_PASSWORD</code> secret)</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /auth/invite?token=</code> · <code>POST /auth/invite/accept</code></td><td>accepting an invite</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /staff</code> · <code>POST /staff</code> · <code>POST /staff/:id/invite</code></td><td>the crew, inviting, a fresh link (admins)</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /staff/:id</code> · <code>PATCH /staff/:id</code></td><td>a profile; changing name, planet, role or status</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /staff/:id/planet.svg</code></td><td>the planet badge (<code>?size=</code>, <code>?animate=1</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /staff/:id/index</code></td><td>that person&#39;s Index partition and the studio&#39;s shared facts</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<ul><li><strong>Passwords:</strong> PBKDF2-SHA256, salted, 100,000 rounds.</li><li><strong>Sessions:</strong> a random token in an httpOnly, Secure cookie. Only its hash is stored, and signing out deletes it.</li><li><strong>Brute force:</strong> sign-in, setup and invite attempts are rate limited.</li><li><strong>Cross-site changes:</strong> changes must come from the site itself.</li></ul>\n<p>The code is in <a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-bot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">nova-bot</a> under <code>src/portal/</code>.</p>","text":"POST /auth/login { email, password, client? } → session cookie, or an app token with client: \"app\" POST /auth/logout ends this session everywhere GET /auth/me · GET /auth/status who's signed in · { setupNeeded, signedIn, staff } POST /auth/setup the first admin (with the ADMIN_PASSWORD secret) GET /auth/invite?token= · POST /auth/invite/accept accepting an invite GET /staff · POST /staff · POST /staff/:id/invite the crew, inviting, a fresh link (admins) GET /staff/:id · PATCH /staff/:id a profile; changing name, planet, role or status GET /staff/:id/planet.svg the planet badge ( ?size= , ?animate=1 ) GET /staff/:id/index that person's Index partition and the studio's shared facts Passwords: PBKDF2-SHA256, salted, 100,000 rounds. Sessions: a random token in an httpOnly, Secure cookie. Only its hash is stored, and signing out deletes it. Brute force: sign-in, setup and invite attempts are rate limited. Cross-site changes: changes must come from the site itself. The code is in nova-bot under src/portal/ ."}],"news":[],"history":{"total":22,"first":"2026-10-07T01:34:16+01:00","commits":[{"hash":"5de742c","date":"2026-10-09T21:42:53+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent: \"Chat\" is now \"Agent\" everywhere you see it","body":"The section title, the panels bar, the phone menu, the status line, the hints, the\ninstall description, Portal's and Calendar's mentions and the manual. Nova Bot's website\nchats (Portal's Chats tab, Index's customer facts) keep their name. Code names stay."},{"hash":"263cf4f","date":"2026-10-09T02:31:27+01:00","subject":"Cosmic icons, one theme for everything, planet colours, smart top bar, status line","body":"Icons: a cosmic set, each with its own colour (mixed with the theme), sky and shape; Talk to\nNova Agent, Quests and Missions have their own. look.js: one theme for every panel (or each its\nown), and colour everything from your planet. Typing hides the panels bar. The top bar: Auto,\nAlways shown or Always hidden. The status line under the bar: Panels button (the top one is\ngone), version and build, what changed lately for the part of the bar you point at, on and off\ntimes, recent activity and a 12-hour clock. Lossless audio's sounds come along."},{"hash":"c228593","date":"2026-10-09T01:24:38+01:00","subject":"Calmer, lusher sounds, and quiet extras with their own switch","body":"Every sound is quieter with a warm top end and more space. New, barely-there extras:\nscrolling, typing, sliders, dragging (Calendar's note cards: pick up, each step, put down)\nand hovering, each kept to its own pace. Their own switch in Portal's Options and the\nphone's gear; only heard while sound effects are on."},{"hash":"48b4b4c","date":"2026-10-09T00:58:39+01:00","subject":"Lush Novacane sounds, and quiet ambient music across all of Nova Agent","body":"Sound effects: glass bells, warm under-tones and breaths of air, in the music's key, with\nstereo, reverb and echo; a hello chime when sounds are switched on. Every old sound kept.\nAmbient music moves to shared/ and becomes one player for the whole app (header switch,\nphone gear → Music, Portal's button), remembered on the device, with a soft electric-piano\nphrase now and then."},{"hash":"a70307d","date":"2026-10-08T17:44:17+01:00","subject":"Admin lives in Portal: no Admin button in Nova Agent","body":"Portal gets an Admin section for admins (Studio pages, Crew, Google, Links),\nshown inside Portal. Nova Agent's bar and launcher lose Admin and All links;\ninviting from the crew page is hidden."},{"hash":"3fbe6c1","date":"2026-10-08T15:30:34+01:00","subject":"Portal on phones: a Today screen, five tabs, full-screen inside Nova Agent, lighter","body":"- Inside Nova Agent on a phone, an open panel gets the whole screen (Nova\n  Agent's header, the panels strip and the floating Manual step aside; the\n  slim bar keeps ← Nova Agent, and the panel's name switches panels), with\n  room for the notch and the home bar.\n- Portal opens on Today: new enquiries, today's chats and bookings, alerts\n  and quests at a glance (each tile opens its section), then the newest\n  enquiries.\n- Phones: five tabs (Today, Enquiries, Chats, Calendar, More); Quests,\n  Alerts, NovaBot and You are under More with their counts. Enquiries fold\n  to one line until tapped; compact alerts and chats; small headings on one\n  line; a smaller planet on You; inputs at 16px (no zoom on typing).\n- Lighter: no frosted glass or moving titles on phones; the ambient music\n  engine loads after the first screen; the Manual (and its 287 KB of\n  content) loads only outside frames, and p"},{"hash":"02e1211","date":"2026-10-08T13:48:41+01:00","subject":"Portal: any password length","body":""},{"hash":"5eb1b0b","date":"2026-10-08T13:43:54+01:00","subject":"Portal: change your password on the You page","body":"Admins choose a new one without the old one; everyone else confirms their\ncurrent password. Other sign-ins end; this one carries on."},{"hash":"ed420d6","date":"2026-10-08T13:33:52+01:00","subject":"Portal is the one sign-in","body":"Signed out, the planet opens Portal's sign-in (in Nova Agent's viewer): no\nsign-in form of its own, and no Sign in with Google anywhere. Google is a\nconnection, not a way in: Portal's You page shows it (connected as whom), with\nSet up / Connect Google for admins (Admin → Google). Notes asks\n/auth/google-status for the studio's Google key."},{"hash":"4fabb4b","date":"2026-10-08T13:26:32+01:00","subject":"Sign in with Google, on the planet and in Portal; Notes uses the studio's Google","body":"- The planet's sign-in card and Portal's sign-in card get a Sign in with\n  Google button once an admin has set Google up (Admin → Google). Google's\n  page opens in a small window (full screen in the installed phone app) and\n  every panel follows when it's done.\n- On the studio PC, Nova Agent starts it (/auth/google): it makes up a\n  verifier, Nova Bot sends back a one-time code to /auth/google/done, and\n  Nova Agent swaps the two for its own sign-in (src/signin.ts).\n- Notes' Save to Google Docs uses the studio's Google key, with nothing to\n  set up; without it, a button opens Admin → Google."},{"hash":"f796db5","date":"2026-10-08T11:47:15+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent lives at /agent/, on the PC and online","body":"/ goes on to /agent/, and /agent/<panel> opens Nova Agent with that panel.\nPanels opened on their own, notifications and the app's shortcuts open\n/agent/?open=<panel>. The installed app starts at /agent/."},{"hash":"00484d5","date":"2026-10-08T11:38:21+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent is the one app: panels open only inside it","body":"- A panel opened on its own (/portal/, /calendar/, /notes/, /app/memory/,\n  /observatory/, /lossless/, /visualizer, /admin...) opens Nova Agent with\n  that panel instead: /?open=<its address>, keeping its query and #hash.\n  The server tells by Sec-Fetch-Dest; inside.js (and Calendar's embed.js)\n  catch browsers that don't say.\n- Nova Agent reads ?open= and opens the panel; a tapped notification opens\n  its panel too (nova-open from the service worker).\n- No more \"Inside / Window\" switch or open-in-a-window button. Visualizer\n  and Admin are panels; Admin is passed on to Nova Bot with this computer's\n  sign-in (Portal first when signed out).\n- One installable app: /sw.js handles phone notifications for the whole\n  app (Portal subscribes through it, keeping an old /app/ or /portal/\n  address if the phone has one, so nothing arrives twice); the old service\n  workers open taps in Nova Agent."},{"hash":"37073d2","date":"2026-10-08T02:15:25+01:00","subject":"One Portal: one staff app at /portal/","body":"Portal is gone as a separate panel. Portal is the one staff app: one header,\none tab bar with Portal's work tabs (Enquiries, Chats, Calendar, Quests,\nAlerts, NovaBot) plus You (your planet and profile; admins reach the crew\nand the admin pages from there). Portal's sign-in, setup and invite cards\nreplace Portal's old sign-in screen.\n- web/portal's scripts and styles move into web/portal (app.js, app.css,\n  ambient.js, options.js, suite.js). portal.js runs the page (who's signed\n  in, the address, the You tab) and starts the work tabs (window.NovaHub);\n  the tabs hand sign-outs back (window.PortalPage). Tabs follow the\n  address: /portal/?view=enquiries|chats|calendar|quests|alerts|bot|me|crew,\n  #nova opens Alerts, no ?view opens the starting tab from Options (which\n  can now be You). Tells the badge when sign-in changes (NovaPortal.changed).\n- portal.css is scoped to Portal's own parts (.pv) with p"},{"hash":"326ecf9","date":"2026-10-08T01:33:59+01:00","subject":"Portal and Index: Portal is the one sign-in","body":"The shared-password box is gone from Portal's and Index's sign-in screens:\nsigned out, there's one button, to Portal, which brings you back to\n/app/ or /app/memory/ (not the old /studio/ and /index/). The guides\nand the Manual say the same."},{"hash":"100fb09","date":"2026-10-08T00:43:48+01:00","subject":"Plain names: everything is Nova Agent, and its panels are Portal, Portal, Calendar…","body":"Undoes the made-up names. \"Studio\" is Portal again and \"Crew\" is Portal again\n(only where the earlier rename had changed them; real uses of the words are\nkept). Every panel and feature drops \"Nova\": Portal, Portal, Calendar, Notes,\nIndex, Observatory, Missions, Quests and the Manual. \"Nova\" stays for Nova\nAgent itself, Nova Bot and Nova Club.\nThe original addresses are back: Portal at /app/, Portal at /portal/ and\nIndex at /app/memory/ (the panels live in web/portal, web/portal, web/index).\nNova Agent's own icons move to /agent/ to make room. /studio/, /crew/ and\n/index/ redirect, for anything that picked them up yesterday."},{"hash":"fef653e","date":"2026-10-07T23:27:20+01:00","subject":"Panels laid out: Studio (was Portal), Crew (was Nova Portal), Index…","body":"- web/studio: Portal's staff app, now Nova Agent's Studio panel\n- web/crew: Nova Portal's app (sign-in, me, crew, invites), now the Crew\n  panel, with the planet avatar generator beside it\n- web/index, web/calendar, web/notes, web/observatory: the panels\n- Each app's README and pictures move to docs/apps/<panel>\n- The manual and badge scripts move to scripts/, and the Observatory's\n  scanning tools to scripts/observatory (npm run observatory:scan,\n  :capture, :build), writing into web/observatory as before\n- Calendar's and Notes' own deploy configs (their separate workers.dev\n  sites) are dropped: they're panels now\nPaths inside the panels are fixed up next."},{"hash":"e91ec2e","date":"2026-10-07T23:23:37+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent takes in Nova Portal (with its history), as web/portal","body":"git-subtree-dir: web/portal\ngit-subtree-mainline: 1ec177bf4bee982fb33f49af61d4e5385a21735e\ngit-subtree-split: 7f3bec195c49d98e0f89c3c6412bbb96cf7fd472"},{"hash":"7f3bec1","date":"2026-10-07T16:31:24+01:00","subject":"The Nova Manual: refreshed with today's changes","body":""},{"hash":"0a62fd3","date":"2026-10-07T16:30:26+01:00","subject":"The Nova Manual: every Nova app's guide, build, history and what's new","body":"<nova-manual> sits beside the Portal badge on every Nova app (or floats\nin the corner where there's no top bar yet). It opens a panel for each\napp in the suite: a Guide, How it's built, its History as a timeline,\nand What's new (the last week, and what's being worked on), with search\nacross all of it. ? opens it anywhere; #nova-manual in the address too.\nscripts/build-manual.mjs makes its pages (app/manual-data.js) from every\napp's README and git history, then shares the badge and the manual with\nNova Notes, Calendar and Observatory. Built like the badge: shadow DOM,\na constructed stylesheet and no inline styles, so it works under Nova\nPortal's strict security rules."},{"hash":"fe6dcd0","date":"2026-10-07T02:01:03+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent's badge: Connect as me, and back to automatic","body":""},{"hash":"dc29ca6","date":"2026-10-07T01:50:03+01:00","subject":"The Nova Portal badge for every Nova app, and Connect","body":"- app/badge.js: <nova-portal-badge>, your planet, name and role with a\n  card (planet up close, profile, Nova Index), themed by each app\n- Connect: other suite sites get a read-only token to show the badge"},{"hash":"d1e6ab3","date":"2026-10-07T01:34:16+01:00","subject":"Nova Portal: one sign-in for the Nova suite, and a planet for everyone","body":"- app/: setup, sign in, invites, profiles with an animated planet, the crew,\n  options; one session for Portal, Nova Index and the admin pages\n- planet/: a pure, deterministic, themeable planet generator (gas giants,\n  rocky, ocean, molten and ice worlds, rings, moons, aurora, storms), with\n  the Nova theme in its own file so the studio's lore can replace it"}],"work":[{"state":"changed","file":"docs/apps/portal/README.md"},{"state":"changed","file":"web/portal/app.css"},{"state":"changed","file":"web/portal/app.js"},{"state":"changed","file":"web/portal/icon.svg"},{"state":"changed","file":"web/portal/old-app-address/apple-touch-icon.png"},{"state":"changed","file":"web/portal/old-app-address/icon-192.png"},{"state":"changed","file":"web/portal/old-app-address/icon-512.png"},{"state":"changed","file":"web/portal/old-app-address/icon-maskable-512.png"},{"state":"changed","file":"web/portal/old-app-address/icon.svg"},{"state":"changed","file":"web/portal/old-app-address/manifest.webmanifest"},{"state":"changed","file":"web/portal/old-app-address/sw.js"},{"state":"changed","file":"web/portal/portal.js"},{"state":"changed","file":"web/portal/sw.js"}],"workCount":13,"workStat":"13 files changed, 68 insertions(+), 60 deletions(-)"}},{"id":"calendar","name":"Calendar","colour":"#F2D9A0","glyph":"◷","where":"A Nova Agent panel","links":[["Open Calendar","http://localhost:4545/calendar/"]],"repo":"na","shared":"","tagline":"The studio's calendar under the real sky: note cards, day cards, the moon and special days, Nova Agent's plan and the studio's bookings, in one place.","intro":"<blockquote><strong>A Nova Agent panel.</strong> Its code is in <code>web/calendar/</code> in Nova Agent&#39;s repo, and it opens inside Nova Agent at <code>/agent/calendar</code>.</blockquote>","guide":[{"id":"what-you-can-do-0","title":"What you can do","html":"<ul><li><strong>See it your way:</strong> Month, Week, Day or List. Arrows (or a swipe) move on, <strong>Today</strong> comes back, and tapping the month&#39;s name jumps to any date. A pink line shows the time now.</li><li><strong>Add a note card:</strong> the <strong>+</strong> button, <strong>+ Note card</strong> under the day, a tap on an empty time (Week and Day), or a second click on a day (Month, on a computer). Typing is quickest: <code>Mix review Friday 2pm 1h @Studio A</code> fills everything in.</li><li><strong>Every note card has its own painted picture</strong> (a planet, a galaxy, a comet…): pick the kind or let it surprise you, press <strong>New artwork</strong> for another, and <strong>Save image</strong> to keep it big.</li><li><strong>Change:</strong> tap a note card to edit it. On a computer, drag it to move it and drag its bottom edge to make it longer; on a phone, hold it for a moment, then drag.</li><li><strong>Repeat:</strong> every day, week, month or year, or a custom rule (every 2 weeks on Mon and Wed, until a date or a number of times). Changing or deleting one of them asks: just this one, this and the ones after, or every one.</li><li><strong>Reminders:</strong> at the start, 10 or 30 minutes, an hour or a day before. They arrive on phones as alerts, even when the studio PC is off.</li><li><strong>Delete</strong> with <strong>Undo</strong> (a few seconds to change your mind), <strong>duplicate</strong>, pick a <strong>colour</strong>, add <strong>where</strong> and <strong>notes</strong>.</li><li><strong>Day cards:</strong> birthdays, release days, studio sessions, holidays and more (<strong>+ Day card</strong>). Each has a kind with its icon, a <strong>title style</strong> (Nebula, Supernova, Orbit, Constellation, Eclipse, Aurora, Celestial), its own <strong>theme</strong> and a painted header (<strong>New artwork</strong> for another). They show as a banner on the day, wear their theme in the month, and can come back every year.</li><li><strong>The real sky:</strong> the moon&#39;s phases (full moons in gold, with their names), and special days (Easter, Bonfire Night, the solstices and equinoxes, meteor-shower peaks…). Tap <strong>Make it a day card</strong> to keep one. The strip above the month shows its day cards, full moon and special days; tap one to go there.</li><li><strong>Backup</strong> (the layers button): <strong>Export</strong> downloads every note card and day card; <strong>Import</strong> brings a backup back in, including one from the old Calendar.</li><li><strong>What to show</strong> (the layers button): note cards, day cards, the moon and special days, Quests (Nova Agent&#39;s plan: read-only here, change them in Quests) and studio bookings (read-only, from the diary).</li><li><strong>Search</strong> every note card and day card by title, place or notes.</li></ul>","text":"See it your way: Month, Week, Day or List. Arrows (or a swipe) move on, Today comes back, and tapping the month's name jumps to any date. A pink line shows the time now. Add a note card: the + button, + Note card under the day, a tap on an empty time (Week and Day), or a second click on a day (Month, on a computer). Typing is quickest: Mix review Friday 2pm 1h @Studio A fills everything in. Every note card has its own painted picture (a planet, a galaxy, a comet…): pick the kind or let it surprise you, press New artwork for another, and Save image to keep it big. Change: tap a note card to edit it. On a computer, drag it to move it and drag its bottom edge to make it longer; on a phone, hold it for a moment, then drag. Repeat: every day, week, month or year, or a custom rule (every 2 weeks on Mon and Wed, until a date or a number of times). Changing or deleting one of them asks: just this one, this and the ones after, or every one. Reminders: at the start, 10 or 30 minutes, an hour or a day before. They arrive on phones as alerts, even when the studio PC is off. Delete with Undo (a few seconds to change your mind), duplicate , pick a colour , add where and notes . Day cards: birthdays, release days, studio sessions, holidays and more ( + Day card ). Each has a kind with its icon, a title style (Nebula, Supernova, Orbit, Constellation, Eclipse, Aurora, Celestial), its own theme and a painted header ( New artwork for another). They show as a banner on the day, wear their theme in the month, and can come back every year. The real sky: the moon's phases (full moons in gold, with their names), and special days (Easter, Bonfire Night, the solstices and equinoxes, meteor-shower peaks…). Tap Make it a day card to keep one. The strip above the month shows its day cards, full moon and special days; tap one to go there. Backup (the layers button): Export downloads every note card and day card; Import brings a backup back in, including one from the old Calendar. What to show (the layers button): note cards, day cards, the moon and special days, Quests (Nova Agent's plan: read-only here, change them in Quests) and studio bookings (read-only, from the diary). Search every note card and day card by title, place or notes."},{"id":"works-with-nova-agent-1","title":"Works with Nova Agent","html":"<ul><li>Ask Agent (a note card is what Agent calls an event): &quot;Add a mix review Friday at 2 for an hour at Studio A&quot;, &quot;Move it to 4&quot;, &quot;Make the standup repeat every weekday&quot;, &quot;Remind me 10 minutes before&quot;, &quot;Delete it&quot;.</li><li>Nova Agent&#39;s planner keeps Quests out of your note cards (every time a repeating one happens). All-day note cards are markers, like day cards, not busy time.</li></ul>","text":"Ask Agent (a note card is what Agent calls an event): \"Add a mix review Friday at 2 for an hour at Studio A\", \"Move it to 4\", \"Make the standup repeat every weekday\", \"Remind me 10 minutes before\", \"Delete it\". Nova Agent's planner keeps Quests out of your note cards (every time a repeating one happens). All-day note cards are markers, like day cards, not busy time."},{"id":"where-it-s-kept-2","title":"Where it's kept","html":"<p>The calendar lives on Nova Bot (its D1 database, <code>calendar_items</code>), so it&#39;s the same on every phone and computer and keeps working when the studio PC is off. Each browser keeps a copy so it opens instantly and works offline; changes made offline save when you&#39;re back. The latest change wins; if another device changed something later, Calendar shows that and says so.</p>\n<p>Nova Agent on the studio PC keeps its own copy (<code>data/calendar.json</code>, read by its chat and planner) in step with Nova Bot every few seconds (<code>src/calendar/cloud.ts</code> ⇄ <code>POST /nova-agent/calendar</code>).</p>\n<p>Anything an earlier version of Calendar saved in a browser is brought in the first time it opens there (once, never twice).</p>","text":"The calendar lives on Nova Bot (its D1 database, calendar_items ), so it's the same on every phone and computer and keeps working when the studio PC is off. Each browser keeps a copy so it opens instantly and works offline; changes made offline save when you're back. The latest change wins; if another device changed something later, Calendar shows that and says so. Nova Agent on the studio PC keeps its own copy ( data/calendar.json , read by its chat and planner) in step with Nova Bot every few seconds ( src/calendar/cloud.ts ⇄ POST /nova-agent/calendar ). Anything an earlier version of Calendar saved in a browser is brought in the first time it opens there (once, never twice)."},{"id":"for-developers-3","title":"For developers","html":"<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>File</th><th>What it is</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>web/calendar/js/cal.js</code></td><td>The views, the editor, drag, keys, backups</td></tr><tr><td><code>web/calendar/js/presets.js</code></td><td>Day card kinds, title styles and line icons</td></tr><tr><td><code>web/calendar/js/sky.js</code></td><td>Moon phases, full moon names, seasonal and cosmic days</td></tr><tr><td><code>web/calendar/js/cosmos.js</code></td><td>The painted pictures (loaded when first needed)</td></tr><tr><td><code>web/calendar/js/themes.js</code></td><td>The themes a day card can wear</td></tr><tr><td><code>web/calendar/js/data.js</code></td><td>Saving to Nova Bot, the offline copy and queue, bringing in old data</td></tr><tr><td><code>web/calendar/js/recur.js</code></td><td>Repeat rules (shared with Nova Agent&#39;s planner and Nova Bot&#39;s reminders)</td></tr><tr><td><code>web/calendar/js/quickadd.js</code></td><td>&quot;Mix review Friday 2pm 1h&quot; → a note card</td></tr><tr><td>Nova Bot <code>src/calendar/items.js</code></td><td><code>GET/PUT/DELETE /app/api/calendar/items</code>, Nova Agent&#39;s sync</td></tr><tr><td>Nova Bot <code>src/calendar/reminders.js</code></td><td>Reminders on phones (every minute)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Keys: ← → move, <strong>T</strong> today, <strong>N</strong> new, <strong>M W D L</strong> views, <strong>Esc</strong> closes.</p>","text":"File What it is web/calendar/js/cal.js The views, the editor, drag, keys, backups web/calendar/js/presets.js Day card kinds, title styles and line icons web/calendar/js/sky.js Moon phases, full moon names, seasonal and cosmic days web/calendar/js/cosmos.js The painted pictures (loaded when first needed) web/calendar/js/themes.js The themes a day card can wear web/calendar/js/data.js Saving to Nova Bot, the offline copy and queue, bringing in old data web/calendar/js/recur.js Repeat rules (shared with Nova Agent's planner and Nova Bot's reminders) web/calendar/js/quickadd.js \"Mix review Friday 2pm 1h\" → a note card Nova Bot src/calendar/items.js GET/PUT/DELETE /app/api/calendar/items , Nova Agent's sync Nova Bot src/calendar/reminders.js Reminders on phones (every minute) Keys: ← → move, T today, N new, M W D L views, Esc closes."}],"built":[],"news":[],"history":{"total":41,"first":"2026-10-06T15:52:52+01:00","commits":[{"hash":"5de742c","date":"2026-10-09T21:42:53+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent: \"Chat\" is now \"Agent\" everywhere you see it","body":"The section title, the panels bar, the phone menu, the status line, the hints, the\ninstall description, Portal's and Calendar's mentions and the manual. Nova Bot's website\nchats (Portal's Chats tab, Index's customer facts) keep their name. Code names stay."},{"hash":"d9eab3f","date":"2026-10-09T18:04:10+01:00","subject":"Calendar: every day measured so nothing is cut off; cards wear the current theme; no \"of\" in day names","body":"Each day steps down only as far as it needs (small line, one-line titles, symbol and title,\nsymbols), then short day numbers, then \"+N\". Special days and the moon become symbols on\nsmall days. The month keeps the screen's height when the chosen day sits below it."},{"hash":"b8f1ce2","date":"2026-10-09T17:35:49+01:00","subject":"Calendar: symbols on phones too","body":""},{"hash":"98b3fab","date":"2026-10-09T17:35:03+01:00","subject":"Calendar: day words and symbols switch at sensible sizes; clear of the moon","body":""},{"hash":"ab63b94","date":"2026-10-09T17:34:13+01:00","subject":"Calendar: size checks read the month's grid (all days alike)","body":""},{"hash":"b12896d","date":"2026-10-09T17:32:46+01:00","subject":"Calendar: small days show cards as symbols, note cards in Nova Agent's glass and glow, the day written out to fit","body":""},{"hash":"69bb593","date":"2026-10-09T17:15:17+01:00","subject":"Calendar: + more under the card","body":""},{"hash":"9fca33a","date":"2026-10-09T17:15:10+01:00","subject":"Calendar: small days show one card on a line and + more","body":""},{"hash":"4fca5a2","date":"2026-10-09T17:14:35+01:00","subject":"Calendar: each day shows what fits it","body":""},{"hash":"bd2a993","date":"2026-10-09T17:14:00+01:00","subject":"Status line: Auto, Always shown or Always hidden, and each part optional; Calendar: fits, spacing, colour, centring (follows Centre all text)","body":""},{"hash":"011089e","date":"2026-10-09T17:02:30+01:00","subject":"Calendar: the time above the title, titles up to three lines","body":""},{"hash":"e2e99aa","date":"2026-10-09T17:01:37+01:00","subject":"Calendar makeover: a cosmic Novacane sky and glassy month, no stripes on Quests and bookings, note cards with their whole title and what they're for","body":""},{"hash":"154133c","date":"2026-10-09T03:08:06+01:00","subject":"Smaller bar, clearer status line, distinct settings icons, compact Quests, glowing scrollbars with sounds, a shifting cosmic sky, centred titles and chat","body":""},{"hash":"1d9cff9","date":"2026-10-09T02:54:25+01:00","subject":"No glass bubbles, one glow everywhere, bars fit their contents, centred text","body":"The panels bar's tiles sit right on the night sky (a glow behind the one you point at, a line of\nlight under the open one, glowing lines between groups). glow.css: the same edge and nebula light\non the header, columns, panel frame, pop-ups and status line, and the same glow on buttons, tabs\nand boxes, in the panels too. On computers the three bars are as wide as their contents. All text\nis centred (a switch in the Panels window turns it off); Notes documents and code keep their own."},{"hash":"263cf4f","date":"2026-10-09T02:31:27+01:00","subject":"Cosmic icons, one theme for everything, planet colours, smart top bar, status line","body":"Icons: a cosmic set, each with its own colour (mixed with the theme), sky and shape; Talk to\nNova Agent, Quests and Missions have their own. look.js: one theme for every panel (or each its\nown), and colour everything from your planet. Typing hides the panels bar. The top bar: Auto,\nAlways shown or Always hidden. The status line under the bar: Panels button (the top one is\ngone), version and build, what changed lately for the part of the bar you point at, on and off\ntimes, recent activity and a 12-hour clock. Lossless audio's sounds come along."},{"hash":"c228593","date":"2026-10-09T01:24:38+01:00","subject":"Calmer, lusher sounds, and quiet extras with their own switch","body":"Every sound is quieter with a warm top end and more space. New, barely-there extras:\nscrolling, typing, sliders, dragging (Calendar's note cards: pick up, each step, put down)\nand hovering, each kept to its own pace. Their own switch in Portal's Options and the\nphone's gear; only heard while sound effects are on."},{"hash":"8ff866a","date":"2026-10-09T01:18:58+01:00","subject":"One panels bar everywhere (no Panels box), softer ambient sounds, light motion","body":"The panels strip loses its Panels box and keeps the same groups and tiles whatever is open;\nwith a panel open it only gets smaller. Sounds swell in and chords bloom together instead of\nrunning up; taps are a low felt touch. Buttons and tiles press in softly, the open panel's\ntile breathes, panels fade in (scale and opacity only; off for reduced motion or calm)."},{"hash":"f276c87","date":"2026-10-08T22:56:34+01:00","subject":"Calendar: note cards again, under the real sky","body":"Every feature the new Calendar had stays; what the old one had comes back.\n- Note cards (stored as kind \"event\"): called note cards everywhere, shown as\n  little tinted cards with their titles in the month (not bars), as cards in\n  week and day, and as rows with their own painted picture. The sheet paints\n  the picture (cosmos.js, back, loaded when first needed): pick its kind,\n  New artwork, Save image (1920×1080).\n- Day cards: their kind and icon, title styles (Nebula … Celestial), their\n  own theme and a painted header (New artwork) are back; a banner on the day,\n  themed in the month. + Day card beside + Note card.\n- The real sky (sky.js, back): moon phases (full moons in gold, with names),\n  the day's moon, seasonal and cosmic days with \"Make it a day card\", and a\n  strip of the month's day cards, full moon and special days. A layer.\n- Backup (in the layers menu): Export, and Import"},{"hash":"3773415","date":"2026-10-08T18:14:42+01:00","subject":"Calendar: a full calendar that works from anywhere","body":"Month, week, day and list views; add (or type it: \"Mix review Friday 2pm 1h\"),\nchange, drag to move and resize, duplicate, delete with Undo; repeats with\n\"just this one / this and following / all\"; reminders on phones; colours,\nplaces, notes; day cards kept; Quests and studio bookings alongside\n(read-only); search. Saved on Nova Bot (works with the PC off), with an\noffline copy and queue in each browser; old browser data brought in once.\nNova Agent keeps data/calendar.json in step with Nova Bot\n(src/calendar/cloud.ts); its planner counts every repeat as busy time and its\nchat can set places, all-day, colours, repeats and reminders."},{"hash":"27a756e","date":"2026-10-08T17:45:50+01:00","subject":"WIP calendar-pro","body":""},{"hash":"932c20c","date":"2026-10-08T16:59:59+01:00","subject":"Panels on phones: fit, lighter, less scrolling","body":"- Notes: one top bar (notes list, the note's name, Google Docs) and the menus;\n  the toolbar is one row you swipe, with the everyday tools (the rest stay in\n  the menus); 16px fields; no glass blur, grain or drifting background.\n- Observatory: a slim title, the numbers as a compact strip, each project as\n  one short row with a small drawn cover (no full-size screenshots on phones);\n  category chips in one row; no star map, no moving sky, no blur.\n- Calendar and Index: no glass blur or endless decorative motion on phones.\n- Lossless audio: snug margins, big buttons, 16px fields.\n- Visualizer: no error when the studio PC is off; fits a phone."},{"hash":"f796db5","date":"2026-10-08T11:47:15+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent lives at /agent/, on the PC and online","body":"/ goes on to /agent/, and /agent/<panel> opens Nova Agent with that panel.\nPanels opened on their own, notifications and the app's shortcuts open\n/agent/?open=<panel>. The installed app starts at /agent/."},{"hash":"00484d5","date":"2026-10-08T11:38:21+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent is the one app: panels open only inside it","body":"- A panel opened on its own (/portal/, /calendar/, /notes/, /app/memory/,\n  /observatory/, /lossless/, /visualizer, /admin...) opens Nova Agent with\n  that panel instead: /?open=<its address>, keeping its query and #hash.\n  The server tells by Sec-Fetch-Dest; inside.js (and Calendar's embed.js)\n  catch browsers that don't say.\n- Nova Agent reads ?open= and opens the panel; a tapped notification opens\n  its panel too (nova-open from the service worker).\n- No more \"Inside / Window\" switch or open-in-a-window button. Visualizer\n  and Admin are panels; Admin is passed on to Nova Bot with this computer's\n  sign-in (Portal first when signed out).\n- One installable app: /sw.js handles phone notifications for the whole\n  app (Portal subscribes through it, keeping an old /app/ or /portal/\n  address if the phone has one, so nothing arrives twice); the old service\n  workers open taps in Nova Agent."},{"hash":"8ac9531","date":"2026-10-08T02:04:26+01:00","subject":"Lossless audio and Observatory as panels everywhere; docs at the real addresses","body":"- Lossless audio is served by Nova Agent at /lossless/ and opens inside it like\n  the other panels. Signalling and the relay setup come from Nova Bot (which now\n  serves it online too), so the other device can be anywhere; invite links point\n  at the online address. /lossless/ice lets Nova Agent's own page ask.\n- Observatory online asks for a Portal sign-in before showing the projects\n  (Nova Bot keeps them for signed-in staff).\n- Calendar's and Notes' guides link to their addresses on Nova Bot, not the old\n  standalone sites."},{"hash":"9e079ef","date":"2026-10-08T00:47:29+01:00","subject":"Notes and Calendar show the current version after an update","body":"Their offline helpers answered from the cache first and refreshed in the\nbackground, so after every change you saw the previous version once (old\nnames, old behaviour). Online they now fetch fresh first and use the cache\nonly when offline. Inside Nova Agent, where nothing needs to work offline,\ntheir helper clears what it kept, unregisters and reloads the page."},{"hash":"100fb09","date":"2026-10-08T00:43:48+01:00","subject":"Plain names: everything is Nova Agent, and its panels are Portal, Portal, Calendar…","body":"Undoes the made-up names. \"Studio\" is Portal again and \"Crew\" is Portal again\n(only where the earlier rename had changed them; real uses of the words are\nkept). Every panel and feature drops \"Nova\": Portal, Portal, Calendar, Notes,\nIndex, Observatory, Missions, Quests and the Manual. \"Nova\" stays for Nova\nAgent itself, Nova Bot and Nova Club.\nThe original addresses are back: Portal at /app/, Portal at /portal/ and\nIndex at /app/memory/ (the panels live in web/portal, web/portal, web/index).\nNova Agent's own icons move to /agent/ to make room. /studio/, /crew/ and\n/index/ redirect, for anything that picked them up yesterday."},{"hash":"9aa754c","date":"2026-10-07T23:40:50+01:00","subject":"README: Nova Agent is the studio's one app, with its panels","body":"The README starts with what Nova Agent is now (every former Nova app as a\npanel, on the studio PC and online for phones), a table of the panels with\ntheir addresses and code, how signing in works on the PC, and the new\nproject layout. Each panel's guide in docs/apps/ loses its old repo's\nbadges, clone and deploy steps and suite tables, says where the panel\nlives, and its pictures point at the right place (every link checked).\nStudio's GIFs move here from Nova Bot. The Nova Manual is rebuilt."},{"hash":"4b86f1f","date":"2026-10-07T23:33:47+01:00","subject":"Portal is Studio, Nova Portal is Crew, and the suite is Nova Agent","body":"- Renamed everywhere in Nova Agent: the code, its page, the panels, the\n  docs and the chat's instructions. On phones, notifications and the\n  installed app say Nova Agent.\n- Nova Agent's launcher lists its panels (Chat, Studio, Crew, Calendar,\n  Notes, Index, Observatory, Lossless audio), which all open inside it from\n  this computer, and Services and admin (Nova Bot, the Visualizer, Admin,\n  All links, the code).\n- On the studio PC, Studio's sign-in is your own account (the shared studio\n  password field is hidden there).\nChecked in a browser on a test copy: every panel opens inside Nova Agent,\nand signed out, Studio and Crew show their sign-in."},{"hash":"d3b02ec","date":"2026-10-07T23:29:25+01:00","subject":"One copy of what the panels share; Studio at /studio/, Crew at /crew/, Index at /index/","body":"- web/shared: the themes, sounds, the Portal badge and the Nova Manual,\n  once, instead of a copy in every app (4-5 copies each before). Nova\n  Agent serves it at /shared/ and no longer fetches the themes from Nova\n  Bot.\n- Studio (was Portal) lives at /studio/, Crew (was Nova Portal) at\n  /crew/ and Index (was at /app/memory/) at /index/; every link between\n  them follows. /app/memory/ redirects. The worker API paths (/app/api,\n  /auth, /staff) are unchanged.\n- Calendar's and Notes' offline helpers no longer list the shared files."},{"hash":"fef653e","date":"2026-10-07T23:27:20+01:00","subject":"Panels laid out: Studio (was Portal), Crew (was Nova Portal), Index…","body":"- web/studio: Portal's staff app, now Nova Agent's Studio panel\n- web/crew: Nova Portal's app (sign-in, me, crew, invites), now the Crew\n  panel, with the planet avatar generator beside it\n- web/index, web/calendar, web/notes, web/observatory: the panels\n- Each app's README and pictures move to docs/apps/<panel>\n- The manual and badge scripts move to scripts/, and the Observatory's\n  scanning tools to scripts/observatory (npm run observatory:scan,\n  :capture, :build), writing into web/observatory as before\n- Calendar's and Notes' own deploy configs (their separate workers.dev\n  sites) are dropped: they're panels now\nPaths inside the panels are fixed up next."},{"hash":"8d2427f","date":"2026-10-07T23:23:35+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent takes in Nova Calendar (with its history), as web/calendar","body":"git-subtree-dir: web/calendar\ngit-subtree-mainline: 851d7a41538174d4f19c4c84b151b36d054e9809\ngit-subtree-split: e57c424622432ebd6c49b6758517f0998c3a40aa"},{"hash":"e57c424","date":"2026-10-07T16:31:15+01:00","subject":"The Nova Manual: refreshed with today's changes","body":""},{"hash":"bef7cda","date":"2026-10-07T16:29:37+01:00","subject":"The Nova Manual, beside the badge","body":"The book button next to the Portal badge opens the Nova Manual: every\nNova app's guide, how it's built, its history and what's new, with\nsearch. js/nova-manual.js and its pages are copies from Nova Portal\n(scripts/build-manual.mjs); the service worker caches them (v7)."},{"hash":"dbe549a","date":"2026-10-07T02:01:05+01:00","subject":"Nova Portal badge: Connect as me in Nova Agent","body":""},{"hash":"8839341","date":"2026-10-07T01:50:07+01:00","subject":"The Nova Portal badge in the top bar (Connect once in Nova Portal)","body":""},{"hash":"361e2e2","date":"2026-10-07T01:34:31+01:00","subject":"README: new screenshots, an add-a-note-card demo, Sound, Links and fit to the window","body":"Fresh screenshots of the month, a day card, the note card and day card\neditors and three themes, all with made-up cards; fit-to-window shots\nat about 900 × 600 and 430 × 600 with ?embed=1; a GIF of adding a note\ncard; and sections on the Sound button, the Links button and how Nova\nAgent builds the calendar in."},{"hash":"07b0820","date":"2026-10-06T23:17:00+01:00","subject":"Fit to the window when shown inside another app","body":"Inside Nova Agent (or with ?embed=1) the calendar fills exactly the space it's\ngiven: a slim header, month rows that share the height, the selected day\nbeside or below with its own scroll, and no footer or legend."},{"hash":"4c636ce","date":"2026-10-06T23:10:50+01:00","subject":"Sound effects, with a Sound button at the top","body":""},{"hash":"755ec37","date":"2026-10-06T21:32:46+01:00","subject":"A locked Links button: every Nova suite address","body":""},{"hash":"9c8e85a","date":"2026-10-06T18:22:19+01:00","subject":"Rename Nova Task to Nova Calendar and make it an installable app","body":"New name throughout (saved data from Nova Task is picked up\nautomatically), a crescent-moon C icon and launch screen, a manifest\nwith New note card / New day card launcher shortcuts, offline support,\nand Cloudflare hosting at https://nova-calendar.novacane-studio.workers.dev"},{"hash":"992a091","date":"2026-10-06T15:52:52+01:00","subject":"Nova Task: a cosmic calendar of note cards and day cards","body":""}],"work":[],"workCount":0,"workStat":""}},{"id":"notes","name":"Notes","colour":"#FF8CC6","glyph":"✎","where":"A Nova Agent panel","links":[["Open Notes","http://localhost:4545/notes/"]],"repo":"na","shared":"","tagline":"A note editor that writes from the centre of the universe outwards.","intro":"<blockquote><strong>A Nova Agent panel.</strong> Its code is in <code>web/notes/</code> in Nova Agent&#39;s repo, and it opens inside Nova Agent at <code>/notes/</code>. Online, Nova Bot serves it at the same address.</blockquote>\n<p>Google Docs–style writing in the Novacane cosmic look: centred by default, six colour themes, soft cosmic sounds, import from Word, HTML, Markdown and text, and send it all to Google Docs.</p>\n<h4>✦ <a href=\"https://novacane-worker.novacane-studio.workers.dev/notes/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open Notes</a> ✦</h4>\n<p>Works in any modern browser · install it as an app · works offline · also built into Nova Agent</p>","guide":[{"id":"what-it-does-0","title":"What it does","html":"<p><strong>Writes like Google Docs</strong></p>\n<ul><li><strong>Menus and a toolbar</strong> you already know: File, Edit, View, Insert, Format, Tools and Help, with undo, redo, print, zoom, styles, fonts, sizes, colours and highlights.</li><li><strong>Paragraph styles:</strong> Title, Subtitle, Heading 1–3, Normal text, Quote and Code.</li><li><strong>Lists:</strong> bulleted, numbered and <strong>checklists</strong> you tick with a click; indent and outdent.</li><li><strong>Tables</strong> (pick a size, then add or remove rows and columns), <strong>pictures</strong> (upload, paste or drop, then resize and align), <strong>links</strong>, horizontal lines and <strong>page breaks</strong>.</li><li><strong>Find and replace</strong> (match case, whole words), <strong>word count</strong>, a live <strong>outline</strong> of your headings, and <strong>undo that remembers everything</strong>, including the tools the browser forgets.</li><li><strong>Shortcuts as you type:</strong> <code>#</code> heading, <code>-</code> list, <code>1.</code> numbered list, <code>[]</code> checklist, <code>&gt;</code> quote and <code>---</code> for a line. Every Google Docs keyboard shortcut you&#39;d expect is there too (press Ctrl+/).</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Centred by default.</strong> Everything you write (headings, paragraphs, lists and tables) sits in the middle of the page until you choose otherwise. Exports keep it that way.</p>\n<p><strong>In and out</strong></p>\n<ul><li><strong>Import</strong> Word (<code>.docx</code>), web pages (<code>.html</code>), Markdown (<code>.md</code>) and text (<code>.txt</code>): use <em>File → Import</em> or drop files onto the window. Text pasted from Google Docs or the web is cleaned up as it lands.</li><li><strong>Export</strong> to Google Docs, Word (<code>.doc</code>), a web page, Markdown, plain text or PDF (print), or a <code>.json</code> backup of one note or all of them.</li><li><strong>Google Docs</strong>, two ways:</li><li class=\"sub\"><strong>Copy &amp; paste (no set-up):</strong> copies the note with its styling and opens a new Google Doc; press Ctrl+V.</li><li class=\"sub\"><strong>Save to Google Drive (one click once set up):</strong> signs in with Google, creates a real Google Doc, and updates that same Doc each time you save the note again.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Looks and sounds the part</strong></p>\n<ul><li><strong>Six themes</strong> from Nova Agent: Novacane (magenta), Solar Flare (red-orange), Pulsar (cyan), Aurora (green and violet), Eclipse (gold) and Quasar (ultraviolet).</li><li><strong>Two page styles:</strong> <em>Cosmic</em> (a glowing glass page among twinkling stars) and <em>Paper</em> (white, exactly how the note exports and prints).</li><li><strong>Sound effects:</strong> gentle bells and sparkles as you work (see below).</li><li><strong>Focus mode,</strong> a pageless view, zoom, and a layout that works on phones and tablets.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Private by default.</strong> Notes are saved in your browser (IndexedDB) as you type. Nothing leaves it unless you export it or send it to Google Docs.</p>","text":"Writes like Google Docs Menus and a toolbar you already know: File, Edit, View, Insert, Format, Tools and Help, with undo, redo, print, zoom, styles, fonts, sizes, colours and highlights. Paragraph styles: Title, Subtitle, Heading 1–3, Normal text, Quote and Code. Lists: bulleted, numbered and checklists you tick with a click; indent and outdent. Tables (pick a size, then add or remove rows and columns), pictures (upload, paste or drop, then resize and align), links , horizontal lines and page breaks . Find and replace (match case, whole words), word count , a live outline of your headings, and undo that remembers everything , including the tools the browser forgets. Shortcuts as you type: # heading, - list, 1. numbered list, [] checklist, > quote and --- for a line. Every Google Docs keyboard shortcut you'd expect is there too (press Ctrl+/). Centred by default. Everything you write (headings, paragraphs, lists and tables) sits in the middle of the page until you choose otherwise. Exports keep it that way. In and out Import Word ( .docx ), web pages ( .html ), Markdown ( .md ) and text ( .txt ): use File → Import or drop files onto the window. Text pasted from Google Docs or the web is cleaned up as it lands. Export to Google Docs, Word ( .doc ), a web page, Markdown, plain text or PDF (print), or a .json backup of one note or all of them. Google Docs , two ways: Copy & paste (no set-up): copies the note with its styling and opens a new Google Doc; press Ctrl+V. Save to Google Drive (one click once set up): signs in with Google, creates a real Google Doc, and updates that same Doc each time you save the note again. Looks and sounds the part Six themes from Nova Agent: Novacane (magenta), Solar Flare (red-orange), Pulsar (cyan), Aurora (green and violet), Eclipse (gold) and Quasar (ultraviolet). Two page styles: Cosmic (a glowing glass page among twinkling stars) and Paper (white, exactly how the note exports and prints). Sound effects: gentle bells and sparkles as you work (see below). Focus mode, a pageless view, zoom, and a layout that works on phones and tablets. Private by default. Notes are saved in your browser (IndexedDB) as you type. Nothing leaves it unless you export it or send it to Google Docs."},{"id":"sound-effects-1","title":"Sound effects","html":"<p>Every press makes a soft cosmic sound: a tap, a menu opening, a dialog closing, an export sending, a note deleting. They&#39;re made live in the browser with the Web Audio API (there are no sound files), tuned to one pentatonic scale so they sound like one family, and kept quiet.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>On or off:</strong> <em>View → Sound effects</em>. It&#39;s ticked while they&#39;re on, and plays a little chime when you switch.</li><li><strong>Remembered</strong> on each device.</li><li><strong>Shared:</strong> the same <code>js/sfx.js</code> makes the sounds in Calendar and Observatory too.</li></ul>","text":"Every press makes a soft cosmic sound: a tap, a menu opening, a dialog closing, an export sending, a note deleting. They're made live in the browser with the Web Audio API (there are no sound files), tuned to one pentatonic scale so they sound like one family, and kept quiet. On or off: View → Sound effects . It's ticked while they're on, and plays a little chime when you switch. Remembered on each device. Shared: the same js/sfx.js makes the sounds in Calendar and Observatory too."},{"id":"inside-nova-agent-2","title":"Inside Nova Agent","html":"<p><a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-agent\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Nova Agent</a>, the studio computer&#39;s helper, serves its own copy of Notes at <strong><code>/notes/</code></strong> (for example <code>http://localhost:4545/notes/</code>) whenever it&#39;s running.</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th>On the web</th><th>Inside Nova Agent</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Address</td><td>novacane-worker.novacane-studio.workers.dev/notes/</td><td><code>/notes/</code> on Nova Agent</td></tr><tr><td>Where Local notes are kept</td><td>In that browser</td><td>On the studio computer, separate from the web app&#39;s</td></tr><tr><td>Shared notes</td><td>The team&#39;s, kept by Nova Bot</td><td>The same team notes</td></tr><tr><td>Privacy-minded browsers</td><td>May limit what a website saves</td><td>Fine: it&#39;s part of Nova Agent</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","text":"Nova Agent , the studio computer's helper, serves its own copy of Notes at /notes/ (for example http://localhost:4545/notes/ ) whenever it's running. On the web Inside Nova Agent Address novacane-worker.novacane-studio.workers.dev/notes/ /notes/ on Nova Agent Where Local notes are kept In that browser On the studio computer, separate from the web app's Shared notes The team's, kept by Nova Bot The same team notes Privacy-minded browsers May limit what a website saves Fine: it's part of Nova Agent"},{"id":"keyboard-shortcuts-3","title":"Keyboard shortcuts","html":"<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bold / italic / underline</td><td>Ctrl B / I / U</td></tr><tr><td>Strikethrough</td><td>Alt Shift 5</td></tr><tr><td>Normal text / Heading 1–3</td><td>Ctrl Alt 0–3</td></tr><tr><td>Left / centre / right / justify</td><td>Ctrl Shift L / E / R / J</td></tr><tr><td>Numbered / bulleted / checklist</td><td>Ctrl Shift 7 / 8 / 9</td></tr><tr><td>Link</td><td>Ctrl K</td></tr><tr><td>Find and replace</td><td>Ctrl H</td></tr><tr><td>Word count</td><td>Ctrl Shift C</td></tr><tr><td>Page break</td><td>Ctrl Enter</td></tr><tr><td>New note · Import · Print</td><td>Ctrl Alt N · Ctrl O · Ctrl P</td></tr><tr><td>Focus mode</td><td>Ctrl Shift F</td></tr><tr><td>Every shortcut</td><td>Ctrl /</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","text":"Bold / italic / underline Ctrl B / I / U Strikethrough Alt Shift 5 Normal text / Heading 1–3 Ctrl Alt 0–3 Left / centre / right / justify Ctrl Shift L / E / R / J Numbered / bulleted / checklist Ctrl Shift 7 / 8 / 9 Link Ctrl K Find and replace Ctrl H Word count Ctrl Shift C Page break Ctrl Enter New note · Import · Print Ctrl Alt N · Ctrl O · Ctrl P Focus mode Ctrl Shift F Every shortcut Ctrl /"}],"built":[{"id":"how-it-works-0","title":"How it works","html":"<pre><code>flowchart LR\n  subgraph Browser\n    E[editor.js&lt;br/&gt;contenteditable page,&lt;br/&gt;own undo history] --&gt; A[app.js&lt;br/&gt;menus, toolbar,&lt;br/&gt;library, dialogs]\n    A --&gt; S[(store.js&lt;br/&gt;IndexedDB)]\n    A --&gt; C[convert.js&lt;br/&gt;clean · Markdown ·&lt;br/&gt;styled export]\n    X[sfx.js&lt;br/&gt;Web Audio sounds] -.-&gt; A\n  end\n  F[.docx · .html · .md · .txt] -- import --&gt; C\n  C -- copy + docs.new --&gt; G[Google Docs]\n  C -- google.js&lt;br/&gt;Drive API, HTML → Doc --&gt; G\n  C -- download --&gt; D[.doc · .html · .md · .txt · PDF]</code></pre>\n<ul><li><strong><code>editor.js</code></strong>: the writing surface. It handles commands and paragraph styles, lists and checklists, tables, pictures, find and replace, and Markdown-style shortcuts. Undo works from snapshots of the page and selection, so every change can be undone.</li><li><strong><code>convert.js</code></strong>: cleans pasted and imported HTML down to what the editor understands, converts Markdown both ways, and builds the <strong>styled export</strong>: every block is inline-styled in the current theme&#39;s colours, made deep enough to read on white, so Google Docs and Word keep the look and the centring.</li><li><strong><code>google.js</code></strong>: the clipboard route (rich HTML plus plain text) and the Drive route (Google Identity Services token → multipart upload that Drive converts to a Google Doc, then <code>PATCH</code> to update it).</li><li><strong><code>store.js</code></strong>: notes in IndexedDB (falling back to localStorage), settings, backup and restore.</li><li><strong><code>sfx.js</code></strong>: Nova Agent&#39;s sound effects. One listener works out what kind of thing was pressed and plays the matching sound; an element can choose its own with <code>data-sfx</code>.</li><li><strong><code>themes.js</code></strong> and <strong><code>backdrop.js</code></strong>: Nova Agent&#39;s colour themes and the star field, shared with <a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-calendar\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Calendar</a>.</li></ul>","text":"flowchart LR subgraph Browser E[editor.js<br/>contenteditable page,<br/>own undo history] --> A[app.js<br/>menus, toolbar,<br/>library, dialogs] A --> S[(store.js<br/>IndexedDB)] A --> C[convert.js<br/>clean · Markdown ·<br/>styled export] X[sfx.js<br/>Web Audio sounds] -.-> A end F[.docx · .html · .md · .txt] -- import --> C C -- copy + docs.new --> G[Google Docs] C -- google.js<br/>Drive API, HTML → Doc --> G C -- download --> D[.doc · .html · .md · .txt · PDF] editor.js : the writing surface. It handles commands and paragraph styles, lists and checklists, tables, pictures, find and replace, and Markdown-style shortcuts. Undo works from snapshots of the page and selection, so every change can be undone. convert.js : cleans pasted and imported HTML down to what the editor understands, converts Markdown both ways, and builds the styled export : every block is inline-styled in the current theme's colours, made deep enough to read on white, so Google Docs and Word keep the look and the centring. google.js : the clipboard route (rich HTML plus plain text) and the Drive route (Google Identity Services token → multipart upload that Drive converts to a Google Doc, then PATCH to update it). store.js : notes in IndexedDB (falling back to localStorage), settings, backup and restore. sfx.js : Nova Agent's sound effects. One listener works out what kind of thing was pressed and plays the matching sound; an element can choose its own with data-sfx . themes.js and backdrop.js : Nova Agent's colour themes and the star field, shared with Calendar ."}],"news":[{"id":"what-s-new-0","title":"What's new","html":"<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>👥 <strong>Shared and Local notes</strong></td><td><strong>Shared</strong> notes are the whole team&#39;s: everyone signed in with Portal sees and edits them, on every device, and changes show up for the others within seconds. <strong>Local</strong> notes stay only on this device. Tap <strong>Local / Shared</strong> by &quot;Saved&quot; to move a note between the two (with Undo), and use <strong>All · Shared · Local</strong> above the list to pick what you see. New notes start Shared when you&#39;re signed in (Local when you&#39;re signed out or looking at Local). If two people change a shared note at the same time, both versions are kept (&quot;… (conflicted copy)&quot;).</td></tr><tr><td>🔔 <strong>Sound effects</strong></td><td>Soft cosmic sounds on every action. Switch them off or on in <strong>View → Sound effects</strong>.</td></tr><tr><td>🔒 <strong>All Nova Agent links</strong></td><td><strong>Help → 🔒 All Nova Agent links</strong> opens the password-protected page with every Nova Agent address, live and testing.</td></tr><tr><td>✦ <strong>Inside Nova Agent</strong></td><td>Nova Agent serves its own copy at <code>/notes/</code>, so privacy-minded browsers don&#39;t block it there. Notes written there are kept on the studio computer.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","text":"👥 Shared and Local notes Shared notes are the whole team's: everyone signed in with Portal sees and edits them, on every device, and changes show up for the others within seconds. Local notes stay only on this device. Tap Local / Shared by \"Saved\" to move a note between the two (with Undo), and use All · Shared · Local above the list to pick what you see. New notes start Shared when you're signed in (Local when you're signed out or looking at Local). If two people change a shared note at the same time, both versions are kept (\"… (conflicted copy)\"). 🔔 Sound effects Soft cosmic sounds on every action. Switch them off or on in View → Sound effects . 🔒 All Nova Agent links Help → 🔒 All Nova Agent links opens the password-protected page with every Nova Agent address, live and testing. ✦ Inside Nova Agent Nova Agent serves its own copy at /notes/ , so privacy-minded browsers don't block it there. Notes written there are kept on the studio computer."}],"history":{"total":27,"first":"2026-10-06T15:46:53+01:00","commits":[{"hash":"f741f8a","date":"2026-10-09T17:41:59+01:00","subject":"Notes: new notes start Shared when signed in (Local only when signed out or on the Local tab)","body":""},{"hash":"b9eb764","date":"2026-10-09T03:19:20+01:00","subject":"Every window size usable; the lower part of the window brings up the bar; Notes stays on screen","body":"Phone layout only below 481px tall (short computer windows keep the computer layout, tighter).\nNarrower computer windows: slimmer columns, a shorter New button, smaller tool buttons. Short\nones: slimmer header, one swipeable row of suggestions, smaller bars. Tablets: the bar in one\ncentred row. The column titles' grid applies on computers only (phones keep their own header).\nThe bottom 14% of the window brings the bar up. Notes inside Nova Agent: its toolbar wraps, the\npage starts as tall as the window, the outline's lines end with an ellipsis."},{"hash":"263cf4f","date":"2026-10-09T02:31:27+01:00","subject":"Cosmic icons, one theme for everything, planet colours, smart top bar, status line","body":"Icons: a cosmic set, each with its own colour (mixed with the theme), sky and shape; Talk to\nNova Agent, Quests and Missions have their own. look.js: one theme for every panel (or each its\nown), and colour everything from your planet. Typing hides the panels bar. The top bar: Auto,\nAlways shown or Always hidden. The status line under the bar: Panels button (the top one is\ngone), version and build, what changed lately for the part of the bar you point at, on and off\ntimes, recent activity and a 12-hour clock. Lossless audio's sounds come along."},{"hash":"8f8db84","date":"2026-10-08T23:34:26+01:00","subject":"Notes: Shared and Local notes","body":"Shared notes are the team's: kept by Nova Bot (/notes-api/), seen and edited by\neveryone signed in with Portal on every device, synced every 15 s and on focus,\nreadable offline with changes queued until the connection is back. Local notes\nstay on this device, as before. One tap by \"Saved\" moves a note between the two\n(with Undo); All · Shared · Local above the list, a badge on each note. Two\npeople changing a shared note at once keeps both (\"… (conflicted copy)\").\nOn the studio PC, Nova Agent passes /notes-api/ on with its sign-in.\nEvery existing Notes feature stays."},{"hash":"932c20c","date":"2026-10-08T16:59:59+01:00","subject":"Panels on phones: fit, lighter, less scrolling","body":"- Notes: one top bar (notes list, the note's name, Google Docs) and the menus;\n  the toolbar is one row you swipe, with the everyday tools (the rest stay in\n  the menus); 16px fields; no glass blur, grain or drifting background.\n- Observatory: a slim title, the numbers as a compact strip, each project as\n  one short row with a small drawn cover (no full-size screenshots on phones);\n  category chips in one row; no star map, no moving sky, no blur.\n- Calendar and Index: no glass blur or endless decorative motion on phones.\n- Lossless audio: snug margins, big buttons, 16px fields.\n- Visualizer: no error when the studio PC is off; fits a phone."},{"hash":"ed420d6","date":"2026-10-08T13:33:52+01:00","subject":"Portal is the one sign-in","body":"Signed out, the planet opens Portal's sign-in (in Nova Agent's viewer): no\nsign-in form of its own, and no Sign in with Google anywhere. Google is a\nconnection, not a way in: Portal's You page shows it (connected as whom), with\nSet up / Connect Google for admins (Admin → Google). Notes asks\n/auth/google-status for the studio's Google key."},{"hash":"4fabb4b","date":"2026-10-08T13:26:32+01:00","subject":"Sign in with Google, on the planet and in Portal; Notes uses the studio's Google","body":"- The planet's sign-in card and Portal's sign-in card get a Sign in with\n  Google button once an admin has set Google up (Admin → Google). Google's\n  page opens in a small window (full screen in the installed phone app) and\n  every panel follows when it's done.\n- On the studio PC, Nova Agent starts it (/auth/google): it makes up a\n  verifier, Nova Bot sends back a one-time code to /auth/google/done, and\n  Nova Agent swaps the two for its own sign-in (src/signin.ts).\n- Notes' Save to Google Docs uses the studio's Google key, with nothing to\n  set up; without it, a button opens Admin → Google."},{"hash":"0f31499","date":"2026-10-08T02:16:18+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'live-fixes' into sign-in","body":""},{"hash":"8ac9531","date":"2026-10-08T02:04:26+01:00","subject":"Lossless audio and Observatory as panels everywhere; docs at the real addresses","body":"- Lossless audio is served by Nova Agent at /lossless/ and opens inside it like\n  the other panels. Signalling and the relay setup come from Nova Bot (which now\n  serves it online too), so the other device can be anywhere; invite links point\n  at the online address. /lossless/ice lets Nova Agent's own page ask.\n- Observatory online asks for a Portal sign-in before showing the projects\n  (Nova Bot keeps them for signed-in staff).\n- Calendar's and Notes' guides link to their addresses on Nova Bot, not the old\n  standalone sites."},{"hash":"53332dc","date":"2026-10-08T02:04:14+01:00","subject":"Panels fit inside Nova Agent's viewer","body":"- While a panel is open, the panels strip shrinks to one row of small\n  switchers (services and admin as icons) and the viewer bar slims down:\n  the panel gets about 80px more height (431 → 511 at 1280×720). Only in\n  the side-by-side layout; stacked on a phone it's unchanged.\n- /shared/inside.js marks <html class=\"embed\"> when a panel is shown in a\n  frame (as Calendar's own embed.js already did), for frame-only fixes.\n- Notes in a frame: a slimmer two-row header (no kicker, smaller mark,\n  icon-only Import/Export/Google Docs below 1500px so the menus aren't\n  cut off), a tighter toolbar, and no word count in short frames. The\n  writing area goes from 215px to 377px tall at 1280×720.\n- Observatory in a frame: a smaller title block. Its stat numbers size to\n  their card (container units), so \"142,408\" no longer breaks in two.\n- Index in a frame: a slimmer tab bar."},{"hash":"9e079ef","date":"2026-10-08T00:47:29+01:00","subject":"Notes and Calendar show the current version after an update","body":"Their offline helpers answered from the cache first and refreshed in the\nbackground, so after every change you saw the previous version once (old\nnames, old behaviour). Online they now fetch fresh first and use the cache\nonly when offline. Inside Nova Agent, where nothing needs to work offline,\ntheir helper clears what it kept, unregisters and reloads the page."},{"hash":"100fb09","date":"2026-10-08T00:43:48+01:00","subject":"Plain names: everything is Nova Agent, and its panels are Portal, Portal, Calendar…","body":"Undoes the made-up names. \"Studio\" is Portal again and \"Crew\" is Portal again\n(only where the earlier rename had changed them; real uses of the words are\nkept). Every panel and feature drops \"Nova\": Portal, Portal, Calendar, Notes,\nIndex, Observatory, Missions, Quests and the Manual. \"Nova\" stays for Nova\nAgent itself, Nova Bot and Nova Club.\nThe original addresses are back: Portal at /app/, Portal at /portal/ and\nIndex at /app/memory/ (the panels live in web/portal, web/portal, web/index).\nNova Agent's own icons move to /agent/ to make room. /studio/, /crew/ and\n/index/ redirect, for anything that picked them up yesterday."},{"hash":"9aa754c","date":"2026-10-07T23:40:50+01:00","subject":"README: Nova Agent is the studio's one app, with its panels","body":"The README starts with what Nova Agent is now (every former Nova app as a\npanel, on the studio PC and online for phones), a table of the panels with\ntheir addresses and code, how signing in works on the PC, and the new\nproject layout. Each panel's guide in docs/apps/ loses its old repo's\nbadges, clone and deploy steps and suite tables, says where the panel\nlives, and its pictures point at the right place (every link checked).\nStudio's GIFs move here from Nova Bot. The Nova Manual is rebuilt."},{"hash":"4b86f1f","date":"2026-10-07T23:33:47+01:00","subject":"Portal is Studio, Nova Portal is Crew, and the suite is Nova Agent","body":"- Renamed everywhere in Nova Agent: the code, its page, the panels, the\n  docs and the chat's instructions. On phones, notifications and the\n  installed app say Nova Agent.\n- Nova Agent's launcher lists its panels (Chat, Studio, Crew, Calendar,\n  Notes, Index, Observatory, Lossless audio), which all open inside it from\n  this computer, and Services and admin (Nova Bot, the Visualizer, Admin,\n  All links, the code).\n- On the studio PC, Studio's sign-in is your own account (the shared studio\n  password field is hidden there).\nChecked in a browser on a test copy: every panel opens inside Nova Agent,\nand signed out, Studio and Crew show their sign-in."},{"hash":"d3b02ec","date":"2026-10-07T23:29:25+01:00","subject":"One copy of what the panels share; Studio at /studio/, Crew at /crew/, Index at /index/","body":"- web/shared: the themes, sounds, the Portal badge and the Nova Manual,\n  once, instead of a copy in every app (4-5 copies each before). Nova\n  Agent serves it at /shared/ and no longer fetches the themes from Nova\n  Bot.\n- Studio (was Portal) lives at /studio/, Crew (was Nova Portal) at\n  /crew/ and Index (was at /app/memory/) at /index/; every link between\n  them follows. /app/memory/ redirects. The worker API paths (/app/api,\n  /auth, /staff) are unchanged.\n- Calendar's and Notes' offline helpers no longer list the shared files."},{"hash":"fef653e","date":"2026-10-07T23:27:20+01:00","subject":"Panels laid out: Studio (was Portal), Crew (was Nova Portal), Index…","body":"- web/studio: Portal's staff app, now Nova Agent's Studio panel\n- web/crew: Nova Portal's app (sign-in, me, crew, invites), now the Crew\n  panel, with the planet avatar generator beside it\n- web/index, web/calendar, web/notes, web/observatory: the panels\n- Each app's README and pictures move to docs/apps/<panel>\n- The manual and badge scripts move to scripts/, and the Observatory's\n  scanning tools to scripts/observatory (npm run observatory:scan,\n  :capture, :build), writing into web/observatory as before\n- Calendar's and Notes' own deploy configs (their separate workers.dev\n  sites) are dropped: they're panels now\nPaths inside the panels are fixed up next."},{"hash":"4ea0638","date":"2026-10-07T23:23:36+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent takes in Nova Notes (with its history), as web/notes","body":"git-subtree-dir: web/notes\ngit-subtree-mainline: 8d2427fdf1afc33e56967b85d00ad060811f104f\ngit-subtree-split: df4f557e8b3d79cc58b6de13712430abffef58e8"},{"hash":"df4f557","date":"2026-10-07T16:31:18+01:00","subject":"The Nova Manual: refreshed with today's changes","body":""},{"hash":"8a13755","date":"2026-10-07T16:30:13+01:00","subject":"The Nova Manual, beside the badge","body":"The book button next to the Portal badge opens the Nova Manual: every\nNova app's guide, how it's built, its history and what's new, with\nsearch. js/nova-manual.js and its pages are copies from Nova Portal;\nthe service worker caches them (v6)."},{"hash":"8f0d4f5","date":"2026-10-07T02:01:05+01:00","subject":"Nova Portal badge: Connect as me in Nova Agent","body":""},{"hash":"8573aa3","date":"2026-10-07T01:50:12+01:00","subject":"The Nova Portal badge in the top bar (Connect once in Nova Portal)","body":""},{"hash":"bc0b45e","date":"2026-10-07T01:34:22+01:00","subject":"README: new screenshots, a typing demo, sound effects and Nova Agent","body":"Fresh screenshots from a new browser with the welcome note and two\nmade-up notes, a GIF of the #, - and [] shortcuts writing a centred\nnote, and sections for View → Sound effects, Help → All Nova suite\nlinks and the copy Nova Agent serves at /notes/. The old MP4 demo\nis gone; the README shows the GIF only."},{"hash":"646698c","date":"2026-10-06T23:10:46+01:00","subject":"Sound effects, with a switch in the View menu","body":""},{"hash":"16aeab4","date":"2026-10-06T21:32:30+01:00","subject":"Help menu: a locked link to every Nova suite address","body":""},{"hash":"cc543e3","date":"2026-10-06T18:23:23+01:00","subject":"Nova Task is now Nova Calendar","body":"Update the name and links to the renamed repo\n(https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-calendar)."},{"hash":"519310e","date":"2026-10-06T16:02:32+01:00","subject":"Make Nova Notes an installable web app","body":"Add a manifest, offline service worker, the cosmic N app icon and\nlaunch screen, an Install button, a New note shortcut, share-to-note\nand opening files with the app, plus Cloudflare hosting with security\nheaders. Live at https://nova-notes.novacane-studio.workers.dev"},{"hash":"739d47a","date":"2026-10-06T15:46:53+01:00","subject":"Nova Notes: a cosmic note editor for the Nova suite","body":"Google Docs-style rich text editing in the Novacane look, centred by\ndefault, with six colour themes, Cosmic and Paper page styles, import\nfrom Word/HTML/Markdown/text, export to Google Docs, Word, HTML,\nMarkdown, text and PDF, and notes saved in the browser."}],"work":[{"state":"changed","file":"web/notes/js/app.js"}],"workCount":1,"workStat":"1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)"}},{"id":"index","name":"Index","colour":"#5CFFC0","glyph":"≡","where":"A Nova Agent panel; online too","links":[["Open Index","http://localhost:4545/app/memory/"]],"repo":"na","shared":"","tagline":"Everything Nova Agent remembers, in one place.","intro":"<blockquote><strong>A Nova Agent panel.</strong> Its code is in <code>web/index/</code> in Nova Agent&#39;s repo, and it opens inside Nova Agent at <code>/app/memory/</code>. Online, Nova Bot serves it at the same address.</blockquote>\n<p>Browse it, watch it grow, fix a line, and say yes or no to what&#39;s been learned about customers.</p>\n<p>Every Nova app hands its conversations to one shared memory. A tiny set of tagged, one-line facts comes out, kept in small files by subject. Before replying, each app reads back only the few files that matter for that turn. Index is the window onto that memory.</p>\n<blockquote>The test for every fact: <strong>&quot;Would this still be true and useful in three months?&quot;</strong> If not, it isn&#39;t kept.</blockquote>\n<p>All the pictures here use made-up files and people.</p>\n<p>Open a file, add a fact, save; then approve a fact learned from a customer chat.</p>","guide":[{"id":"what-it-does-0","title":"What it does","html":"<h4>Browse</h4>\n<p>Studio, staff and customer files as cards, grouped by who they&#39;re about, with counts at the top (tap one to jump to it). The <strong>scope chips</strong> (All, Studio, Staff, Customers) narrow it down, and <strong>search</strong> looks through names, aliases, owners and descriptions, and inside the facts themselves: a card shows the line that matched, with your words lit up. <strong>+ New file</strong> starts one by hand.</p>\n<p>Search finds facts, not just file names. An open file: each fact with its tag pill, ready to edit.</p>\n<h4>Edit, safely</h4>\n<p>Open a file to change, add or delete a fact (and its tag), its description (the line the apps use to decide whether to read it) or its aliases. <strong>Save</strong> only goes through if nobody else has saved the file since you opened it. If someone has, you see both versions side by side, with the differences lit up, and can put your edit on top of theirs in one tap, or keep theirs.</p>\n<h4>Live and Approve</h4>\n<p>Live: what the suite just learned, and which app learned it. Approve: nothing about a customer is kept until someone says yes.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Live</strong> shows what the suite has just learned, and which app learned it (NovaBot, Nova Agent, Portal, Index). It checks every 20 seconds while it&#39;s on screen, and anything new glows as it arrives. Tap a row to open the file.</li><li><strong>Approve</strong> holds facts learned from customers. One tap approves, edits or rejects each one. Nothing about a customer is kept without a person saying yes.</li><li><strong>Options</strong>: the theme (shared with Portal), sound effects, refresh everything, open Portal and sign out. It installs as an app, with the suite&#39;s cosmic &quot;I&quot;.</li></ul>","text":"Browse Studio, staff and customer files as cards, grouped by who they're about, with counts at the top (tap one to jump to it). The scope chips (All, Studio, Staff, Customers) narrow it down, and search looks through names, aliases, owners and descriptions, and inside the facts themselves: a card shows the line that matched, with your words lit up. + New file starts one by hand. Search finds facts, not just file names. An open file: each fact with its tag pill, ready to edit. Edit, safely Open a file to change, add or delete a fact (and its tag), its description (the line the apps use to decide whether to read it) or its aliases. Save only goes through if nobody else has saved the file since you opened it. If someone has, you see both versions side by side, with the differences lit up, and can put your edit on top of theirs in one tap, or keep theirs. Live and Approve Live: what the suite just learned, and which app learned it. Approve: nothing about a customer is kept until someone says yes. Live shows what the suite has just learned, and which app learned it (NovaBot, Nova Agent, Portal, Index). It checks every 20 seconds while it's on screen, and anything new glows as it arrives. Tap a row to open the file. Approve holds facts learned from customers. One tap approves, edits or rejects each one. Nothing about a customer is kept without a person saying yes. Options : the theme (shared with Portal), sound effects, refresh everything, open Portal and sign out. It installs as an app, with the suite's cosmic \"I\"."}],"built":[{"id":"how-the-memory-works-0","title":"How the memory works","html":"<pre><code>- [stated]   said directly          &quot;prefers evening sessions&quot;\n- [observed] seen in what happened  &quot;usually books the Live Room&quot;\n- [inferred] a clear pattern        &quot;books in the run-up to releases&quot;</code></pre>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Scopes</strong></td><td><code>studio</code> (shared, including <code>public</code>, which customers may be told), <code>staff</code> (one set per staff member), <code>customer</code> (one set per client: their email, or a website chat until it&#39;s known)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Paths</strong></td><td><code>studio</code>, <code>public</code>, <code>profile</code>, <code>people/</code>, <code>topics/</code>, <code>areas/</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Learning</strong></td><td>In the background, so no reply ever waits. A small model pulls out only durable facts; each file is then rewritten with them folded in, never just added to. Files past about 3 KB are condensed. Card, bank and ID numbers are never kept.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Reading</strong></td><td>Each turn loads the studio file and the person&#39;s profile, plus at most three other files whose description or aliases match, within a budget of about 800 tokens</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Saving</strong></td><td>Every write carries the version it was based on; a clash returns the current file instead of overwriting it</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong>Who sees what</strong> is decided by the server, never by the app asking:</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Who</th><th>What they can see</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nova Agent (its key)</td><td>The studio&#39;s memory and staff memory; never customers&#39;</td></tr><tr><td>The website&#39;s NovaBot</td><td>Only that customer&#39;s own file and the public studio facts</td></tr><tr><td>Portal and Index, signed in</td><td>Everything, including approvals</td></tr><tr><td>Staff signed in with <a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-portal\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Portal</a></td><td>Staff who aren&#39;t admins: the studio&#39;s memory and their own; admins: everything</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Index signs in with <strong>Portal</strong>, the suite&#39;s one sign-in (&quot;✦ Sign in with Nova Portal&quot;), so each person sees what&#39;s theirs to see.</p>\n<p>The memory engine runs on Nova Bot&#39;s worker (<code>src/memory/</code> in <a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-bot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">nova-bot</a>): the store, extraction and the API. The memories live in its database, never in git. The full design is in docs/spec.md.</p>","text":"- [stated] said directly \"prefers evening sessions\" - [observed] seen in what happened \"usually books the Live Room\" - [inferred] a clear pattern \"books in the run-up to releases\" Scopes studio (shared, including public , which customers may be told), staff (one set per staff member), customer (one set per client: their email, or a website chat until it's known) Paths studio , public , profile , people/ , topics/ , areas/ Learning In the background, so no reply ever waits. A small model pulls out only durable facts; each file is then rewritten with them folded in, never just added to. Files past about 3 KB are condensed. Card, bank and ID numbers are never kept. Reading Each turn loads the studio file and the person's profile, plus at most three other files whose description or aliases match, within a budget of about 800 tokens Saving Every write carries the version it was based on; a clash returns the current file instead of overwriting it Who sees what is decided by the server, never by the app asking: Who What they can see Nova Agent (its key) The studio's memory and staff memory; never customers' The website's NovaBot Only that customer's own file and the public studio facts Portal and Index, signed in Everything, including approvals Staff signed in with Portal Staff who aren't admins: the studio's memory and their own; admins: everything Index signs in with Portal , the suite's one sign-in (\"✦ Sign in with Nova Portal\"), so each person sees what's theirs to see. The memory engine runs on Nova Bot's worker ( src/memory/ in nova-bot ): the store, extraction and the API. The memories live in its database, never in git. The full design is in docs/spec.md."}],"news":[],"history":{"total":17,"first":"2026-10-07T00:22:46+01:00","commits":[{"hash":"263cf4f","date":"2026-10-09T02:31:27+01:00","subject":"Cosmic icons, one theme for everything, planet colours, smart top bar, status line","body":"Icons: a cosmic set, each with its own colour (mixed with the theme), sky and shape; Talk to\nNova Agent, Quests and Missions have their own. look.js: one theme for every panel (or each its\nown), and colour everything from your planet. Typing hides the panels bar. The top bar: Auto,\nAlways shown or Always hidden. The status line under the bar: Panels button (the top one is\ngone), version and build, what changed lately for the part of the bar you point at, on and off\ntimes, recent activity and a 12-hour clock. Lossless audio's sounds come along."},{"hash":"932c20c","date":"2026-10-08T16:59:59+01:00","subject":"Panels on phones: fit, lighter, less scrolling","body":"- Notes: one top bar (notes list, the note's name, Google Docs) and the menus;\n  the toolbar is one row you swipe, with the everyday tools (the rest stay in\n  the menus); 16px fields; no glass blur, grain or drifting background.\n- Observatory: a slim title, the numbers as a compact strip, each project as\n  one short row with a small drawn cover (no full-size screenshots on phones);\n  category chips in one row; no star map, no moving sky, no blur.\n- Calendar and Index: no glass blur or endless decorative motion on phones.\n- Lossless audio: snug margins, big buttons, 16px fields.\n- Visualizer: no error when the studio PC is off; fits a phone."},{"hash":"3b87ce8","date":"2026-10-08T02:16:18+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'portal-merge' into sign-in","body":""},{"hash":"37073d2","date":"2026-10-08T02:15:25+01:00","subject":"One Portal: one staff app at /portal/","body":"Portal is gone as a separate panel. Portal is the one staff app: one header,\none tab bar with Portal's work tabs (Enquiries, Chats, Calendar, Quests,\nAlerts, NovaBot) plus You (your planet and profile; admins reach the crew\nand the admin pages from there). Portal's sign-in, setup and invite cards\nreplace Portal's old sign-in screen.\n- web/portal's scripts and styles move into web/portal (app.js, app.css,\n  ambient.js, options.js, suite.js). portal.js runs the page (who's signed\n  in, the address, the You tab) and starts the work tabs (window.NovaHub);\n  the tabs hand sign-outs back (window.PortalPage). Tabs follow the\n  address: /portal/?view=enquiries|chats|calendar|quests|alerts|bot|me|crew,\n  #nova opens Alerts, no ?view opens the starting tab from Options (which\n  can now be You). Tells the badge when sign-in changes (NovaPortal.changed).\n- portal.css is scoped to Portal's own parts (.pv) with p"},{"hash":"53332dc","date":"2026-10-08T02:04:14+01:00","subject":"Panels fit inside Nova Agent's viewer","body":"- While a panel is open, the panels strip shrinks to one row of small\n  switchers (services and admin as icons) and the viewer bar slims down:\n  the panel gets about 80px more height (431 → 511 at 1280×720). Only in\n  the side-by-side layout; stacked on a phone it's unchanged.\n- /shared/inside.js marks <html class=\"embed\"> when a panel is shown in a\n  frame (as Calendar's own embed.js already did), for frame-only fixes.\n- Notes in a frame: a slimmer two-row header (no kicker, smaller mark,\n  icon-only Import/Export/Google Docs below 1500px so the menus aren't\n  cut off), a tighter toolbar, and no word count in short frames. The\n  writing area goes from 215px to 377px tall at 1280×720.\n- Observatory in a frame: a smaller title block. Its stat numbers size to\n  their card (container units), so \"142,408\" no longer breaks in two.\n- Index in a frame: a slimmer tab bar."},{"hash":"326ecf9","date":"2026-10-08T01:33:59+01:00","subject":"Portal and Index: Portal is the one sign-in","body":"The shared-password box is gone from Portal's and Index's sign-in screens:\nsigned out, there's one button, to Portal, which brings you back to\n/app/ or /app/memory/ (not the old /studio/ and /index/). The guides\nand the Manual say the same."},{"hash":"100fb09","date":"2026-10-08T00:43:48+01:00","subject":"Plain names: everything is Nova Agent, and its panels are Portal, Portal, Calendar…","body":"Undoes the made-up names. \"Studio\" is Portal again and \"Crew\" is Portal again\n(only where the earlier rename had changed them; real uses of the words are\nkept). Every panel and feature drops \"Nova\": Portal, Portal, Calendar, Notes,\nIndex, Observatory, Missions, Quests and the Manual. \"Nova\" stays for Nova\nAgent itself, Nova Bot and Nova Club.\nThe original addresses are back: Portal at /app/, Portal at /portal/ and\nIndex at /app/memory/ (the panels live in web/portal, web/portal, web/index).\nNova Agent's own icons move to /agent/ to make room. /studio/, /crew/ and\n/index/ redirect, for anything that picked them up yesterday."},{"hash":"9aa754c","date":"2026-10-07T23:40:50+01:00","subject":"README: Nova Agent is the studio's one app, with its panels","body":"The README starts with what Nova Agent is now (every former Nova app as a\npanel, on the studio PC and online for phones), a table of the panels with\ntheir addresses and code, how signing in works on the PC, and the new\nproject layout. Each panel's guide in docs/apps/ loses its old repo's\nbadges, clone and deploy steps and suite tables, says where the panel\nlives, and its pictures point at the right place (every link checked).\nStudio's GIFs move here from Nova Bot. The Nova Manual is rebuilt."},{"hash":"4b86f1f","date":"2026-10-07T23:33:47+01:00","subject":"Portal is Studio, Nova Portal is Crew, and the suite is Nova Agent","body":"- Renamed everywhere in Nova Agent: the code, its page, the panels, the\n  docs and the chat's instructions. On phones, notifications and the\n  installed app say Nova Agent.\n- Nova Agent's launcher lists its panels (Chat, Studio, Crew, Calendar,\n  Notes, Index, Observatory, Lossless audio), which all open inside it from\n  this computer, and Services and admin (Nova Bot, the Visualizer, Admin,\n  All links, the code).\n- On the studio PC, Studio's sign-in is your own account (the shared studio\n  password field is hidden there).\nChecked in a browser on a test copy: every panel opens inside Nova Agent,\nand signed out, Studio and Crew show their sign-in."},{"hash":"d3b02ec","date":"2026-10-07T23:29:25+01:00","subject":"One copy of what the panels share; Studio at /studio/, Crew at /crew/, Index at /index/","body":"- web/shared: the themes, sounds, the Portal badge and the Nova Manual,\n  once, instead of a copy in every app (4-5 copies each before). Nova\n  Agent serves it at /shared/ and no longer fetches the themes from Nova\n  Bot.\n- Studio (was Portal) lives at /studio/, Crew (was Nova Portal) at\n  /crew/ and Index (was at /app/memory/) at /index/; every link between\n  them follows. /app/memory/ redirects. The worker API paths (/app/api,\n  /auth, /staff) are unchanged.\n- Calendar's and Notes' offline helpers no longer list the shared files."},{"hash":"fef653e","date":"2026-10-07T23:27:20+01:00","subject":"Panels laid out: Studio (was Portal), Crew (was Nova Portal), Index…","body":"- web/studio: Portal's staff app, now Nova Agent's Studio panel\n- web/crew: Nova Portal's app (sign-in, me, crew, invites), now the Crew\n  panel, with the planet avatar generator beside it\n- web/index, web/calendar, web/notes, web/observatory: the panels\n- Each app's README and pictures move to docs/apps/<panel>\n- The manual and badge scripts move to scripts/, and the Observatory's\n  scanning tools to scripts/observatory (npm run observatory:scan,\n  :capture, :build), writing into web/observatory as before\n- Calendar's and Notes' own deploy configs (their separate workers.dev\n  sites) are dropped: they're panels now\nPaths inside the panels are fixed up next."},{"hash":"d7b8800","date":"2026-10-07T23:23:36+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent takes in Nova Index (with its history), as web/index","body":"git-subtree-dir: web/index\ngit-subtree-mainline: 4ea063844af5a5cd7e39524bb794b0fc061b39a8\ngit-subtree-split: 7127214aa027363c9e126bc99b7068a143217074"},{"hash":"7127214","date":"2026-10-07T16:30:11+01:00","subject":"The Nova Manual, beside the badge","body":""},{"hash":"c7f1806","date":"2026-10-07T01:50:06+01:00","subject":"The Nova Portal badge in the top bar","body":""},{"hash":"4317639","date":"2026-10-07T01:35:40+01:00","subject":"Sign in with Nova Portal, and open straight to a file","body":"- \"✦ Sign in with Nova Portal\" on the sign-in screen\n- ?scope=&owner= open Browse on one person's or one scope's files\n- README: Portal sign-in is live"},{"hash":"5591755","date":"2026-10-07T01:33:23+01:00","subject":"README: Nova Index with screenshots and a walkthrough","body":"- Browse with the scope chips, an open file with tag pills, search finding a\n  fact, the conflict panel, Live and Approve, all with made-up files\n- A GIF: open a file, add a fact, save, then approve a customer's fact\n- Who sees what, including Nova Portal sign-in (coming): staff who aren't\n  admins see the studio's memory and their own; admins see everything\n- The build step is scripts/sync-apps.mjs"},{"hash":"d2de367","date":"2026-10-07T00:22:46+01:00","subject":"Nova Index: the Nova suite's memory, browsable","body":"Browse, edit and approve everything the Nova suite remembers: studio, staff\nand customer facts as small files of one-line facts, a live feed of what's\njust been learned, and the approval queue for customers' facts. Served by\nNova Bot's worker at /app/memory/ (with Portal's sign-in) and by Nova Agent."}],"work":[{"state":"changed","file":"docs/apps/index/spec.md"},{"state":"changed","file":"web/index/index.html"},{"state":"changed","file":"web/index/memory.css"},{"state":"changed","file":"web/index/memory.js"}],"workCount":4,"workStat":"4 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)"}},{"id":"observatory","name":"Observatory","colour":"#FFB86B","glyph":"✧","where":"A Nova Agent panel","links":[["Open Observatory","http://localhost:4545/observatory/"]],"repo":"na","shared":"","tagline":"Every project in one sky: a dashboard that measures your work on disk and shows it in screenshots and video.","intro":"<blockquote><strong>A Nova Agent panel.</strong> Its code is in <code>web/observatory/</code> in Nova Agent&#39;s repo, and it opens inside Nova Agent at <code>/observatory/</code>.</blockquote>\n<p>Always on inside Nova Agent at /observatory/ · or open index.html anywhere</p>\n<p>Observatory is a dashboard of everything being worked on. It&#39;s kept true by scanning the disk rather than by hand: one script measures every project, another opens each one in headless Chromium and records screenshots and a short demo video, and a static page shows the lot as project decks and a star map.</p>\n<p>The screenshots here come from the studio&#39;s own catalogue: Nova Agent, plus games, tools and experiments. They show project names, sizes and folder trees, and nothing personal.</p>","guide":[{"id":"what-it-does-0","title":"What it does","html":"<p>Each project gets a <strong>deck</strong> showing:</p>\n<ul><li>where it lives in the folder tree</li><li>its goal and vision, and what it does</li><li>its size on disk, project files, lines of code and languages</li><li>git state and last activity</li><li>screenshots and a demo video (or a generated cosmic cover)</li></ul>\n<p>And across all of them:</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Totals</strong></td><td>Lines of code, project files, size on disk, files, languages and last activity, with a language bar</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Search, filter and sort</strong></td><td>By name, goal, stack or path; by category; by recent activity and more</td></tr><tr><td><strong>A detailed view</strong></td><td>Each project&#39;s video, screenshots, folder tree, languages and facts</td></tr><tr><td><strong>A star map</strong></td><td>The whole folder structure, with every project as a star sized by its lines of code</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Six colour themes</strong></td><td>Shared with <a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-calendar\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Calendar</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-notes\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Notes</a></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Sound effects</strong></td><td>The shared Nova Agent sounds, with a switch in the header</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","text":"Each project gets a deck showing: where it lives in the folder tree its goal and vision, and what it does its size on disk, project files, lines of code and languages git state and last activity screenshots and a demo video (or a generated cosmic cover) And across all of them: Totals Lines of code, project files, size on disk, files, languages and last activity, with a language bar Search, filter and sort By name, goal, stack or path; by category; by recent activity and more A detailed view Each project's video, screenshots, folder tree, languages and facts A star map The whole folder structure, with every project as a star sized by its lines of code Six colour themes Shared with Calendar and Notes Sound effects The shared Nova Agent sounds, with a switch in the header"},{"id":"inside-nova-agent-1","title":"Inside Nova Agent","html":"<p><a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-agent\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Nova Agent</a> serves this folder at <strong><code>/observatory/</code></strong> (for example <code>http://localhost:4545/observatory/</code>) whenever it&#39;s running, so the Observatory is always on there with the latest scan. Nova Agent looks for it next to itself, in <code>../no</code>.</p>","text":"Nova Agent serves this folder at /observatory/ (for example http://localhost:4545/observatory/ ) whenever it's running, so the Observatory is always on there with the latest scan. Nova Agent looks for it next to itself, in ../no ."},{"id":"sound-effects-2","title":"Sound effects","html":"<p>Every press makes a soft cosmic sound, made live with the Web Audio API (no sound files) and kept quiet. The <strong>Sound on / Sound off</strong> switch beside <strong>🔒 All links</strong> turns them off and on, plays a little chime when it does, and is remembered on each device. The same <code>js/sfx.js</code> makes the sounds in Notes and Calendar.</p>","text":"Every press makes a soft cosmic sound, made live with the Web Audio API (no sound files) and kept quiet. The Sound on / Sound off switch beside 🔒 All links turns them off and on, plays a little chime when it does, and is remembered on each device. The same js/sfx.js makes the sounds in Notes and Calendar."}],"built":[{"id":"how-it-works-0","title":"How it works","html":"<pre><code>flowchart LR\n    CFG[projects.config.json&lt;br/&gt;the catalogue] --&gt; SCAN[scan.mjs]\n    CFG --&gt; CAP[capture.mjs]\n    DISK[(your projects&lt;br/&gt;on disk)] --&gt; SCAN\n    DISK --&gt; CAP\n    CAP --&gt;|Playwright + ffmpeg| MEDIA[media/&amp;lt;id&amp;gt;/&lt;br/&gt;shots + video]\n    MEDIA --&gt; SCAN\n    SCAN --&gt; DATA[data/projects.js&lt;br/&gt;data/projects.json]\n    DATA --&gt; PAGE[index.html&lt;br/&gt;js/observatory.js]\n    MEDIA --&gt; PAGE\n    PAGE -.-&gt;|served at /observatory/| AGENT[Nova Agent]</code></pre>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Job</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>projects.config.json</code></td><td>Your catalogue. It holds what a scan can&#39;t know: each project&#39;s name, goal, vision, features, category, theme, and how to show it. <strong>Add a project here.</strong> Git ignores it; start from <code>projects.config.example.json</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>scan.mjs</code></td><td>Measures each project on disk. Writes <code>data/projects.json</code> and <code>data/projects.js</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>capture.mjs</code></td><td>Drives headless Chromium (Playwright) and ffmpeg. Writes into <code>media//</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>index.html</code>, <code>css/</code>, <code>js/observatory.js</code></td><td>The page.</td></tr><tr><td><code>js/themes.js</code>, <code>js/cosmos.js</code>, <code>js/backdrop.js</code></td><td>Shared with Calendar: the colour themes, the generative space covers and the star backdrop.</td></tr><tr><td><code>js/sfx.js</code></td><td>The Nova Agent sound effects, shared with Notes and Calendar.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong>What counts as what in a scan:</strong></p>\n<ul><li><strong>On disk</strong> is everything, from <code>du</code>.</li><li><strong>Project files</strong> and <strong>lines of code</strong> leave out:</li><li class=\"sub\">dependencies and build output: <code>node_modules</code>, <code>build*</code>, <code>dist</code>, <code>.gradle</code>, <code>.godot</code> and so on</li><li class=\"sub\">vendored third-party code: <code>lib</code>, <code>deps</code>, <code>glad</code>, <code>Libs</code>, <code>vendor</code>, <code>thirdparty</code></li><li class=\"sub\">anything listed under <code>exclude</code> in the catalogue, such as copied-in SDL or cglm headers</li><li>Lines are counted only for code. Markdown, JSON, XML and config files don&#39;t count.</li></ul>\n<h4>Capture</h4>\n<p><strong>Capture modes</strong> (<code>capture.mode</code> in the catalogue):</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>page</code></td><td>Opens the project in Chromium and plays a short scripted demo, recording the screen. The project can be opened as a file, from a local static server (<code>serve</code>, with optional <code>mounts</code>), from the project&#39;s own Vite (<code>vite: true</code>) or from a <code>url</code>. The demo scripts are in <code>capture.mjs</code> under <code>SCRIPTS</code>.</td></tr><tr><td><code>images</code></td><td>Turns pictures already in the project into a Ken Burns slideshow video.</td></tr><tr><td><code>none</code></td><td>Shows a generated cosmic cover instead.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong>Safety:</strong> during capture, every request that leaves the machine is blocked, except Google Fonts, and every non-GET request is blocked too. A demo can type into a chat widget, but nothing can reach a live service.</p>\n<p><strong>Private projects:</strong> projects marked <code>&quot;private&quot;: true</code> are skipped unless you pass <code>--include-private</code>. Use it for anything whose pages can show personal data (Nova Agent&#39;s visualizer can show client names, so it&#39;s marked private in the example).</p>","text":"flowchart LR CFG[projects.config.json<br/>the catalogue] --> SCAN[scan.mjs] CFG --> CAP[capture.mjs] DISK[(your projects<br/>on disk)] --> SCAN DISK --> CAP CAP -->|Playwright + ffmpeg| MEDIA[media/<id>/<br/>shots + video] MEDIA --> SCAN SCAN --> DATA[data/projects.js<br/>data/projects.json] DATA --> PAGE[index.html<br/>js/observatory.js] MEDIA --> PAGE PAGE -.->|served at /observatory/| AGENT[Nova Agent] File Job projects.config.json Your catalogue. It holds what a scan can't know: each project's name, goal, vision, features, category, theme, and how to show it. Add a project here. Git ignores it; start from projects.config.example.json . scan.mjs Measures each project on disk. Writes data/projects.json and data/projects.js . capture.mjs Drives headless Chromium (Playwright) and ffmpeg. Writes into media// . index.html , css/ , js/observatory.js The page. js/themes.js , js/cosmos.js , js/backdrop.js Shared with Calendar: the colour themes, the generative space covers and the star backdrop. js/sfx.js The Nova Agent sound effects, shared with Notes and Calendar. What counts as what in a scan: On disk is everything, from du . Project files and lines of code leave out: dependencies and build output: node_modules , build* , dist , .gradle , .godot and so on vendored third-party code: lib , deps , glad , Libs , vendor , thirdparty anything listed under exclude in the catalogue, such as copied-in SDL or cglm headers Lines are counted only for code. Markdown, JSON, XML and config files don't count. Capture Capture modes ( capture.mode in the catalogue): Mode What it does page Opens the project in Chromium and plays a short scripted demo, recording the screen. The project can be opened as a file, from a local static server ( serve , with optional mounts ), from the project's own Vite ( vite: true ) or from a url . The demo scripts are in capture.mjs under SCRIPTS . images Turns pictures already in the project into a Ken Burns slideshow video. none Shows a generated cosmic cover instead. Safety: during capture, every request that leaves the machine is blocked, except Google Fonts, and every non-GET request is blocked too. A demo can type into a chat widget, but nothing can reach a live service. Private projects: projects marked \"private\": true are skipped unless you pass --include-private . Use it for anything whose pages can show personal data (Nova Agent's visualizer can show client names, so it's marked private in the example)."}],"news":[{"id":"what-s-new-0","title":"What's new","html":"<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>🔔 <strong>Sound switch</strong></td><td>Soft cosmic sound effects on every press. The <strong>Sound on / Sound off</strong> switch beside All links turns them off and on.</td></tr><tr><td>🔒 <strong>All links</strong></td><td>A pill in the header that opens the password-protected page with every Nova Agent address, live and testing.</td></tr><tr><td>✦ <strong>Served by Nova Agent</strong></td><td>Nova Agent serves it at <code>/observatory/</code>, so it&#39;s always on while Nova Agent is.</td></tr><tr><td>🧠 <strong>Index</strong></td><td>The suite&#39;s shared memory now has its own deck. Portal may join it later.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","text":"🔔 Sound switch Soft cosmic sound effects on every press. The Sound on / Sound off switch beside All links turns them off and on. 🔒 All links A pill in the header that opens the password-protected page with every Nova Agent address, live and testing. ✦ Served by Nova Agent Nova Agent serves it at /observatory/ , so it's always on while Nova Agent is. 🧠 Index The suite's shared memory now has its own deck. Portal may join it later."}],"history":{"total":22,"first":"2026-10-06T15:57:57+01:00","commits":[{"hash":"28ebf5d","date":"2026-10-10T02:44:33+01:00","subject":"Observatory: only the categories that have projects show as filters","body":""},{"hash":"ae32409","date":"2026-10-10T01:26:38+01:00","subject":"Observatory: more on screen, in Nova Agent's glass; Agent: \"Give me a goal\" sits last, by the box","body":"Observatory: the title, the six numbers and the links share one slim header (the colours and\nthe languages the next line), the search, filters and sort stay at the top as one row, and the\ndecks are tighter with a glowing glass edge, so a full row of decks shows straight away. Short\nwindows drop the summary line and the goal (both in each deck's details); phones get one small\nblock above the projects, with the numbers sliding sideways. Nothing removed.\nAgent's welcome: the suggestions, Today in music, then the hello (\"Give me a goal…\") at the\nbottom, next to where you type."},{"hash":"263cf4f","date":"2026-10-09T02:31:27+01:00","subject":"Cosmic icons, one theme for everything, planet colours, smart top bar, status line","body":"Icons: a cosmic set, each with its own colour (mixed with the theme), sky and shape; Talk to\nNova Agent, Quests and Missions have their own. look.js: one theme for every panel (or each its\nown), and colour everything from your planet. Typing hides the panels bar. The top bar: Auto,\nAlways shown or Always hidden. The status line under the bar: Panels button (the top one is\ngone), version and build, what changed lately for the part of the bar you point at, on and off\ntimes, recent activity and a 12-hour clock. Lossless audio's sounds come along."},{"hash":"932c20c","date":"2026-10-08T16:59:59+01:00","subject":"Panels on phones: fit, lighter, less scrolling","body":"- Notes: one top bar (notes list, the note's name, Google Docs) and the menus;\n  the toolbar is one row you swipe, with the everyday tools (the rest stay in\n  the menus); 16px fields; no glass blur, grain or drifting background.\n- Observatory: a slim title, the numbers as a compact strip, each project as\n  one short row with a small drawn cover (no full-size screenshots on phones);\n  category chips in one row; no star map, no moving sky, no blur.\n- Calendar and Index: no glass blur or endless decorative motion on phones.\n- Lossless audio: snug margins, big buttons, 16px fields.\n- Visualizer: no error when the studio PC is off; fits a phone."},{"hash":"0f31499","date":"2026-10-08T02:16:18+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'live-fixes' into sign-in","body":""},{"hash":"8ac9531","date":"2026-10-08T02:04:26+01:00","subject":"Lossless audio and Observatory as panels everywhere; docs at the real addresses","body":"- Lossless audio is served by Nova Agent at /lossless/ and opens inside it like\n  the other panels. Signalling and the relay setup come from Nova Bot (which now\n  serves it online too), so the other device can be anywhere; invite links point\n  at the online address. /lossless/ice lets Nova Agent's own page ask.\n- Observatory online asks for a Portal sign-in before showing the projects\n  (Nova Bot keeps them for signed-in staff).\n- Calendar's and Notes' guides link to their addresses on Nova Bot, not the old\n  standalone sites."},{"hash":"53332dc","date":"2026-10-08T02:04:14+01:00","subject":"Panels fit inside Nova Agent's viewer","body":"- While a panel is open, the panels strip shrinks to one row of small\n  switchers (services and admin as icons) and the viewer bar slims down:\n  the panel gets about 80px more height (431 → 511 at 1280×720). Only in\n  the side-by-side layout; stacked on a phone it's unchanged.\n- /shared/inside.js marks <html class=\"embed\"> when a panel is shown in a\n  frame (as Calendar's own embed.js already did), for frame-only fixes.\n- Notes in a frame: a slimmer two-row header (no kicker, smaller mark,\n  icon-only Import/Export/Google Docs below 1500px so the menus aren't\n  cut off), a tighter toolbar, and no word count in short frames. The\n  writing area goes from 215px to 377px tall at 1280×720.\n- Observatory in a frame: a smaller title block. Its stat numbers size to\n  their card (container units), so \"142,408\" no longer breaks in two.\n- Index in a frame: a slimmer tab bar."},{"hash":"100fb09","date":"2026-10-08T00:43:48+01:00","subject":"Plain names: everything is Nova Agent, and its panels are Portal, Portal, Calendar…","body":"Undoes the made-up names. \"Studio\" is Portal again and \"Crew\" is Portal again\n(only where the earlier rename had changed them; real uses of the words are\nkept). Every panel and feature drops \"Nova\": Portal, Portal, Calendar, Notes,\nIndex, Observatory, Missions, Quests and the Manual. \"Nova\" stays for Nova\nAgent itself, Nova Bot and Nova Club.\nThe original addresses are back: Portal at /app/, Portal at /portal/ and\nIndex at /app/memory/ (the panels live in web/portal, web/portal, web/index).\nNova Agent's own icons move to /agent/ to make room. /studio/, /crew/ and\n/index/ redirect, for anything that picked them up yesterday."},{"hash":"9aa754c","date":"2026-10-07T23:40:50+01:00","subject":"README: Nova Agent is the studio's one app, with its panels","body":"The README starts with what Nova Agent is now (every former Nova app as a\npanel, on the studio PC and online for phones), a table of the panels with\ntheir addresses and code, how signing in works on the PC, and the new\nproject layout. Each panel's guide in docs/apps/ loses its old repo's\nbadges, clone and deploy steps and suite tables, says where the panel\nlives, and its pictures point at the right place (every link checked).\nStudio's GIFs move here from Nova Bot. The Nova Manual is rebuilt."},{"hash":"4b86f1f","date":"2026-10-07T23:33:47+01:00","subject":"Portal is Studio, Nova Portal is Crew, and the suite is Nova Agent","body":"- Renamed everywhere in Nova Agent: the code, its page, the panels, the\n  docs and the chat's instructions. On phones, notifications and the\n  installed app say Nova Agent.\n- Nova Agent's launcher lists its panels (Chat, Studio, Crew, Calendar,\n  Notes, Index, Observatory, Lossless audio), which all open inside it from\n  this computer, and Services and admin (Nova Bot, the Visualizer, Admin,\n  All links, the code).\n- On the studio PC, Studio's sign-in is your own account (the shared studio\n  password field is hidden there).\nChecked in a browser on a test copy: every panel opens inside Nova Agent,\nand signed out, Studio and Crew show their sign-in."},{"hash":"d3b02ec","date":"2026-10-07T23:29:25+01:00","subject":"One copy of what the panels share; Studio at /studio/, Crew at /crew/, Index at /index/","body":"- web/shared: the themes, sounds, the Portal badge and the Nova Manual,\n  once, instead of a copy in every app (4-5 copies each before). Nova\n  Agent serves it at /shared/ and no longer fetches the themes from Nova\n  Bot.\n- Studio (was Portal) lives at /studio/, Crew (was Nova Portal) at\n  /crew/ and Index (was at /app/memory/) at /index/; every link between\n  them follows. /app/memory/ redirects. The worker API paths (/app/api,\n  /auth, /staff) are unchanged.\n- Calendar's and Notes' offline helpers no longer list the shared files."},{"hash":"fef653e","date":"2026-10-07T23:27:20+01:00","subject":"Panels laid out: Studio (was Portal), Crew (was Nova Portal), Index…","body":"- web/studio: Portal's staff app, now Nova Agent's Studio panel\n- web/crew: Nova Portal's app (sign-in, me, crew, invites), now the Crew\n  panel, with the planet avatar generator beside it\n- web/index, web/calendar, web/notes, web/observatory: the panels\n- Each app's README and pictures move to docs/apps/<panel>\n- The manual and badge scripts move to scripts/, and the Observatory's\n  scanning tools to scripts/observatory (npm run observatory:scan,\n  :capture, :build), writing into web/observatory as before\n- Calendar's and Notes' own deploy configs (their separate workers.dev\n  sites) are dropped: they're panels now\nPaths inside the panels are fixed up next."},{"hash":"1ec177b","date":"2026-10-07T23:23:37+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent takes in Nova Observatory (with its history), as web/observatory","body":"git-subtree-dir: web/observatory\ngit-subtree-mainline: d7b88000c2e0a7ba290b081327d3c9a8353d21c9\ngit-subtree-split: 1687028b1bfb772362f663103dd72b017826eaa5"},{"hash":"1687028","date":"2026-10-07T16:31:21+01:00","subject":"The Nova Manual: refreshed with today's changes","body":""},{"hash":"79e928f","date":"2026-10-07T16:30:16+01:00","subject":"The Nova Manual, beside the badge","body":"js/nova-manual.js and its pages are copies from Nova Portal\n(scripts/build-manual.mjs there)."},{"hash":"1f5052f","date":"2026-10-07T02:01:05+01:00","subject":"Nova Portal badge: Connect as me in Nova Agent","body":""},{"hash":"ae149c8","date":"2026-10-07T01:50:13+01:00","subject":"The Nova Portal badge in the header","body":""},{"hash":"b173664","date":"2026-10-07T01:34:40+01:00","subject":"README: new screenshots, a tour GIF, the Sound switch and Nova Agent","body":"Fresh overview, decks, project detail, folder tree and star map\nscreenshots from the current scan (now with Nova Index), a GIF that\nscrolls the overview and opens a project, and notes on the Sound\nswitch, the All links pill and Nova Agent serving it at /observatory/."},{"hash":"4b6ec2b","date":"2026-10-06T23:10:48+01:00","subject":"Sound effects, with a Sound switch beside All links","body":""},{"hash":"97aab97","date":"2026-10-06T21:32:33+01:00","subject":"A locked link to every Nova suite address","body":""},{"hash":"0412651","date":"2026-10-06T18:23:25+01:00","subject":"Nova Task is now Nova Calendar","body":"Update the name and links to the renamed repo\n(https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-calendar)."},{"hash":"7afacab","date":"2026-10-06T15:57:57+01:00","subject":"Nova Observatory: every project in one sky","body":""}],"work":[{"state":"changed","file":"scripts/observatory/capture.mjs"},{"state":"changed","file":"scripts/observatory/projects.config.example.json"}],"workCount":2,"workStat":"2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)"}},{"id":"bot","name":"Nova Bot","colour":"#5CE1FF","glyph":"◎","where":"On the website and Cloudflare: Nova Agent's back end","links":[["Admin pages","https://novacane-worker.novacane-studio.workers.dev/admin"]],"repo":"nb/novacane-worker","shared":"","tagline":"The front desk that never closes: a website assistant, a staff app and the engines behind Nova Agent, for Novacane Studios.","intro":"<p>Nova Bot runs on Cloudflare Workers for <a href=\"https://novacane.co.uk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Novacane Studios</a>, a recording studio in London. One Worker does four jobs:</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th>What it is</th><th>Where</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>✦ <strong>NovaBot</strong></td><td>The chat assistant on the studio&#39;s website. Answers questions with Claude and gets bookings ready, always with the deposit first</td><td><code>public/novabot.js</code>, <code>src/index.js</code></td></tr><tr><td>✦ <strong>Portal</strong></td><td>The staff app: enquiries, chats, a smart calendar, quests, alerts, a staff chat with NovaBot, sign-in, everyone&#39;s planet and the team</td><td>Nova Agent&#39;s Portal panel (copied into <code>public/portal/</code>), <code>src/app-page.js</code>, <code>src/portal/</code></td></tr><tr><td>✦ <strong>Admin pages</strong></td><td>Password-protected pages for referrals, enquiries, conversations, feedback, the booking system and the master list of links</td><td><code>src/admin.js</code></td></tr><tr><td>✦ <strong>Suite engines</strong></td><td>The memory behind <strong>Index</strong> and the sign-in behind <strong>Portal</strong>, shared by every Nova app</td><td><code>src/memory/</code>, <code>src/portal/</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>It comes with a <strong>sandbox</strong>, so you can run the whole thing on your own computer without any accounts.</p>\n<blockquote>Every screenshot and animation here was made with made-up data (Dana Hollis, Eric Mensah, Kai and friends, <code>example.com</code> addresses and <code>07700 900xxx</code> numbers). No real customers appear anywhere.</blockquote>","guide":[{"id":"novabot-on-the-website-0","title":"NovaBot, on the website","html":"<p>The chat widget on a page.   The booking card: session, day, free start times and details, all in the chat.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>It answers questions</strong> (<code>src/index.js</code>). Claude answers from the studio&#39;s own information: prices, policies and booking rules. Every link it gives is checked, and anything made up is replaced with a real one.</li><li><strong>Bookings always take the deposit.</strong> Nothing NovaBot does puts a session into Acuity unpaid (<code>src/book-session.js</code>). It works out the session, checks the time is still free and fills in the customer&#39;s details, then hands them Acuity&#39;s own booking page with everything ready. Paying the deposit there is what books it; the time isn&#39;t held until they pay. The same rule covers the staff chat and Nova Agent.</li><li><strong>The chat widget</strong> (<code>public/novabot.js</code>, <code>public/novabot.css</code>): opens after the page loads, keeps out of the way of buttons and forms, remembers the conversation across pages, and has a &quot;Keep chat closed&quot; switch. Optional voice: speak to it (Whisper on Workers AI) and hear replies (the browser&#39;s voice or MeloTTS).</li><li><strong>Booking links and free times</strong> (<code>src/booking.js</code>): reads session types and free start times from the studio&#39;s <em>public</em> Acuity booking page (no login, read-only).</li><li><strong>The booking card</strong> (<code>src/booking-form.js</code>): &quot;Book a session&quot; opens a card in the chat with the session, a strip of days, that day&#39;s free times and the visitor&#39;s details. The Worker checks the time again before anything happens.</li><li><strong>Enquiries</strong> (<code>src/enquiries.js</code>): NovaBot can take an enquiry, show the visitor a summary, and send it to the team once they confirm. It&#39;s saved for Portal and the admin pages, and can be emailed (Resend).</li><li><strong>Safety</strong>: per-visitor rate limits, only allowed websites can use the chat, spam limits on enquiries, and IP addresses stored only as a hash.</li></ul>","text":"The chat widget on a page. The booking card: session, day, free start times and details, all in the chat. It answers questions ( src/index.js ). Claude answers from the studio's own information: prices, policies and booking rules. Every link it gives is checked, and anything made up is replaced with a real one. Bookings always take the deposit. Nothing NovaBot does puts a session into Acuity unpaid ( src/book-session.js ). It works out the session, checks the time is still free and fills in the customer's details, then hands them Acuity's own booking page with everything ready. Paying the deposit there is what books it; the time isn't held until they pay. The same rule covers the staff chat and Nova Agent. The chat widget ( public/novabot.js , public/novabot.css ): opens after the page loads, keeps out of the way of buttons and forms, remembers the conversation across pages, and has a \"Keep chat closed\" switch. Optional voice: speak to it (Whisper on Workers AI) and hear replies (the browser's voice or MeloTTS). Booking links and free times ( src/booking.js ): reads session types and free start times from the studio's public Acuity booking page (no login, read-only). The booking card ( src/booking-form.js ): \"Book a session\" opens a card in the chat with the session, a strip of days, that day's free times and the visitor's details. The Worker checks the time again before anything happens. Enquiries ( src/enquiries.js ): NovaBot can take an enquiry, show the visitor a summary, and send it to the team once they confirm. It's saved for Portal and the admin pages, and can be emailed (Resend). Safety : per-visitor rate limits, only allowed websites can use the chat, spam limits on enquiries, and IP addresses stored only as a hash."},{"id":"portal-the-staff-app-1","title":"Portal, the staff app","html":"<p>The staff app (enquiries, website chats, bookings, alerts, Ask NovaBot and push to the staff phones, plus sign-in, everyone&#39;s planet and the team) is Nova Agent&#39;s <strong>Portal</strong> panel. Portal is part of it now. Its pages live in Nova Agent&#39;s repo (<code>web/portal</code>) and are copied in at build time (see The build step). Online it&#39;s at <code>/portal/</code>; this Worker is its back end (<code>/app/api/*</code>, <code>src/app-page.js</code>, and <code>src/portal/</code> for sign-in and the team). Portal&#39;s old address, <code>/app/</code>, redirects to Portal, but phones that installed Portal keep their push helper (<code>/app/sw.js</code>). Its guide and pictures are in Nova Agent&#39;s <code>docs/apps/portal</code>.</p>","text":"The staff app (enquiries, website chats, bookings, alerts, Ask NovaBot and push to the staff phones, plus sign-in, everyone's planet and the team) is Nova Agent's Portal panel. Portal is part of it now. Its pages live in Nova Agent's repo ( web/portal ) and are copied in at build time (see The build step). Online it's at /portal/ ; this Worker is its back end ( /app/api/* , src/app-page.js , and src/portal/ for sign-in and the team). Portal's old address, /app/ , redirects to Portal, but phones that installed Portal keep their push helper ( /app/sw.js ). Its guide and pictures are in Nova Agent's docs/apps/portal ."},{"id":"the-admin-pages-2","title":"The admin pages","html":"<p><code>/admin</code>, in Portal&#39;s look and themes. Sign in with Portal as an admin; signed out, it sends you to Portal and back.</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Page</th><th>What&#39;s there</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Referrals</strong> (<code>/admin</code>)</td><td>Referral codes, the appointments they brought in, and a CSV report</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Enquiries</strong></td><td>Every enquiry, mark done, and a test email</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Conversations</strong></td><td>Recent chats (kept 90 days), one in full with <code>?chat=ID</code></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Feedback</strong></td><td>What visitors said about NovaBot, good and bad</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Booking system</strong> (<code>/admin/connections</code>)</td><td>The Acuity / Nova switch, plus Google and Stripe</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Links</strong> (<code>/admin/links</code>)</td><td>The master list: every address with a live check, <strong>What&#39;s changed</strong>, and <strong>everything the suite can do</strong>. Edited here as JSON</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>The Links page&#39;s changelog (sample entries).</p>\n<p>The master list is kept in the database (<code>settings</code>), never in the code, because the code is public. Portal&#39;s Nova Agent sheet reads the same list from <code>/app/api/links</code> (<code>src/links.js</code>).</p>","text":"/admin , in Portal's look and themes. Sign in with Portal as an admin; signed out, it sends you to Portal and back. Page What's there Referrals ( /admin ) Referral codes, the appointments they brought in, and a CSV report Enquiries Every enquiry, mark done, and a test email Conversations Recent chats (kept 90 days), one in full with ?chat=ID Feedback What visitors said about NovaBot, good and bad Booking system ( /admin/connections ) The Acuity / Nova switch, plus Google and Stripe Links ( /admin/links ) The master list: every address with a live check, What's changed , and everything the suite can do . Edited here as JSON The Links page's changelog (sample entries). The master list is kept in the database ( settings ), never in the code, because the code is public. Portal's Nova Agent sheet reads the same list from /app/api/links ( src/links.js )."},{"id":"index-the-memory-engine-3","title":"Index: the memory engine","html":"<p>Index, browsing the suite&#39;s memory (sample data).</p>\n<p><code>src/memory/</code> is one shared memory for Nova Agent. Nova Agent&#39;s Index panel (copied in at <code>/app/memory/</code>) is the window onto it; NovaBot, Portal and Nova Agent read and add to it.</p>\n<p><strong>How it&#39;s kept.</strong> Small files of one-line facts, one file per subject, in D1 (never in git). Each line is tagged: <code>[stated]</code> said directly, <code>[observed]</code> seen in bookings or behaviour, <code>[inferred]</code> a pattern. Files stay small (about 3 KB; a condense pass tidies them), and at most about 800 tokens of memory go into any one prompt.</p>\n<p><strong>Scopes, and who sees what.</strong> The caller&#39;s role decides, never what it asks for.</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Scope</th><th>Holds</th><th>Read by</th><th>Written by</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>studio</code></td><td>The studio&#39;s shared facts: people, topics, areas</td><td>Staff, Nova Agent, Portal members</td><td>Staff, Nova Agent</td></tr><tr><td><code>staff</code></td><td>Each staff member&#39;s own partition</td><td>Staff, Nova Agent; a Portal member sees only their own</td><td>Staff, Nova Agent, the member themself</td></tr><tr><td><code>customer</code></td><td>One file per client (their email, or the chat until it&#39;s known)</td><td>Staff; NovaBot on the website sees only <em>that</em> customer&#39;s file</td><td>Staff (website facts wait for approval)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong>What it learns, and when.</strong> Always in the background, never while someone waits:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Portal&#39;s staff chats</strong>: facts are saved straight away (staff are trusted).</li><li><strong>Website chats</strong>: the every-minute job reads a chat once it&#39;s been quiet for 10 minutes (or every 20 messages), two chats a run. Facts about clients go into an <strong>approval queue</strong> in Index instead of being saved.</li><li><strong>Nova Agent</strong>: hands over conversation chunks with <code>POST /memory/extract</code>.</li></ul>\n<p>Each pass asks a small model for <strong>durable</strong> facts only (&quot;would this still be true and useful in three months?&quot;), and folds them into the file: a new line on the same subject replaces the old one rather than contradicting it. Writes carry a version token, so two apps can&#39;t overwrite each other.</p>\n<p><strong>Privacy.</strong> Card numbers, bank details, sort codes, National Insurance and passport numbers and passwords are refused at the door. Nothing is learned while a visitor waits. The website only ever sees the public studio file and that customer&#39;s own file, and client facts need a person to approve them.</p>\n<p>The API</p>\n<p>For Nova Agent (<code>Authorization: Bearer </code>):</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Route</th><th>Does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>GET /memory/context?scope=&amp;owner_id=&amp;q=</code></td><td>The files that matter for this turn, as text</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /memory/file?scope=&amp;owner_id=&amp;path=</code></td><td>One file and its version token</td></tr><tr><td><code>PUT /memory/file</code></td><td>Write a file (<code>if_version: &quot;new&quot;</code> or the token; 409 with the current file on a clash)</td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /memory/extract</code></td><td>Hand over a conversation chunk; learned in the background (202)</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /memory/index?scope=</code></td><td>The listing (no bodies)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>For Portal and Index (signed in), under <code>/app/api/memory/</code>: <code>index</code>, <code>file</code> (GET/PUT/DELETE), <code>pending</code>, <code>pending/:id</code> (approve or reject, optionally with an edited fact), and <code>stats</code>.</p>","text":"Index, browsing the suite's memory (sample data). src/memory/ is one shared memory for Nova Agent. Nova Agent's Index panel (copied in at /app/memory/ ) is the window onto it; NovaBot, Portal and Nova Agent read and add to it. How it's kept. Small files of one-line facts, one file per subject, in D1 (never in git). Each line is tagged: [stated] said directly, [observed] seen in bookings or behaviour, [inferred] a pattern. Files stay small (about 3 KB; a condense pass tidies them), and at most about 800 tokens of memory go into any one prompt. Scopes, and who sees what. The caller's role decides, never what it asks for. Scope Holds Read by Written by studio The studio's shared facts: people, topics, areas Staff, Nova Agent, Portal members Staff, Nova Agent staff Each staff member's own partition Staff, Nova Agent; a Portal member sees only their own Staff, Nova Agent, the member themself customer One file per client (their email, or the chat until it's known) Staff; NovaBot on the website sees only that customer's file Staff (website facts wait for approval) What it learns, and when. Always in the background, never while someone waits: Portal's staff chats : facts are saved straight away (staff are trusted). Website chats : the every-minute job reads a chat once it's been quiet for 10 minutes (or every 20 messages), two chats a run. Facts about clients go into an approval queue in Index instead of being saved. Nova Agent : hands over conversation chunks with POST /memory/extract . Each pass asks a small model for durable facts only (\"would this still be true and useful in three months?\"), and folds them into the file: a new line on the same subject replaces the old one rather than contradicting it. Writes carry a version token, so two apps can't overwrite each other. Privacy. Card numbers, bank details, sort codes, National Insurance and passport numbers and passwords are refused at the door. Nothing is learned while a visitor waits. The website only ever sees the public studio file and that customer's own file, and client facts need a person to approve them. The API For Nova Agent ( Authorization: Bearer ): Route Does GET /memory/context?scope=&owner_id=&q= The files that matter for this turn, as text GET /memory/file?scope=&owner_id=&path= One file and its version token PUT /memory/file Write a file ( if_version: \"new\" or the token; 409 with the current file on a clash) POST /memory/extract Hand over a conversation chunk; learned in the background (202) GET /memory/index?scope= The listing (no bodies) For Portal and Index (signed in), under /app/api/memory/ : index , file (GET/PUT/DELETE), pending , pending/:id (approve or reject, optionally with an edited fact), and stats ."},{"id":"portal-one-sign-in-for-the-suite-4","title":"Portal: one sign-in for the suite","html":"<p>Sign in once for every Nova app.  The crew, each with their own planet (sample people).</p>\n<p><code>src/portal/</code> signs people in once for Portal, Index and the admin pages. The pages are Nova Agent&#39;s Portal panel (<code>web/portal</code> in Nova Agent&#39;s repo), copied in at build time (see the build step); this Worker serves them at <code>/portal/</code> and runs the API.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Accounts.</strong> Everyone has their own (<code>staff</code> table): a readable id like <code>dana</code>, an email, a display name, a role and a status (active, invited or switched off). The first admin is set up with the studio&#39;s current password.</li><li><strong>Invites.</strong> An admin invites someone by email and gets a link that works once, for 7 days. Only a hash of its token is stored. The new person chooses a password and is signed in.</li><li><strong>Passwords.</strong> PBKDF2-SHA256 with 100,000 rounds and a random salt for each person; a few tries a minute at most per address.</li><li><strong>Sessions.</strong> A random token in an httpOnly, Secure cookie for 30 days (or an app token, <code>Authorization: Bearer nsess_…</code>, for native apps). Only its SHA-256 is stored, and signing out deletes it, so it stops working everywhere at once.</li><li><strong>Roles.</strong> <code>admin</code> (everything, including the crew and the admin pages) or <code>staff</code>. A staff member who isn&#39;t an admin sees the studio&#39;s memory and their own partition of Index.</li><li><strong>Planets.</strong> Every person gets a planet, drawn fresh from their seed by the planet generator: <code>GET /staff/:id/planet.svg?size=&amp;animate=1</code>. It&#39;s their avatar across the suite.</li><li><strong>One sign-in.</strong> There&#39;s no shared password any more: Portal, Index, the admin pages and every other panel take a Portal sign-in.</li></ul>\n<p>The API</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Route</th><th>Does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>POST /auth/login</code></td><td><code>{ email, password, client? }</code> → session cookie (or an app token)</td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /auth/logout</code></td><td>Ends this session everywhere</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /auth/me</code></td><td>Who&#39;s signed in (every app starts with this)</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /auth/status</code></td><td><code>{ setupNeeded }</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /auth/setup</code></td><td>The first admin, proven with the studio&#39;s current password</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /auth/invite?token=</code> / <code>POST /auth/invite/accept</code></td><td>Who an invite is for; choose a password</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /staff</code>, <code>POST /staff</code></td><td>Admins: everyone; invite someone</td></tr><tr><td><code>POST /staff/:id/invite</code></td><td>Admins: a fresh invite link</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /staff/:id</code>, <code>PATCH /staff/:id</code></td><td>A profile; change it (admins: role and status too)</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /staff/:id/planet.svg</code></td><td>The planet badge</td></tr><tr><td><code>GET /staff/:id/index</code></td><td>That person&#39;s Index view</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Changes from a browser must come from this site (the Origin header).</p>","text":"Sign in once for every Nova app. The crew, each with their own planet (sample people). src/portal/ signs people in once for Portal, Index and the admin pages. The pages are Nova Agent's Portal panel ( web/portal in Nova Agent's repo), copied in at build time (see the build step); this Worker serves them at /portal/ and runs the API. Accounts. Everyone has their own ( staff table): a readable id like dana , an email, a display name, a role and a status (active, invited or switched off). The first admin is set up with the studio's current password. Invites. An admin invites someone by email and gets a link that works once, for 7 days. Only a hash of its token is stored. The new person chooses a password and is signed in. Passwords. PBKDF2-SHA256 with 100,000 rounds and a random salt for each person; a few tries a minute at most per address. Sessions. A random token in an httpOnly, Secure cookie for 30 days (or an app token, Authorization: Bearer nsess_… , for native apps). Only its SHA-256 is stored, and signing out deletes it, so it stops working everywhere at once. Roles. admin (everything, including the crew and the admin pages) or staff . A staff member who isn't an admin sees the studio's memory and their own partition of Index. Planets. Every person gets a planet, drawn fresh from their seed by the planet generator: GET /staff/:id/planet.svg?size=&animate=1 . It's their avatar across the suite. One sign-in. There's no shared password any more: Portal, Index, the admin pages and every other panel take a Portal sign-in. The API Route Does POST /auth/login { email, password, client? } → session cookie (or an app token) POST /auth/logout Ends this session everywhere GET /auth/me Who's signed in (every app starts with this) GET /auth/status { setupNeeded } POST /auth/setup The first admin, proven with the studio's current password GET /auth/invite?token= / POST /auth/invite/accept Who an invite is for; choose a password GET /staff , POST /staff Admins: everyone; invite someone POST /staff/:id/invite Admins: a fresh invite link GET /staff/:id , PATCH /staff/:id A profile; change it (admins: role and status too) GET /staff/:id/planet.svg The planet badge GET /staff/:id/index That person's Index view Changes from a browser must come from this site (the Origin header)."},{"id":"nova-bot-s-own-booking-system-behind-a-switch-5","title":"Nova Bot's own booking system (behind a switch)","html":"<p>Bookings go through <strong>Acuity</strong> by default. Alongside it, <code>src/nova/</code> holds Nova Bot&#39;s own booking system, switched <strong>off</strong> until you choose otherwise:</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Booking page</strong> at <code>/book</code>, with the studio&#39;s <strong>Google Calendar</strong> as the diary, confirmation emails from the studio&#39;s <strong>Gmail</strong>, and deposits through <strong>Stripe</strong>.</li><li><strong>Customer pages</strong>: each customer gets a page to pay, move or cancel.</li><li><strong>Staff tools</strong> in Portal: cancel, move, refund and send payment links.</li></ul>\n<p><strong>The switch</strong> is on <code>/admin/connections</code>, under &quot;Booking system&quot;. It&#39;s stored in the <code>settings</code> table as <code>booking_system</code> (<code>acuity</code> or <code>nova</code>), and falls back to the <code>BOOKING_SYSTEM</code> variable, then to Acuity (<code>src/mode.js</code>).</p>\n<ul><li>It takes effect straight away, with no redeploy.</li><li>Nova can only be switched on once Google and Stripe both work. Switching back to Acuity is always one click.</li><li>On Acuity, everything behaves exactly as before, and the original tests prove it.</li><li>Either way, a booking made with Nova keeps working (its page, payment links and Stripe&#39;s webhook), and Acuity&#39;s webhook is still listened to.</li></ul>\n<p>Setting it up</p>\n<ol><li><strong>Google:</strong> in Nova Agent, Admin → Google walks through it a step at a time (Google Cloud&#39;s pages open from buttons, with copy buttons for every address to paste), then takes the key and has a <strong>Connect Google</strong> button. The same key gives everyone <strong>Sign in with Google</strong> and Notes&#39; Google Docs. (Setting <code>GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID</code> and <code>GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET</code> as secrets still works, and wins.)</li><li><strong>Stripe:</strong> <code>npx wrangler secret put STRIPE_SECRET_KEY</code> (use a <code>sk_test_…</code> key to try it). Add a webhook endpoint <code>https:///stripe/webhook</code> with the events <code>checkout.session.completed</code>, <code>checkout.session.async_payment_succeeded</code> and <code>checkout.session.expired</code>, and save its signing secret as <code>STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET</code>.</li><li><strong>Database:</strong> <code>npx wrangler d1 migrations apply novabot --remote</code>.</li><li><strong>Deploy,</strong> then on <code>/admin/connections</code>: press <strong>Send a test email</strong>, and flip the switch to try it.</li></ol>\n<p>Sessions, prices and rules (opening hours, 50% deposit, 48-hour cancellation) are in <code>src/nova/studio.js</code>.</p>","text":"Bookings go through Acuity by default. Alongside it, src/nova/ holds Nova Bot's own booking system, switched off until you choose otherwise: Booking page at /book , with the studio's Google Calendar as the diary, confirmation emails from the studio's Gmail , and deposits through Stripe . Customer pages : each customer gets a page to pay, move or cancel. Staff tools in Portal: cancel, move, refund and send payment links. The switch is on /admin/connections , under \"Booking system\". It's stored in the settings table as booking_system ( acuity or nova ), and falls back to the BOOKING_SYSTEM variable, then to Acuity ( src/mode.js ). It takes effect straight away, with no redeploy. Nova can only be switched on once Google and Stripe both work. Switching back to Acuity is always one click. On Acuity, everything behaves exactly as before, and the original tests prove it. Either way, a booking made with Nova keeps working (its page, payment links and Stripe's webhook), and Acuity's webhook is still listened to. Setting it up Google: in Nova Agent, Admin → Google walks through it a step at a time (Google Cloud's pages open from buttons, with copy buttons for every address to paste), then takes the key and has a Connect Google button. The same key gives everyone Sign in with Google and Notes' Google Docs. (Setting GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID and GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET as secrets still works, and wins.) Stripe: npx wrangler secret put STRIPE_SECRET_KEY (use a sk_test_… key to try it). Add a webhook endpoint https:///stripe/webhook with the events checkout.session.completed , checkout.session.async_payment_succeeded and checkout.session.expired , and save its signing secret as STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET . Database: npx wrangler d1 migrations apply novabot --remote . Deploy, then on /admin/connections : press Send a test email , and flip the switch to try it. Sessions, prices and rules (opening hours, 50% deposit, 48-hour cancellation) are in src/nova/studio.js ."},{"id":"works-with-nova-agent-6","title":"Works with Nova Agent","html":"<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Project</th><th>What it is</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-agent\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">nova-agent</a></td><td>The studio&#39;s one app: chat, Missions and Quests, and every panel (Portal, Calendar, Notes, Index, Observatory, Lossless audio). On the studio PC, and online from here for phones</td></tr><tr><td><strong><a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-bot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">nova-bot</a></strong></td><td>This repo: NovaBot on the website, and the back end behind Nova Agent (sign-in, push, bookings, the memory engine, jobs)</td></tr><tr><td><a href=\"https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-club\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">nova-club</a></td><td>Members&#39; Android app that shows the studio&#39;s busy times</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","text":"Project What it is nova-agent The studio's one app: chat, Missions and Quests, and every panel (Portal, Calendar, Notes, Index, Observatory, Lossless audio). On the studio PC, and online from here for phones nova-bot This repo: NovaBot on the website, and the back end behind Nova Agent (sign-in, push, bookings, the memory engine, jobs) nova-club Members' Android app that shows the studio's busy times"}],"built":[{"id":"how-it-works-0","title":"How it works","html":"<pre><code>flowchart LR\n    V[Website visitor] --&gt;|chat widget| W\n    S[Staff · Portal&lt;br/&gt;Index] --&gt; W\n    C[Nova Club app] --&gt;|/club/busy| W\n    subgraph W[Nova Bot · Cloudflare Worker]\n      R[Routes · src/index.js] --&gt; CL[Claude]\n      R --&gt; DB[(D1 database)]\n      R --&gt; AI[Workers AI&lt;br/&gt;voice]\n      R --&gt; MEM[Memory engine&lt;br/&gt;src/memory]\n      R --&gt; PO[Sign-in&lt;br/&gt;src/portal]\n    end\n    W --&gt;|public booking page,&lt;br/&gt;API, calendar feed| A[Acuity Scheduling]\n    NA[Nova Agent&lt;br/&gt;studio PC] --&gt;|jobs, quests,&lt;br/&gt;memory| W\n    NA --&gt;|admin pages| A\n    W --&gt;|Web Push| S\n    W -.-&gt;|behind the switch| G[Google Calendar · Gmail · Stripe]</code></pre>\n<ul><li><strong>One Worker</strong> serves the widget, the chat API, Portal, Index, the admin pages, webhooks and a once-a-minute cron (booking pings, and reading website chats for memory).</li><li><strong>D1</strong> holds enquiries, chat logs (90 days), referral codes, notifications, settings, Nova Agent&#39;s job queue, the memory files, staff accounts and sessions and, when switched on, Nova Bot&#39;s own bookings (<code>migrations/</code>).</li><li><strong>Secrets</strong> live in Cloudflare (<code>wrangler secret put</code>), never in the code.</li></ul>","text":"flowchart LR V[Website visitor] -->|chat widget| W S[Staff · Portal<br/>Index] --> W C[Nova Club app] -->|/club/busy| W subgraph W[Nova Bot · Cloudflare Worker] R[Routes · src/index.js] --> CL[Claude] R --> DB[(D1 database)] R --> AI[Workers AI<br/>voice] R --> MEM[Memory engine<br/>src/memory] R --> PO[Sign-in<br/>src/portal] end W -->|public booking page,<br/>API, calendar feed| A[Acuity Scheduling] NA[Nova Agent<br/>studio PC] -->|jobs, quests,<br/>memory| W NA -->|admin pages| A W -->|Web Push| S W -.->|behind the switch| G[Google Calendar · Gmail · Stripe] One Worker serves the widget, the chat API, Portal, Index, the admin pages, webhooks and a once-a-minute cron (booking pings, and reading website chats for memory). D1 holds enquiries, chat logs (90 days), referral codes, notifications, settings, Nova Agent's job queue, the memory files, staff accounts and sessions and, when switched on, Nova Bot's own bookings ( migrations/ ). Secrets live in Cloudflare ( wrangler secret put ), never in the code."},{"id":"run-it-locally-sandbox-1","title":"Run it locally (sandbox)","html":"<p>You need <a href=\"https://nodejs.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Node.js</a> 20 or newer. No Cloudflare, Claude or Acuity account is needed.</p>\n<pre><code>git clone https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-bot.git\ncd nova-bot\nnpm install\nnpm run sandbox:setup   # creates .dev.vars from the example, and a local database\nnpm run sandbox         # starts it at http://localhost:8787</code></pre>\n<p>Open : a pretend website with the chat widget on it.</p>\n<p>The sandbox: a pretend studio site, with clearly labelled stand-in replies when no AI key is set.</p>\n<ul><li><strong>Everything stays on your computer.</strong> The sandbox has its own local database and can&#39;t reach any live Nova Bot, database or calendar.</li><li><strong>Without an AI key</strong>, NovaBot gives clearly labelled stand-in replies, so you can try the widget, enquiries, Portal and the admin pages for free.</li><li><strong>For real answers</strong>, put your own Claude API key (<a href=\"https://console.anthropic.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">console.anthropic.com</a>) in <code>.dev.vars</code> as <code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...</code> and restart. That uses your own Anthropic account.</li><li><strong>Admin pages and Portal</strong>:  and ; set up the first admin with the password in <code>.dev.vars</code> (<code>sandbox</code>).</li><li><strong>The booking card</strong> needs a booking system it can check times against. To try it offline, start the sandbox with Nova Bot&#39;s own system switched on: <code>npx wrangler dev --env sandbox --var BOOKING_SYSTEM:nova</code> (no Google key means the &quot;calendar&quot; is the local bookings table; no Stripe key means a local stand-in checkout).</li><li><strong>Voice</strong>: speech uses your browser&#39;s own voice; the microphone needs Workers AI, so it isn&#39;t available in the sandbox.</li></ul>\n<p><code>.dev.vars</code> is in <code>.gitignore</code>: your keys never get committed.</p>","text":"You need Node.js 20 or newer. No Cloudflare, Claude or Acuity account is needed. git clone https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-bot.git cd nova-bot npm install npm run sandbox:setup # creates .dev.vars from the example, and a local database npm run sandbox # starts it at http://localhost:8787 Open : a pretend website with the chat widget on it. The sandbox: a pretend studio site, with clearly labelled stand-in replies when no AI key is set. Everything stays on your computer. The sandbox has its own local database and can't reach any live Nova Bot, database or calendar. Without an AI key , NovaBot gives clearly labelled stand-in replies, so you can try the widget, enquiries, Portal and the admin pages for free. For real answers , put your own Claude API key ( console.anthropic.com ) in .dev.vars as ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=... and restart. That uses your own Anthropic account. Admin pages and Portal : and ; set up the first admin with the password in .dev.vars ( sandbox ). The booking card needs a booking system it can check times against. To try it offline, start the sandbox with Nova Bot's own system switched on: npx wrangler dev --env sandbox --var BOOKING_SYSTEM:nova (no Google key means the \"calendar\" is the local bookings table; no Stripe key means a local stand-in checkout). Voice : speech uses your browser's own voice; the microphone needs Workers AI, so it isn't available in the sandbox. .dev.vars is in .gitignore : your keys never get committed."},{"id":"the-build-step-2","title":"The build step","html":"<p>Nova Agent&#39;s panels (Portal, Index, Calendar, Notes, and what they share) live in Nova Agent&#39;s repo (<code>na/web</code>). They&#39;re served from here online, so they share this Worker&#39;s sign-in, so before every deploy or local run, wrangler&#39;s build step (<code>&quot;build&quot;: { &quot;command&quot;: &quot;node scripts/sync-apps.mjs&quot; }</code>) copies them in:</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>From (Nova Agent)</th><th>To</th><th>What</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>web/portal/</code></td><td><code>public/portal/</code></td><td>Portal</td></tr><tr><td><code>web/portal/old-app-address/</code></td><td><code>public/app/</code></td><td>What phones that installed Portal from <code>/app/</code> still use: its push helper, manifest and icons</td></tr><tr><td><code>web/index/</code></td><td><code>public/app/memory/</code></td><td>Index</td></tr><tr><td><code>web/calendar/</code>, <code>web/notes/</code></td><td><code>public/calendar/</code>, <code>public/notes/</code></td><td>Calendar and Notes (online, they save in the browser)</td></tr><tr><td><code>web/shared/</code></td><td><code>public/shared/</code></td><td>Themes, sounds, the badge and the Manual</td></tr><tr><td><code>web/portal/planet/</code></td><td><code>src/portal/planet/</code></td><td>The planet generator (also draws <code>planet.svg</code>)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Nova Agent is expected at <code>../../na</code>; <code>NOVA_AGENT_DIR</code> points elsewhere. The page copies are never saved in this repo (<code>.gitignore</code>). The planet generator copy is, so the project still builds and tests on its own.</p>\n<p><strong>Addresses</strong>: Portal at <code>/portal/</code>, Index at <code>/app/memory/</code>. Portal&#39;s old pages (<code>/app/</code>, <code>/app/?view=alerts</code> and so on) redirect to Portal (<code>src/index.js</code>, <code>movedPage</code>); its API (<code>/app/api/</code>) and the files in <code>public/app/</code> stay. The addresses the panels had for a day (<code>/studio/</code>, <code>/crew/</code>, <code>/index/</code>) redirect too.</p>","text":"Nova Agent's panels (Portal, Index, Calendar, Notes, and what they share) live in Nova Agent's repo ( na/web ). They're served from here online, so they share this Worker's sign-in, so before every deploy or local run, wrangler's build step ( \"build\": { \"command\": \"node scripts/sync-apps.mjs\" } ) copies them in: From (Nova Agent) To What web/portal/ public/portal/ Portal web/portal/old-app-address/ public/app/ What phones that installed Portal from /app/ still use: its push helper, manifest and icons web/index/ public/app/memory/ Index web/calendar/ , web/notes/ public/calendar/ , public/notes/ Calendar and Notes (online, they save in the browser) web/shared/ public/shared/ Themes, sounds, the badge and the Manual web/portal/planet/ src/portal/planet/ The planet generator (also draws planet.svg ) Nova Agent is expected at ../../na ; NOVA_AGENT_DIR points elsewhere. The page copies are never saved in this repo ( .gitignore ). The planet generator copy is, so the project still builds and tests on its own. Addresses : Portal at /portal/ , Index at /app/memory/ . Portal's old pages ( /app/ , /app/?view=alerts and so on) redirect to Portal ( src/index.js , movedPage ); its API ( /app/api/ ) and the files in public/app/ stay. The addresses the panels had for a day ( /studio/ , /crew/ , /index/ ) redirect too."},{"id":"configuration-3","title":"Configuration","html":"<p>Everything secret is a <strong>Wrangler secret</strong> (<code>npx wrangler secret put NAME</code>), or a line in <code>.dev.vars</code> for local runs. Names only; values never belong in the repository.</p>\n<div class=\"table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Needed for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code></td><td>Claude answers and memory (required live)</td></tr><tr><td><code>ADMIN_PASSWORD</code></td><td>Only proves it&#39;s you when setting up the very first Portal admin</td></tr><tr><td><code>ACUITY_USER_ID</code>, <code>ACUITY_API_KEY</code></td><td>Referral tracking, real-booking checks and managing bookings from Portal (Acuity&#39;s Powerhouse plan)</td></tr><tr><td><code>ACUITY_WEBHOOK_KEY</code></td><td>Accepting Acuity&#39;s webhook (<code>/acuity/webhook?key=…</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>ACUITY_CALENDAR_URL</code></td><td>Acuity&#39;s private calendar feed: booking details, the Calendar tab and Nova Club&#39;s busy times</td></tr><tr><td><code>ACUITY_EMAIL_KEY</code></td><td>The Google Apps Script that forwards Acuity&#39;s emails (<code>tools/acuity-email-forwarder.gs</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>AGENT_NOVA_KEY</code></td><td>Nova Agent&#39;s routes (<code>/nova-agent/*</code>; <code>/memory/*</code>), and its online link (<code>/nova-agent/link</code>, the AgentLink Durable Object in <code>src/agent-relay.js</code>: Nova Agent&#39;s chat, Missions, Quests, Calendar and Visualizer online, through the studio PC)</td></tr><tr><td><code>VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY</code>, <code>VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY</code></td><td>Phone notifications (Web Push)</td></tr><tr><td><code>RESEND_API_KEY</code>, <code>ENQUIRY_EMAIL_TO</code>, <code>ENQUIRY_EMAIL_FROM</code></td><td>Emailing enquiries (optional)</td></tr><tr><td><code>GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID</code>, <code>GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET</code></td><td>Optional: Admin → Google keeps the same key without them (Notes&#39; Google Docs, Calendar and Gmail for bookings; Google is never a way to sign in, Portal is)</td></tr><tr><td><code>GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN</code>, <code>GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ID</code>, <code>GOOGLE_ACCOUNT</code></td><td>Optional overrides; normally set by &quot;Connect Google&quot; on <code>/admin/connections</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>STRIPE_SECRET_KEY</code>, <code>STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET</code></td><td>Nova Bot&#39;s own booking system: deposits (optional)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Plain variables (in <code>wrangler.jsonc</code> or <code>--var</code>): <code>BOOKING_SYSTEM</code> (<code>acuity</code> or <code>nova</code>, the fallback for the switch), <code>PUBLIC_URL</code>, <code>SANDBOX</code>, <code>BOOKING_DETAILS_WAIT_SECONDS</code>.</p>\n<p>Bindings in <code>wrangler.jsonc</code>: <code>DB</code> (D1), <code>AI</code> (Workers AI), <code>CHAT_LIMIT</code>, <code>VOICE_LIMIT</code> and <code>CLUB_LIMIT</code> (rate limits), static assets from <code>public/</code>, the build step, and a cron trigger every minute.</p>\n<p>More detail lives alongside this file: README-ENQUIRIES.md (enquiries, booking links, free times, chat log), README-REFERRALS.md (referral codes and Acuity&#39;s webhook), README-SQUARESPACE.md (adding the widget to a Squarespace site) and PRIVACY-POLICY-NOVABOT.md (privacy policy wording).</p>\n<p>Booking details from Acuity&#39;s confirmation page (optional back-up)</p>\n<p>Paste this into Acuity → Integrations → Custom conversion tracking, under anything already there, replacing <code>YOUR-WORKER</code> with your Worker&#39;s address:</p>\n<pre><code>&lt;!-- Portal: sends this booking&#39;s details to the staff notification --&gt;\n&lt;div id=&quot;nv-booked&quot; hidden&gt;&lt;i&gt;%type%&lt;/i&gt;&lt;i&gt;%id%&lt;/i&gt;&lt;i&gt;%appointmentType%&lt;/i&gt;&lt;i&gt;%clientDate%&lt;/i&gt;&lt;i&gt;%clientTime%&lt;/i&gt;&lt;i&gt;%price%&lt;/i&gt;&lt;i&gt;%email%&lt;/i&gt;&lt;i&gt;%calendar%&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;script&gt;\n(function () {\n  var names = [&quot;type&quot;, &quot;id&quot;, &quot;session&quot;, &quot;date&quot;, &quot;time&quot;, &quot;price&quot;, &quot;email&quot;, &quot;calendar&quot;];\n  var values = document.querySelectorAll(&quot;#nv-booked i&quot;);\n  var query = names.map(function (name, i) { return name + &quot;=&quot; + encodeURIComponent(values[i].textContent.trim()); }).join(&quot;&amp;&quot;);\n  new Image().src = &quot;https://YOUR-WORKER/acuity/booked?&quot; + query;\n})();\n&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre>\n<p>The main source of booking details is Acuity&#39;s private calendar feed (Acuity → Sync with Other Calendars → 1-way Calendar Sync, saved as <code>ACUITY_CALENDAR_URL</code>), which works on every Acuity plan and for bookings staff add themselves. Acuity&#39;s own booking emails are a second back-up: <code>tools/acuity-email-forwarder.gs</code> runs in the mailbox Acuity emails and passes each one to <code>/acuity/email</code>. Once emails are coming through, notifications wait for them (up to 3 minutes, then the once-a-minute cron sends them anyway).</p>","text":"Everything secret is a Wrangler secret ( npx wrangler secret put NAME ), or a line in .dev.vars for local runs. Names only; values never belong in the repository. Name Needed for ANTHROPIC_API_KEY Claude answers and memory (required live) ADMIN_PASSWORD Only proves it's you when setting up the very first Portal admin ACUITY_USER_ID , ACUITY_API_KEY Referral tracking, real-booking checks and managing bookings from Portal (Acuity's Powerhouse plan) ACUITY_WEBHOOK_KEY Accepting Acuity's webhook ( /acuity/webhook?key=… ) ACUITY_CALENDAR_URL Acuity's private calendar feed: booking details, the Calendar tab and Nova Club's busy times ACUITY_EMAIL_KEY The Google Apps Script that forwards Acuity's emails ( tools/acuity-email-forwarder.gs ) AGENT_NOVA_KEY Nova Agent's routes ( /nova-agent/* ; /memory/* ), and its online link ( /nova-agent/link , the AgentLink Durable Object in src/agent-relay.js : Nova Agent's chat, Missions, Quests, Calendar and Visualizer online, through the studio PC) VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY , VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY Phone notifications (Web Push) RESEND_API_KEY , ENQUIRY_EMAIL_TO , ENQUIRY_EMAIL_FROM Emailing enquiries (optional) GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID , GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET Optional: Admin → Google keeps the same key without them (Notes' Google Docs, Calendar and Gmail for bookings; Google is never a way to sign in, Portal is) GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN , GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ID , GOOGLE_ACCOUNT Optional overrides; normally set by \"Connect Google\" on /admin/connections STRIPE_SECRET_KEY , STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET Nova Bot's own booking system: deposits (optional) Plain variables (in wrangler.jsonc or --var ): BOOKING_SYSTEM ( acuity or nova , the fallback for the switch), PUBLIC_URL , SANDBOX , BOOKING_DETAILS_WAIT_SECONDS . Bindings in wrangler.jsonc : DB (D1), AI (Workers AI), CHAT_LIMIT , VOICE_LIMIT and CLUB_LIMIT (rate limits), static assets from public/ , the build step, and a cron trigger every minute. More detail lives alongside this file: README-ENQUIRIES.md (enquiries, booking links, free times, chat log), README-REFERRALS.md (referral codes and Acuity's webhook), README-SQUARESPACE.md (adding the widget to a Squarespace site) and PRIVACY-POLICY-NOVABOT.md (privacy policy wording). Booking details from Acuity's confirmation page (optional back-up) Paste this into Acuity → Integrations → Custom conversion tracking, under anything already there, replacing YOUR-WORKER with your Worker's address: <!-- Portal: sends this booking's details to the staff notification --> <div id=\"nv-booked\" hidden><i>%type%</i><i>%id%</i><i>%appointmentType%</i><i>%clientDate%</i><i>%clientTime%</i><i>%price%</i><i>%email%</i><i>%calendar%</i></div> <script> (function () { var names = [\"type\", \"id\", \"session\", \"date\", \"time\", \"price\", \"email\", \"calendar\"]; var values = document.querySelectorAll(\"#nv-booked i\"); var query = names.map(function (name, i) { return name + \"=\" + encodeURIComponent(values[i].textContent.trim()); }).join(\"&\"); new Image().src = \"https://YOUR-WORKER/acuity/booked?\" + query; })(); </script> The main source of booking details is Acuity's private calendar feed (Acuity → Sync with Other Calendars → 1-way Calendar Sync, saved as ACUITY_CALENDAR_URL ), which works on every Acuity plan and for bookings staff add themselves. Acuity's own booking emails are a second back-up: tools/acuity-email-forwarder.gs runs in the mailbox Acuity emails and passes each one to /acuity/email . Once emails are coming through, notifications wait for them (up to 3 minutes, then the once-a-minute cron sends them anyway)."},{"id":"tests-4","title":"Tests","html":"<pre><code>npm test            # watch mode\nnpx vitest run      # once</code></pre>\n<p>388 tests across 27 files, fully offline: they run inside the Workers runtime (<code>@cloudflare/vitest-plugin</code>) with a local database and fake versions of Claude, Acuity, Google, Stripe and Resend (<code>test/fakes.js</code>). Every key in <code>vitest.config.mjs</code> is a test-only stand-in. The original Acuity tests run against the default; <code>test/*-nova.spec.js</code> run with the switch on Nova, and <code>test/switch.spec.js</code> tests the switch itself. The memory engine and Portal have their own (<code>test/memory.spec.js</code>, <code>test/portal.spec.js</code>).</p>","text":"npm test # watch mode npx vitest run # once 388 tests across 27 files, fully offline: they run inside the Workers runtime ( @cloudflare/vitest-plugin ) with a local database and fake versions of Claude, Acuity, Google, Stripe and Resend ( test/fakes.js ). Every key in vitest.config.mjs is a test-only stand-in. The original Acuity tests run against the default; test/*-nova.spec.js run with the switch on Nova, and test/switch.spec.js tests the switch itself. The memory engine and Portal have their own ( test/memory.spec.js , test/portal.spec.js )."},{"id":"deploying-your-own-copy-5","title":"Deploying your own copy","html":"<ol><li>Log in to Cloudflare: <code>npx wrangler login</code>.</li><li>Create the database: <code>npx wrangler d1 create novabot</code>, put its <code>database_id</code> in <code>wrangler.jsonc</code>, then <code>npx wrangler d1 migrations apply novabot --remote</code>.</li><li>Add the secrets you need from Configuration, at least <code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code> and <code>ADMIN_PASSWORD</code>.</li><li>Swap Novacane&#39;s details for your own:</li><li class=\"sub\"><code>src/index.js</code>: <code>BOOKING_LINK</code>, <code>ENQUIRY_LINK</code>, <code>WHATSAPP_NUMBER</code>, <code>WHATSAPP_LINK</code>, <code>ALLOWED_ORIGINS</code>, and the studio information in <code>STUDIO_INFO</code></li><li class=\"sub\"><code>src/booking.js</code>: <code>ACUITY_OWNER</code> (the number after <code>owner=</code> in your Acuity booking page&#39;s address)</li><li class=\"sub\"><code>src/nova/studio.js</code> and <code>src/nova/booking.js</code> (<code>LIVE_URL</code>) for the Nova system</li><li class=\"sub\"><code>public/novabot.js</code>: <code>LIVE_WORKER_URL</code>, <code>BOOKING_LINK</code>, <code>PRIVACY_LINK</code></li><li>Deploy with <code>npm run deploy</code> (the build step copies Index and Portal in), then add the widget to your website (see README-SQUARESPACE.md).</li><li>Open <code>/portal/</code> to set up the first admin with the studio password, then invite the team.</li></ol>","text":"Log in to Cloudflare: npx wrangler login . Create the database: npx wrangler d1 create novabot , put its database_id in wrangler.jsonc , then npx wrangler d1 migrations apply novabot --remote . Add the secrets you need from Configuration, at least ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and ADMIN_PASSWORD . Swap Novacane's details for your own: src/index.js : BOOKING_LINK , ENQUIRY_LINK , WHATSAPP_NUMBER , WHATSAPP_LINK , ALLOWED_ORIGINS , and the studio information in STUDIO_INFO src/booking.js : ACUITY_OWNER (the number after owner= in your Acuity booking page's address) src/nova/studio.js and src/nova/booking.js ( LIVE_URL ) for the Nova system public/novabot.js : LIVE_WORKER_URL , BOOKING_LINK , PRIVACY_LINK Deploy with npm run deploy (the build step copies Index and Portal in), then add the widget to your website (see README-SQUARESPACE.md). Open /portal/ to set up the first admin with the studio password, then invite the team."},{"id":"project-layout-6","title":"Project layout","html":"<pre><code>public/novabot.js, novabot.css   the chat widget (served by the Worker)\npublic/app, portal, calendar, … Nova Agent&#39;s panels, copied in at build time (not in this repo)\n  app.js, app.css                  the tabs, the smart calendar, alerts, voice, pings\n  suite.js                         Nova Agent sheet, All links, What&#39;s changed\n  options.js, themes.js/.css       Options and the six themes\n  ambient.js, sfx.js               ambient music and sound effects\n  sw.js                            notifications with the app closed\n  memory/                          Index (copied in at build time, not in git)\npublic/portal/                   Portal&#39;s pages (copied in at build time, not in git)\nsrc/index.js                     the Worker: chat, voice, routes, NovaBot&#39;s instructions\nsrc/app-page.js                  Portal&#39;s staff API (/app/api/*, from Portal&#39;s old address)\nsrc/portal-ask.js                Ask Nova: questions about bookings, enquiries and alerts\nsrc/admin.js                     the admin pages\nsrc/links.js                     the master list: links, features, changelog\nsrc/memory/                      the memory engine (store, extract, routes)\nsrc/portal/                      Portal: sign-in, sessions, staff, planets\nsrc/booking.js                   session types, booking links, free times (public Acuity page)\nsrc/booking-form.js              the booking card&#39;s API\nsrc/book-session.js              booking checks (deposit first)\nsrc/manage-bookings.js           staff finding, cancelling, moving and changing bookings\nsrc/agent-nova.js                jobs, quests and alerts for Nova Agent\nsrc/enquiries.js                 enquiries, enquiry emails, chat log\nsrc/push.js                      notifications, the Alerts tab, real-booking checks\nsrc/booking-calendar.js          booking details from Acuity&#39;s calendar feed\nsrc/booking-details.js           booking details from Acuity&#39;s confirmation page\nsrc/booking-emails.js            booking details from Acuity&#39;s emails\nsrc/booking-pings.js             when booking notifications go out\nsrc/club-calendar.js             busy times for Nova Club\nsrc/referrals.js                 referral tracking (Acuity API)\nsrc/feedback.js                  what visitors said about NovaBot\nsrc/health.js                    daily Acuity API check\nsrc/mode.js                      the booking-system switch\nsrc/nova/                        Nova Bot&#39;s own booking system (Google, Gmail, Stripe)\nsrc/fonts/                       Saira, Geist Mono and Source Code Pro (SIL OFL)\nmigrations/                      D1 tables\ntest/                            Vitest tests and fakes\ntools/acuity-email-forwarder.gs  Google Apps Script that forwards Acuity&#39;s emails\nscripts/sync-apps.mjs            the build step: copies Index and Portal in\nscripts/sandbox-setup.mjs        sandbox setup\ndocs/media/                      README images (all sample data)</code></pre>","text":"public/novabot.js, novabot.css the chat widget (served by the Worker) public/app, portal, calendar, … Nova Agent's panels, copied in at build time (not in this repo) app.js, app.css the tabs, the smart calendar, alerts, voice, pings suite.js Nova Agent sheet, All links, What's changed options.js, themes.js/.css Options and the six themes ambient.js, sfx.js ambient music and sound effects sw.js notifications with the app closed memory/ Index (copied in at build time, not in git) public/portal/ Portal's pages (copied in at build time, not in git) src/index.js the Worker: chat, voice, routes, NovaBot's instructions src/app-page.js Portal's staff API (/app/api/*, from Portal's old address) src/portal-ask.js Ask Nova: questions about bookings, enquiries and alerts src/admin.js the admin pages src/links.js the master list: links, features, changelog src/memory/ the memory engine (store, extract, routes) src/portal/ Portal: sign-in, sessions, staff, planets src/booking.js session types, booking links, free times (public Acuity page) src/booking-form.js the booking card's API src/book-session.js booking checks (deposit first) src/manage-bookings.js staff finding, cancelling, moving and changing bookings src/agent-nova.js jobs, quests and alerts for Nova Agent src/enquiries.js enquiries, enquiry emails, chat log src/push.js notifications, the Alerts tab, real-booking checks src/booking-calendar.js booking details from Acuity's calendar feed src/booking-details.js booking details from Acuity's confirmation page src/booking-emails.js booking details from Acuity's emails src/booking-pings.js when booking notifications go out src/club-calendar.js busy times for Nova Club src/referrals.js referral tracking (Acuity API) src/feedback.js what visitors said about NovaBot src/health.js daily Acuity API check src/mode.js the booking-system switch src/nova/ Nova Bot's own booking system (Google, Gmail, Stripe) src/fonts/ Saira, Geist Mono and Source Code Pro (SIL OFL) migrations/ D1 tables test/ Vitest tests and fakes tools/acuity-email-forwarder.gs Google Apps Script that forwards Acuity's emails scripts/sync-apps.mjs the build step: copies Index and Portal in scripts/sandbox-setup.mjs sandbox setup docs/media/ README images (all sample data)"}],"news":[],"history":{"total":58,"first":"2026-10-06T15:46:34+01:00","commits":[{"hash":"42a8399","date":"2026-10-10T13:27:14+01:00","subject":"Portal everywhere: no more Portal (names, addresses, code, docs)","body":"The staff app is Portal in every word: notifications, the Ask feature (portal-ask.js), Index's\nmemory scope, the admin link, comments, tests and docs. Nova Agent's routes are /nova-agent/* only\n(the older addresses are gone; the PC has used the new ones since 2026-10-08). Migration 0019\nrenames stored text (remembered facts' source, facts, alert history) that still used the old\nname. The one-off link-fixing tool, already run, is removed."},{"hash":"ca5d1d9","date":"2026-10-09T16:41:51+01:00","subject":"/music-world/img: an exact Apple Music cover, served from here","body":""},{"hash":"29d0176","date":"2026-10-09T16:38:37+01:00","subject":"/music-world/file/<name>: one exact Commons photo, served from here","body":""},{"hash":"a2e835d","date":"2026-10-09T16:33:46+01:00","subject":"/music-world photos and art served from here (not redirects): nothing in the browser blocks them","body":""},{"hash":"d996840","date":"2026-10-09T04:27:42+01:00","subject":"/music-world: a fresh cache (forgets the early misses)","body":""},{"hash":"34b4431","date":"2026-10-09T04:25:38+01:00","subject":"/music-world: Apple's current chart address with a browser identity, Wikipedia's new picture host, album art lookup","body":""},{"hash":"416c43a","date":"2026-10-09T04:13:55+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent's front page music bits: /music-world (live Top 10 across 12 markets) and musicians' photos","body":""},{"hash":"4310d50","date":"2026-10-09T02:31:26+01:00","subject":"Sign-in details carry the planet's colours (for Nova Agent's planet colouring)","body":""},{"hash":"48897b9","date":"2026-10-08T23:34:26+01:00","subject":"Shared notes: /notes-api/ for the team's notes","body":"Migration 0018 (shared_notes), staff-only API with conflict-safe saves\n(a clash keeps both: the second becomes a conflicted copy), refused stale\ndeletes, change paging by rev, size and rate limits."},{"hash":"46482fa","date":"2026-10-08T17:45:50+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'main' into calendar-pro","body":""},{"hash":"0402fe8","date":"2026-10-08T17:45:50+01:00","subject":"WIP calendar-pro","body":""},{"hash":"738a7ee","date":"2026-10-08T17:44:17+01:00","subject":"Admin addresses open Portal's Admin section","body":""},{"hash":"8e0a8e3","date":"2026-10-08T16:59:59+01:00","subject":"Admin pages on phones: rows as cards, swipeable tabs","body":"Each table row becomes a small card with every value named after its column;\nname-value tables stack; the tabs are one row you swipe; number tiles in one\ncompact row; 16px fields; no blur."},{"hash":"e37085c","date":"2026-10-08T14:01:04+01:00","subject":"tools/add-admin.mjs: make an admin straight away (no invite)","body":"Asks for a name, an email and a hidden password, then adds them to the live\ndatabase as an active admin."},{"hash":"881c629","date":"2026-10-08T13:48:41+01:00","subject":"Any password the person likes (not empty, not over 200 characters)","body":"Guessing is still held back by the sign-in rate limit."},{"hash":"6dc17c0","date":"2026-10-08T13:44:08+01:00","subject":"Portal: POST /auth/password to choose a new password","body":"Admins needn't give the old one; staff confirm it. Other sign-ins end."},{"hash":"4b2ff2d","date":"2026-10-08T13:33:58+01:00","subject":"Portal is the one sign-in: no Sign in with Google","body":"Sign in with Google is gone (its routes, the PC hand-off, the per-person\nGoogle email links and its redirect address in Admin → Google). Google stays a\nconnection for Docs, Calendar and Gmail. /auth/google-status tells signed-in\nstaff whether Google is set up and as whom (Portal's You page, Notes)."},{"hash":"082d92b","date":"2026-10-08T13:28:18+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'google' into relay","body":""},{"hash":"7bb7999","date":"2026-10-08T13:27:09+01:00","subject":"The PC link: Nova Agent online, through the studio PC","body":"AgentLink (a Durable Object) holds the socket the studio PC opens to\n/nova-agent/link with AGENT_NOVA_KEY. Nova Agent's own addresses are passed\nto it for signed-in staff (the Visualizer's feeds for admins), streamed, with\npath tricks refused and changes only from this site; PC off answers 503\n{ pcOffline } straight away. Calendar's page online gets calendar-sync.js\n(copied in at build) so it uses Nova Agent's calendar."},{"hash":"ac5fd6e","date":"2026-10-08T13:26:26+01:00","subject":"Google, set up from inside Nova Agent; Sign in with Google","body":"- Admin → Google: a step-at-a-time setup (buttons to the right Google\n  Cloud pages, copy buttons for every address), then paste the key and\n  press Connect Google. The client ID is kept in settings, the secret and\n  the refresh token encrypted (AES-GCM, key from AGENT_NOVA_KEY via HKDF).\n  Cloudflare secrets, if set, still win. Every Google feature reads the\n  key through one place (nova/google-keys.js).\n- Connect Google runs in a small window and comes back (Google won't show\n  inside Nova Agent).\n- Sign in with Google (/auth/google/*): openid + email only, state and\n  PKCE; matches the verified Google email to a Portal account (or a Google\n  email an admin linked). The studio PC gets a two-minute, single-use code\n  bound to a verifier only it has, and swaps it for its own sign-in.\n- /auth/google/available tells the buttons (and Notes) when it's set up."},{"hash":"780350e","date":"2026-10-08T13:15:37+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'main' into relay","body":"# Conflicts:\n#\twrangler.jsonc"},{"hash":"84c681a","date":"2026-10-08T13:15:28+01:00","subject":"WIP: the PC link (from the earlier attempt)","body":""},{"hash":"364e6ca","date":"2026-10-08T12:33:36+01:00","subject":"Old Lossless preview site: redirect into Nova Agent too","body":""},{"hash":"019afe7","date":"2026-10-08T12:03:07+01:00","subject":"Privacy policy: the staff app is Nova Agent","body":""},{"hash":"f4ab37a","date":"2026-10-08T12:00:35+01:00","subject":"/agent/ is the only address","body":"Any page opened in a browser that isn't Nova Agent goes to /agent/ (a panel's\naddress, an old one or /agent/<panel> opens that panel). Files, the website\nchat's customer pages (/book, /referral, /privacy) and connecting Google stay.\nThe old Notes, Calendar and Lossless sites send people into Nova Agent, and\ntools/only-agent-links.mjs brings Admin → Links down to the one address."},{"hash":"bc5d96d","date":"2026-10-08T11:50:33+01:00","subject":"Links: drop Nova Agent's old main-address links now it's at /agent/","body":""},{"hash":"76f2409","date":"2026-10-08T11:48:07+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent at /agent/; the main address is Nova Bot's again","body":"A browser opening / goes on to /agent/; the website chat still POSTs to /.\n/agent/<panel> opens Nova Agent with that panel, and panels opened on their\nown go to /agent/?open=<panel>. The links list points at /agent/."},{"hash":"df52ab7","date":"2026-10-08T11:38:31+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent at the main address; the panels open only inside it","body":"- GET / is Nova Agent's page (web/agent/chat.html, copied to\n  public/index.html at build time, with its icons, manifest and /sw.js).\n  The website chat still POSTs to /; the sandbox keeps its demo page.\n- A panel's page opened on its own (Sec-Fetch-Dest: document) goes to\n  /?open=<its address>; inside Nova Agent's viewer (iframe) it loads as\n  itself. Not pages: Lossless audio's signalling, connecting Google (it\n  leaves Nova Agent: Google won't show inside a frame), files, the API.\n  run_worker_first sends / and the panels' pages through the Worker.\n- Portal, Index and the admin pages may be shown inside Nova Agent (same\n  site only: SAMEORIGIN, frame-ancestors 'self'); Nova Agent itself isn't\n  shown inside other pages. The admin pages fit the Admin panel.\n- tools/fix-links.mjs: for the studio team, just Nova Agent online and on\n  the studio computer (the panels are inside it); the d"},{"hash":"3104217","date":"2026-10-08T02:16:39+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'portal-merge' into sign-in","body":"# Conflicts:\n#\tsrc/index.js"},{"hash":"05655e2","date":"2026-10-08T02:16:32+01:00","subject":"Merge branch 'live-fixes' into sign-in","body":""},{"hash":"54bf9ce","date":"2026-10-08T02:15:38+01:00","subject":"One Portal: /app/ pages go to /portal/","body":"Nova Agent's Portal panel is now part of Portal (one staff app at /portal/).\n- The build copies Portal (web/portal) to public/portal/, and only what\n  phones that installed Portal still need (web/portal/old-app-address: the push\n  helper /app/sw.js, its manifest and icons) to public/app/. Index stays at\n  /app/memory/, the staff API at /app/api/.\n- Page visits to /app/... (and /studio/) redirect to /portal/, keeping the\n  query (/app/?view=alerts → /portal/?view=alerts); the API, Index and the\n  install files stay put. /portal/sw.js isn't cached.\n- Notifications link to /portal/ (and /portal/#nova for Nova Agent's); the\n  old push helper turns old /app/ links into Portal ones.\n- What staff read says Portal: NovaBot's staff prompts, booking notes,\n  the test notification, the voice hint, the admin pages' header and link,\n  and the privacy page. Guides and README too.\n- Tests: Portal's old pages re"},{"hash":"661fada","date":"2026-10-08T02:04:26+01:00","subject":"Lossless audio and Observatory online; the old Notes and Calendar sites move people over","body":"- Lossless audio at /lossless/: its page is copied in from Nova Agent with the\n  other panels, and its signalling (the LosslessRoom Durable Object, new\n  migration lossless-v1) and relay setup (/lossless/ice, STUN only until the\n  TURN key secrets are set) run here.\n- Observatory at /observatory/: the page is public, its projects and media\n  (data/, media/) only for signed-in staff. They're made on the studio PC, so\n  the build takes them from there when a worktree has none.\n- tools/old-sites: replacements for the nova-notes and nova-calendar Workers.\n  Both apps save in the browser, per site, so the old address checks what this\n  browser kept: nothing → straight to /notes/ or /calendar/ here; something →\n  download a backup, then restore it at the new address. Their offline helper\n  clears itself so installed copies stop showing the old version.\n- tools/fix-links.mjs: rewrites Admin → L"},{"hash":"70973f3","date":"2026-10-08T01:58:47+01:00","subject":"An app's sign-in keeps going while it's used","body":"Nova Agent's sign-in on the studio PC (an app token) gets another 30 days\neach time it's used, so it lasts until someone signs out."},{"hash":"9687c65","date":"2026-10-08T01:33:54+01:00","subject":"Guides: Portal is the one sign-in","body":"The admin pages, referrals and enquiries guides no longer mention the\nshared password; ADMIN_PASSWORD only sets up the first Portal admin."},{"hash":"2e375c1","date":"2026-10-08T00:57:27+01:00","subject":"Portal is the one sign-in","body":"- Portal's API takes a Portal sign-in only: the studio's shared password\n  (POST /app/api/login and its nvadmin cookie) is gone; /app/api/login\n  says to sign in with Portal, and signing out signs out of Portal and\n  clears any old shared-password cookie.\n- The admin pages are for Portal admins: signed out, they send you to\n  Portal and back (no more browser password prompt); a signed-in staff\n  member who isn't an admin is told so.\n- Portal's \"connect\" for other sites (/auth/connect, read-only profile\n  tokens and their cross-site access) is gone: every panel shares Portal's\n  own sign-in now. ADMIN_PASSWORD only proves the very first admin.\n- Tests sign in the one way there is: a Portal account and session\n  (test/sign-in.js), instead of the shared password."},{"hash":"226cc0d","date":"2026-10-08T00:45:27+01:00","subject":"Plain names, and the panels back at their own addresses","body":"- Portal is served at /app/ again (its push helper /app/sw.js is a plain file\n  again), Index at /app/memory/ and Portal at /portal/; pushes and alerts\n  link to /app/. /studio/, /crew/ and /index/ (yesterday's addresses)\n  redirect back.\n- \"Studio\" is Portal and \"Crew\" is Portal again (only where the earlier rename\n  changed them); src/studio-ask.js is src/portal-ask.js again.\n- Nova Agent's features drop \"Nova\": Portal, Portal, Calendar, Notes, Index,\n  Quests, Missions and so on. Nova Agent, Nova Bot and Nova Club keep it."},{"hash":"a697369","date":"2026-10-07T23:40:50+01:00","subject":"Studio's GIFs move to Nova Agent with its guide","body":""},{"hash":"6fe1da2","date":"2026-10-07T23:38:00+01:00","subject":"Portal and Nova Portal leave Nova Bot: Nova Agent's panels are served instead","body":"- public/app (Portal) is gone. The build step copies Nova Agent's panels\n  in from its repo (web/studio, crew, index, calendar, notes, shared) and\n  this Worker serves them at /studio/, /crew/, /index/, /calendar/ and\n  /notes/, with their security headers.\n- Old addresses keep working: /app/... goes to /studio/..., /app/memory/...\n  to /index/..., /portal/... to /crew/..., and /app/sw.js is still the push\n  helper (Studio's), so phones that installed Portal keep getting\n  notifications. Pushes and alerts now link to /studio/.\n- Nova Agent's machine routes have their own address, /nova-agent/*; the\n  old /portal/* still answers.\n- Renamed throughout: Portal → Studio, Nova Portal → Crew, the suite →\n  Nova Agent. src/portal-ask.js is src/studio-ask.js. Studio's guide and\n  pictures move to Nova Agent's docs/apps/studio.\n- Tests for the old addresses, the push helper and the new route."},{"hash":"3b5ae08","date":"2026-10-07T21:46:23+01:00","subject":"Portal quest taps: none lost, none handed over twice","body":"Taps were kept as a JSON list in settings, added and taken with a read and\nthen a write. Taps made at the same moment overwrote each other (1 of 10\nkept in the new test), and Nova Agent's two collectors (the job check and\nthe plan upload) could both be handed the same tap: a \"Session done\" then\ncounted twice and skipped the next session without a ping (P0-1).\n- Taps are appended in one statement, and taken and cleared in one\n  (DELETE ... RETURNING).\n- Each tap gets a tapId, so Nova Agent counts it once.\n- Portal sends the session a \"Session done\" was tapped on, and the\n  worker passes it on, so a late or repeated tap can't count against the\n  next session."},{"hash":"0d953c7","date":"2026-10-07T16:30:08+01:00","subject":"The Nova Manual in Portal and the admin pages","body":"A book button beside the Portal badge opens the Nova Manual: every Nova\napp's guide, how it's built, its history and what's new, with search.\nIt comes from Nova Portal (copied in by the build step, /portal/manual.js);\non the sign-in screen it floats in the corner."},{"hash":"fe6d945","date":"2026-10-07T02:01:03+01:00","subject":"Nova Agent finds who it works for: the studio's first admin","body":"/portal/agent/me without a staff_id picks the first active admin, and the\nNova Index files Nova Agent kept as \"owner\" become theirs."},{"hash":"a59a975","date":"2026-10-07T01:50:03+01:00","subject":"Nova Portal badge on Portal and the admin pages; connect tokens","body":"- /auth/me adds the planet's name, description and glow colour\n- POST /auth/connect: a read-only profile token for another suite site,\n  with CORS on /auth/me and /auth/logout for those sites only\n- /portal/agent/me: who Nova Agent works for, for its badge"},{"hash":"aa08441","date":"2026-10-07T01:35:25+01:00","subject":"Nova Portal: the code (the previous commit only carried the script rename)","body":"- /auth and /staff: email + password sign-in (PBKDF2, hashed session\n  tokens, httpOnly cookie or app token), first-admin setup with the studio\n  password, invite links, roles, switching accounts off\n- Portal, the admin pages and Nova Index all accept a Portal session;\n  staff who aren't admins see only the studio's memory and their own\n- /staff/:id/planet.svg: each person's generated planet badge\n- sync-apps.mjs copies in Nova Index, the Portal and the planet generator\n- Portal's desktop calendar keeps the week strip and the picked day's\n  smart panel in place"},{"hash":"54d2f55","date":"2026-10-07T01:35:09+01:00","subject":"Nova Portal: one sign-in for the Nova suite","body":"- /auth and /staff: email + password sign-in (PBKDF2, hashed session\n  tokens, httpOnly cookie or app token), first-admin setup with the studio\n  password, invite links, roles, switching accounts off\n- Portal, the admin pages and Nova Index all accept a Portal session;\n  staff who aren't admins see only the studio's memory and their own\n- /staff/:id/planet.svg: each person's generated planet badge\n- sync-apps.mjs copies in Nova Index, the Portal and the planet generator\n- Portal's desktop calendar keeps the week strip and the picked day's\n  smart panel in place"},{"hash":"8cc628f","date":"2026-10-07T01:30:21+01:00","subject":"README: a fresh look at NovaBot, Portal, the admin pages, Nova Index and Nova Portal","body":"New screenshots and GIF walkthroughs, all made with made-up data and mocked\nAPIs: Portal's sign-in, enquiries, the smart calendar (week, clash, tight\nchangeover, free slots), quests and missions, alerts with real-booking checks,\nthe suite sheet with links and the changelog, Options, the six themes, the\ndesktop side rail and NovaBot in staff mode; plus Nova Index, Nova Portal and\nthe admin Links page. The README now covers the memory engine, Nova Portal's\nsign-in, the build step, configuration and tests."},{"hash":"5569aed","date":"2026-10-07T00:23:49+01:00","subject":"Nova Index's memory engine: one shared memory for the Nova suite","body":"- src/memory/: small files of one-line facts in studio, staff and customer\n  scopes (D1, never git), written with version tokens; the server decides\n  who sees what (Nova Agent: studio + staff; the website: that customer and\n  the public studio facts; Portal/Index: everything)\n- Learning in the background: a small model distils durable facts, each file\n  is rewritten with them merged in (and condensed past 3 KB); customers'\n  facts wait for approval; card, bank and ID numbers are never kept\n- Reading: the studio file, the person's profile and up to 3 matching files,\n  within ~800 tokens, for NovaBot, Ask Nova and Nova Agent\n- /memory/* for Nova Agent (its key) and /app/api/memory/* for Nova Index;\n  quiet website chats are read by the every-minute job\n- Nova Index (ns/ni) is copied into /app/memory/ at build time; a tile in\n  Portal's suite sheet; the privacy notice explains memory"},{"hash":"cecf7e3","date":"2026-10-06T23:32:45+01:00","subject":"Portal: a smart calendar, and it always talks to you as staff","body":"- Smart calendar: the week at a glance (sessions, hours, session value,\n  busiest day, next free hour, clashes), days shaded by how full they are, and\n  each day's fullness, clashes, tight changeovers, free slots (one tap to a\n  booking link), filters and Ask Nova\n- NovaBot inside Portal is told it's talking to staff, never a customer;\n  its tab is 'NovaBot · bookings'; Ask Nova speaks as a colleague"},{"hash":"6ac8b85","date":"2026-10-06T23:10:44+01:00","subject":"Portal: sound effects, a plain-English changelog, a chime for NovaBot's answers","body":"- sfx.js: soft cosmic sounds on every tap, tab, switch, open, close, send,\n  done and delete (shared by every Nova app); a switch in Options\n- 'What's changed' in the master list: every change with what, why and the\n  benefit, grouped by day and app, on the Links page and in Portal"},{"hash":"3c53388","date":"2026-10-06T22:57:13+01:00","subject":"Portal suite sheet: every app opens somewhere that works","body":"Nova Agent and Nova Observatory open on the studio computer (Observatory is\nnow served by Nova Agent, always on); Nova Calendar offers the web app and\nNova Agent's copy, with what each is; Admin is listed. Tiles stack so the\nwords are never squeezed."},{"hash":"442136d","date":"2026-10-06T22:49:11+01:00","subject":"Portal: Nova Quests and Missions stand out; every feature in the master list","body":"Every quest card says Nova Quest (and its mission), missions wear a gold Nova\nMission badge, with entrance, shine, sweep and progress-ring animations. The\nmaster list gains 'Everything the Nova suite can do', app by app, on the\nadmin Links page and in Portal's suite sheet."},{"hash":"61b229d","date":"2026-10-06T21:47:06+01:00","subject":"Portal Options, and everything centred","body":"An Options sheet (gear in the header): theme, text alignment (centred by\ndefault) and size, how alert times show, animations, the starfield, pings,\nambient music volume, the starting tab, plus Refresh, Sign out and Reset.\nSaved on the device and applied before the page draws. The brand sits in\nthe middle of the header, and cards, alerts, quests and the admin pages are\ncentred unless Options says left."},{"hash":"facdcd0","date":"2026-10-06T21:41:15+01:00","subject":"Portal overhaul: Nova suite look, six themes, suite sheet and links","body":"- A cosmic H icon, glass panels, Archivo headings, a floating one-row tab bar\n  (a side rail on desktop), sheets that become dialogs on larger screens\n- Six themes (cosmic, ember, aurora, ocean, gold, mono) from themes.css and\n  themes.js, shared with the admin pages so a theme carries across\n- The Nova suite sheet: the apps, the locked list of every address (checked\n  live), and the theme picker\n- The admin pages in the same look; alert times on one line; the links check\n  no longer flags planned addresses or ones that need details"},{"hash":"9c93bfc","date":"2026-10-06T21:32:35+01:00","subject":"Links page, booking checks with Acuity, alert labels and times, notification fix","body":"- /admin/links (and Portal's API): every Nova suite address from the\n  database, checked live each time; editable on the page\n- Booking alerts are checked with Acuity: real, cancelled or not found, with\n  when it was booked and what's been paid; every alert gets a label and its\n  exact time\n- Notifications show on iPhones with the app closed (plain form), and a new\n  service worker takes over at once\n- Nova Calendar cards and quests in Portal's Calendar tab"},{"hash":"9a9356b","date":"2026-10-06T21:11:23+01:00","subject":"Portal: Nova Quests tab, ambient music and Nova suite touches","body":"A Quests tab shows Nova Agent's plan (today, pulses, missions with progress,\nall quests) with buttons that go back to Nova Agent. A music button plays\ngenerative electronic ambient made on the phone. A drifting starfield and the\nNova suite name join the header."},{"hash":"9997e2d","date":"2026-10-06T20:59:29+01:00","subject":"Portal: quick repeats ring without filling the Alerts list","body":"Alerts sent with keep: false still reach the phones but aren't saved, and a\nnewer banner about the same thing replaces the old one."},{"hash":"44a352c","date":"2026-10-06T20:44:45+01:00","subject":"Portal: labelled Nova Agent, Quest and Mission alerts with pings and buzz","body":"Alerts from Nova Agent carry their source, kind and urgency: each gets its own\nlabel, buzz pattern and tag, check-ins stay on screen, the Home Screen icon gets\na dot, and an open Portal pings and drops a banner."},{"hash":"38520f3","date":"2026-10-06T18:23:31+01:00","subject":"Nova Task is now Nova Calendar","body":"Update the name and links to the renamed repo\n(https://github.com/tuniveza/nova-calendar)."},{"hash":"1734edc","date":"2026-10-06T15:46:34+01:00","subject":"Nova Bot: chat assistant, booking card and Portal for Novacane Studios","body":""}],"work":[],"workCount":0,"workStat":""}}]};
